helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158446				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>MUNIT function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158446	12			0	uk	MUNIT				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154121	13			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EINHEITSMATRIX\"\>Returns the unitary square array of a certain size.\</ahelp\> The unitary array is a square array where the main diagonal elements equal 1 and all other array elements are equal to 0.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155123	14			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3156271	15			0	uk	MUNIT(Dimensions)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3159390	16			0	uk	\<emph\>Dimensions\</emph\> refers to the size of the array unit.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C9B				0	uk	You can find a general introduction to Array functions at the top of this page.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156162	17			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150949	18			0	uk	Select a square range within the spreadsheet, for example, from A1 to E5.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3151260	19			0	uk	Without deselecting the range, select the MUNIT function. Mark the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> check box. Enter the desired dimensions for the array unit, in this case \<item type=\"input\"\>5\</item\>, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150403	20			0	uk	You can also enter the \<item type=\"input\"\>=Munit(5)\</item\> formula in the last cell of the selected range (E5), and press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Shift+Command+Enter\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Shift+Ctrl+Enter\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3156143	21			0	uk	You now see a unit array with a range of A1:E5.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN10FA7				0	uk	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159084				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>FREQUENCY function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159084	22			0	uk	FREQUENCY				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3145777	23			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HAEUFIGKEIT\"\>Indicates the frequency distribution in a one-column-array.\</ahelp\> The function counts the number of values in the Data array that are within the values given by the Classes array.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153347	24			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
