helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"szenariotext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ScenarioManager\"\>Defines a scenario for the selected sheet area.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	uk	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/scenario.xhp#scenario\"/\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280	3			0	uk	Name of scenario				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041	13			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SCENWIN_TOP\"\>Defines the name for the scenario. Use a clear and unique name so you can easily identify the scenario.\</ahelp\> You can also modify a scenario name in the Navigator through the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>context menu command.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153954	14			0	uk	Comment				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	15			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SCENWIN_BOTTOM\"\>Specifies additional information about the scenario. This information will be displayed in the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> when you click the \<emph\>Scenarios\</emph\> icon and select the desired scenario.\</ahelp\> You can also modify this information in the Navigator through the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>context menu command.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145273	16			0	uk	Settings				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364	17			0	uk	This section is used to define some of the settings used in the scenario display.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367	18			0	uk	Display border				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	19			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:LB_COLOR\"\>Highlights the scenario in your table with a border. The color for the border is specified in the field to the right of this option.\</ahelp\> The border will have a title bar displaying the name of the last scenario. The button on the right of the scenario border offers you an overview of all the scenarios in this area, if several have been defined. You can choose any of the scenarios from this list without restrictions.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149582	20			0	uk	Copy back				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942	21			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_TWOWAY\"\>Copies the values of cells that you change into the active scenario. If you do not select this option, the scenario is not changed when you change cell values. The behavior of the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> setting depends on the cell protection, the sheet protection, and the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> settings.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149402	22			0	uk	Copy entire sheet				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	23			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_COPYALL\"\>Copies the entire sheet into an additional scenario sheet. \</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075A				0	uk	Prevent changes				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075E				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:CheckBox:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_PROTECT\"\>Prevents changes to the active scenario. The behavior of the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> setting depends on the cell protection, the sheet protection, and the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> settings.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	uk	You can only change the scenario properties if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is not selected and if the sheet is not protected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10780				0	uk	You can only edit cell values if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is selected, if the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> is option is not selected, and if the cells are not protected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	uk	You can only change scenario cell values and write them back into the scenario if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is not selected, if the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> option is selected, and if the cells are not protected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Right				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02140200.xhp\" name=\"Right\"\>Right\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillRight\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Fills a selected range of at least two columns with the contents of the left most cell.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684	3			0	uk	If a range of only one row is selected, the contents of the far left cell are copied to all the other selected cells. If you have selected several rows, each of the far left cells is copied into those cells to the right.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Detective				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151245				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>cell links search\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching; links in cells\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>traces;precedents and dependents\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Formula Auditing,see Detective\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Detective\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151245	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030000.xhp\" name=\"Detective\"\>Detective\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211	2			0	uk	This command activates the Spreadsheet Detective. With the Detective, you can trace the dependencies from the current formula cell to the cells in the spreadsheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447	3			0	uk	Once you have defined a trace, you can point with the mouse cursor to the trace. The mouse cursor will change its shape. Double-click the trace with this cursor to select the referenced cell at the end of the trace. 				20220827 09:49:47
