helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149566				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>ISLEAPYEAR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>leap year determination\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149566	14			0	uk	ISLEAPYEAR				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150297	15			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Determines whether a year is a leap year.\</ahelp\> If yes, the function will return the value 1 (TRUE); if not, it will return 0 (FALSE).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148487	16			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205	17			0	uk	ISLEAPYEAR("Date")				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3159239	18			0	uk	\<emph\>Date\</emph\> specifies whether a given date falls within a leap year. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149817	19			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786	20			0	uk	=ISLEAPYEAR(A1) returns 1, if A1 contains 1968-02-29, the valid date 29th of February 1968 in your locale setting.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E7				0	uk	You may also use =ISLEAPYEAR("1968-02-29") or =ISLEAPYEAR("2/29/68").				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EA				0	uk	Never use =ISLEAPYEAR(2/29/68), because this would first evaluate 2 divided by 29 divided by 68, and then calculate the ISLEAPYEAR function from this small number as a serial date number.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154656				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>YEARS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of years between two dates\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
