helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811	49			0	uk	=DAYSINYEAR(A1) returns 366 days if A1 contains 1968-02-29, a valid date for the year 1968.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154737				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>DAYSINMONTH function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of days;in a specific month of a year\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154737	50			0	uk	DAYSINMONTH				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3149316	51			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_DAYSINMONTH\"\>Calculates the number of days of the month in which the date entered occurs.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145114	52			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150955	53			0	uk	DAYSINMONTH(Date)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147501	54			0	uk	\<emph\>Date\</emph\> is any date in the respective month of the desired year. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149871	55			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3155742	56			0	uk	=DAYSINMONTH(A1) returns 29 days if A1 contains 1968-02-17, a valid date for February 1968.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149048				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of weeks;between two dates\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
