helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154636	223			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VDB\"\>Returns the depreciation of an asset for a specified or partial period using a variable declining balance method.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155519	224			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149025	225			0	uk	VDB(Cost; Salvage; Life; S; End; Factor; Type)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150692	226			0	uk	\<emph\>Cost\</emph\> is the initial value of an asset.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155369	227			0	uk	\<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> is the value of an asset at the end of the depreciation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154954	228			0	uk	\<emph\>Life\</emph\> is the depreciation duration of the asset.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152817	229			0	uk	\<emph\>S\</emph\> is the start of the depreciation. A must be entered in the same date unit as the duration.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153221	230			0	uk	\<emph\>End\</emph\> is the end of the depreciation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147536	231			0	uk	\<emph\>Factor\</emph\> (optional) is the depreciation factor. Factor = 2 is double rate depreciation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154865	232			0	uk	\<emph\>Type \</emph\>is an optional parameter. Type = 1 means a switch to linear depreciation. In Type = 0 no switch is made.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0D				0	uk	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148429	233			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153927	234			0	uk	What is the declining-balance double-rate depreciation for a period if the initial cost is 35,000 currency units and the value at the end of the depreciation is 7,500 currency units. The depreciation period is 3 years. The depreciation from the 10th to the 20th period is calculated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155991	235			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=VDB(35000;7500;36;10;20;2)\</item\> = 8603.80 currency units. The depreciation during the period between the 10th and the 20th period is 8,603.80 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147485				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;internal rates of return, irregular payments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>internal rates of return;irregular payments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XIRR function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147485	193			0	uk	XIRR				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145614	194			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_XIRR\"\>Calculates the internal rate of return for a list of payments which take place on different dates.\</ahelp\> The calculation is based on a 365 days per year basis, ignoring leap years.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E62				0	uk	If the payments take place at regular intervals, use the IRR function.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146149	195			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149826	196			0	uk	XIRR(Values; Dates; Guess)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3163821	197			0	uk	\<emph\>Values\</emph\> and \<emph\>Dates\</emph\> refer to a series of payments and the series of associated date values. The first pair of dates defines the start of the payment plan. All other date values must be later, but need not be in any order. The series of values must contain at least one negative and one positive value (receipts and deposits).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149708	198			0	uk	\<emph\>Guess\</emph\> (optional) is a guess that can be input for the internal rate of return. The default is 10%.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145085	199			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149273	200			0	uk	Calculation of the internal rate of return for the following five payments:				20220827 09:49:47
