helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148690				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>CHIDIST function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148690	106			0	uk	CHIDIST				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156338	156			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CHIVERT\"\>Returns the probability value from the indicated Chi square that a hypothesis is confirmed.\</ahelp\> CHIDIST compares the Chi square value to be given for a random sample that is calculated from the sum of (observed value-expected value)^2/expected value for all values with the theoretical Chi square distribution and determines from this the probability of error for the hypothesis to be tested.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151316	157			0	uk	The probability determined by CHIDIST can also be determined by CHITEST.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155123	108			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158439	109			0	uk	CHIDIST(Number; DegreesFreedom)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148675	110			0	uk	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the chi-square value of the random sample used to determine the error probability.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155615	111			0	uk	            \<emph\>DegreesFreedom\</emph\> are the degrees of freedom of the experiment.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146787	112			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145774	113			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIDIST(13.27; 5)\</item\> equals 0.02.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156141	158			0	uk	If the Chi square value of the random sample is 13.27 and if the experiment has 5 degrees of freedom, then the hypothesis is assured with a probability of error of 2%.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id0119200902231887				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>CHISQDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chi-square distribution\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200901583452				0	uk	CHISQDIST				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200901583471				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Returns the value of the probability density function or the cumulative distribution function for the chi-square distribution.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200902395520				0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395679				0	uk	CHISQDIST(Number; Degrees Of Freedom; Cumulative)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id011920090239564				0	uk	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number for which the function is to be calculated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395660				0	uk	            \<emph\>Degrees Of Freedom\</emph\> is the degrees of freedom for the chi-square function.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395623				0	uk	            \<emph\>Cumulative\</emph\> (optional): 0 or False calculates the probability density function. Other values or True or omitted calculates the cumulative distribution function.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150603				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>EXPONDIST function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>exponential distributions\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150603	115			0	uk	EXPONDIST				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149563	116			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EXPONVERT\"\>Returns the exponential distribution.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153789	117			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150987	118			0	uk	EXPONDIST(Number; Lambda; C)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154663	119			0	uk	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value of the function.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154569	120			0	uk	            \<emph\>Lambda\</emph\> is the parameter value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147332	121			0	uk	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> is a logical value that determines the form of the function. \<emph\>C = 0\</emph\> calculates the density function, and \<emph\>C = 1\</emph\> calculates the distribution.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146133	122			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150357	123			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=EXPONDIST(3;0.5;1)\</item\> returns 0.78.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Protecting document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150541	1			0	uk	Protecting document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145172	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"dokumenttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToolProtectionDocument\"\>Protects the sheet structure of your document from modifications. It is impossible to insert, delete, rename, move or copy sheets.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Open the \<emph\>Protect document\</emph\> dialog with \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\>. Optionally enter a password and click OK.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188	6			0	uk	The structure of protected spreadsheet documents can be changed only if the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> option is disabled. On the context menus for the spreadsheet tabs at the lower graphic border, only the menu item \<emph\>Select All Sheets\</emph\> can be activated. All other menu items are deactivated. To remove the protection, call up the command \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\> again. If no password is assigned, protection is immediately removed. If you were assigned a password, the \<emph\>Remove Spreadsheet Protection\</emph\> dialog appears, in which you must enter the password. Only then can you remove the check mark specifying that protection is active.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	7			0	uk	A protected document, once saved, can only be saved again with the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> menu command. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596	4			0	uk	Password (optional)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155412	5			0	uk	You can create a password to protect your document against unauthorized or accidental modifications.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	9			0	uk	You can completely protect your work by combining both options from \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, including password entry. If you want to prevent the document from being opened by other users, select \<emph\>Save With Password \</emph\>and click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button. The \<emph\>Enter Password\</emph\> dialog appears. Consider carefully when choosing a password; if you forget it after you close a document you will be unable to access the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Grouping				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN1054D				0	uk	Grouping				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10551				0	uk	Grouping pivot tables displays the \<emph\>Grouping\</emph\> dialog for either values or dates.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10568				0	uk	Start				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056C				0	uk	Specifies the start of the grouping.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056F				0	uk	Automatically				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10573				0	uk	Specifies whether to start grouping at the smallest value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10576				0	uk	Manually at				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057A				0	uk	Specifies whether to enter the start value for grouping yourself.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057D				0	uk	End				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10581				0	uk	Specifies the end of the grouping.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10584				0	uk	Automatically				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10588				0	uk	Specifies whether to end grouping at the largest value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058B				0	uk	Manually at				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058F				0	uk	Specifies whether to enter the end value for grouping yourself.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10592				0	uk	Group by				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10596				0	uk	Specifies the value range by which every group's limits are calculated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10599				0	uk	Number of days				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059D				0	uk	In the case of grouping date values, specifies the number of days to group by.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A0				0	uk	Intervals				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A4				0	uk	In the case of grouping date values, specifies the intervals to group by.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105B2				0	uk	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_grouping.xhp#datapilot_grouping\"/\>				20220827 09:49:47
