helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149000	64			0	uk	 This function returns the inverse hyperbolic cosine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic cosine is Number. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6393932				0	uk	 Number must be greater than or equal to 1.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150566	65			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145629	66			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOSH(1)\</item\> returns 0.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id951567				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOSH(COSH(4))\</item\> returns 4.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149027				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>ACOT function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
