helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155818	71			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCCOT\"\>Returns the inverse cotangent (the arccotangent) of the given number.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153225	72			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158419	73			0	uk	ACOT(Number)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154948	74			0	uk	 This function returns the inverse trigonometric cotangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose cotangent is Number. The angle returned is between 0 and PI.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5834528				0	uk	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				20220827 09:49:47
