helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155802				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>COMBIN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155802	273			0	uk	COMBIN				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156172	274			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN\"\>Returns the number of combinations for elements without repetition.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193	275			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	276			0	uk	COMBIN(Count1; Count2)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150313	277			0	uk	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153830	278			0	uk	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6807458				0	uk	COMBIN returns the number of ordered ways to choose these items. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 3 different ways, namely AB, AC and BC.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7414471				0	uk	COMBIN implements the formula: Count1!/(Count2!*(Count1-Count2)!)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153171	279			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153517	280			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COMBIN(3;2)\</item\> returns 3.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150284				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>COMBINA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations with repetitions\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150284	282			0	uk	COMBINA				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157894	283			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN2\"\>Returns the number of combinations of a subset of items including repetitions.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145752	284			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145765	285			0	uk	COMBINA(Count1; Count2)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153372	286			0	uk	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155544	287			0	uk	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1997131				0	uk	COMBINA returns the number of unique ways to choose these items, where the order of choosing is irrelevant, and repetition of items is allowed. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 6 different ways, namely AA, AB, AC, BB, BC and CC.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2052064				0	uk	COMBINA implements the formula: (Count1+Count2-1)! / (Count2!(Count1-1)!)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154584	288			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152904	289			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COMBINA(3;2)\</item\> returns 6.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156086				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>TRUNC function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places;cutting off\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156086	291			0	uk	TRUNC				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157866	292			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUERZEN\"\>Truncates a number by removing decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148499	293			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148511	294			0	uk	TRUNC(Number; Count)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150796	295			0	uk	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> with at most \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. Excess decimal places are simply removed, irrespective of sign.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150816	296			0	uk	\<item type=\"literal\"\>TRUNC(Number; 0)\</item\> behaves as \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(Number)\</item\> for positive numbers, but effectively rounds towards zero for negative numbers.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148548	557			0	uk	The \<emph\>visible\</emph\> decimal places of the result are specified in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152555	297			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152569	298			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(1.239;2)\</item\> returns 1.23. The 9 is lost.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7050080				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(-1.234999;3)\</item\> returns -1.234. All the 9s are lost.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153601				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>LN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>natural logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153601	301			0	uk	LN				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154974	302			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LN\"\>Returns the natural logarithm based on the constant e of a number.\</ahelp\> The constant e has a value of approximately 2.71828182845904.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154993	303			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155284	304			0	uk	LN(Number)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155297	305			0	uk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose natural logarithm is to be calculated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153852	306			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153866	307			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LN(3)\</item\> returns the natural logarithm of 3 (approximately 1.0986).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5747245				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LN(EXP(321))\</item\> returns 321.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109813				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>LOG function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>logarithms\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109813	311			0	uk	LOG				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3109841	312			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG\"\>Returns the logarithm of a number to the specified base.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144719	313			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144732	314			0	uk	LOG(Number; Base)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144746	315			0	uk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose logarithm is to be calculated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152840	316			0	uk	\<emph\>Base\</emph\> (optional) is the base for the logarithm calculation. If omitted, Base 10 is assumed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152860	317			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154429	318			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG(10;3)\</item\> returns the logarithm to base 3 of 10 (approximately 2.0959).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5577562				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG(7^4;7)\</item\> returns 4.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154187				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>LOG10 function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>base-10 logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154187	322			0	uk	LOG10				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155476	323			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG10\"\>Returns the base-10 logarithm of a number.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155494	324			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159294	325			0	uk	LOG10(Number)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159308	326			0	uk	Returns the logarithm to base 10 of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159328	327			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157916	328			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG10(5)\</item\> returns the base-10 logarithm of 5 (approximately 0.69897).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152518				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>CEILING function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding;up to multiples of significance\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152518	332			0	uk	CEILING				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153422	558			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_OBERGRENZE\"\>Rounds a number up to the nearest multiple of Significance.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153440	334			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153454	335			0	uk	CEILING(Number; Significance; Mode)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153467	336			0	uk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded up.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155000	337			0	uk	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the number to whose multiple the value is to be rounded up.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155020	559			0	uk	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the Mode value is given and not equal to zero, and if Number and Significance are negative, then rounding is done based on the absolute value of Number. This parameter is ignored when exporting to MS Excel as Excel does not know any third parameter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163792	629			0	uk	If both parameters Number and Significance are negative and the Mode value is equal to zero or is not given, the results in $[officename] and Excel will differ after the import has been completed. If you export the spreadsheet to Excel, use Mode=1 to see the same results in Excel as in Calc.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145697	338			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145710	339			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2)\</item\> returns -10				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145725	340			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2;0)\</item\> returns -10				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145740	341			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2;1)\</item\> returns -12				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157762				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>PI function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157762	343			0	uk	PI				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157790	344			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PI\"\>Returns 3.14159265358979, the value of the mathematical constant PI to 14 decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157809	345			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157822	346			0	uk	PI()				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157836	347			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152370	348			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PI()\</item\> returns 3.14159265358979.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152418				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>MULTINOMIAL function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152418	635			0	uk	MULTINOMIAL				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152454	636			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_MULTINOMIAL\"\> Returns the factorial of the sum of the arguments divided by the product of the factorials of the arguments.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155646	637			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155660	638			0	uk	MULTINOMIAL(Number(s))				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155673	639			0	uk	\<emph\>Number(s)\</emph\> is a list of up to 30 numbers.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155687	640			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155701	641			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MULTINOMIAL(F11:H11)\</item\> returns 1260, if F11 to H11 contain the values \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>, \<item type=\"input\"\>3\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\>. This corresponds to the formula =(2+3+4)! / (2!*3!*4!)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155717				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>POWER function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155717	350			0	uk	POWER				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159495	351			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_POTENZ\"\>Returns a number raised to another number.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159513	352			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159526	353			0	uk	POWER(Base; Exponent)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159540	354			0	uk	Returns \<emph\>Base\</emph\> raised to the power of \<emph\>Exponent\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	uk	The same result may be achieved by using the exponentiation operator ^:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9759514				0	uk	\<item type=\"literal\"\>Base^Exponent\</item\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159580	356			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159594	357			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=POWER(4;3)\</item\> returns 64, which is 4 to the power of 3.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1614429				0	uk	=4^3 also returns 4 to the power of 3.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152651				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>SERIESSUM function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152651	642			0	uk	SERIESSUM				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152688	643			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sums the first terms of a power series.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152708	644			0	uk	SERIESSUM(x;n;m;coefficients) = coefficient_1*x^n + coefficient_2*x^(n+m) + coefficient_3*x^(n+2m) +...+ coefficient_i*x^(n+(i-1)m)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152724	645			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_idN11BD9				0	uk	SERIESSUM(X; N; M; Coefficients)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152737	646			0	uk	\<emph\>X\</emph\> is the input value for the power series.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144344	647			0	uk	\<emph\>N\</emph\> is the initial power				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144357	648			0	uk	\<emph\>M\</emph\> is the increment to increase N				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144370	649			0	uk	\<emph\>Coefficients\</emph\> is a series of coefficients. For each coefficient the series sum is extended by one section.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144386				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>PRODUCT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers;multiplying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiplying;numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144386	361			0	uk	PRODUCT				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144414	362			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PRODUKT\"\>Multiplies all the numbers given as arguments and returns the product.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144433	363			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144446	364			0	uk	PRODUCT(Number1; Number2; ...; Number30)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144460	365			0	uk	\<emph\>Number1 to 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments whose product is to be calculated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1589098				0	uk	PRODUCT returns number1 * number2 * number3 * ...				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144480	366			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144494	367			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PRODUCT(2;3;4)\</item\> returns 24.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3160340				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>SUMSQ function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square number additions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sums;of square numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160340	369			0	uk	SUMSQ				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160368	370			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUADRATESUMME\"\>If you want to calculate the sum of the squares of numbers (totaling up of the squares of the arguments), enter these into the text fields.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160388	371			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160402	372			0	uk	SUMSQ(Number1; Number2; ...; Number30)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160415	373			0	uk	\<emph\>Number1 to 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments the sum of whose squares is to be calculated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160436	374			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160449	375			0	uk	If you enter the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>; \<item type=\"input\"\>3\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\> in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 29 is returned as the result.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158247				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>MOD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remainders of divisions\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158247	387			0	uk	MOD				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158276	388			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_REST\"\>Returns the remainder when one integer is divided by another.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158294	389			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158308	390			0	uk	MOD(Dividend; Divisor)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158321	391			0	uk	 For integer arguments this function returns Dividend modulo Divisor, that is the remainder when \<emph\>Dividend\</emph\> is divided by \<emph\>Divisor\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158341	392			0	uk	This function is implemented as \<item type=\"literal\"\>Dividend - Divisor * INT(Dividend/Divisor)\</item\> , and this formula gives the result if the arguments are not integer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158361	393			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158374	394			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MOD(22;3)\</item\> returns 1, the remainder when 22 is divided by 3.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1278420				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MOD(11.25;2.5)\</item\> returns 1.25.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144592				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>QUOTIENT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>divisions\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144592	652			0	uk	QUOTIENT				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144627	653			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_QUOTIENT\"\>Returns the integer part of a division operation.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144646	654			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144659	655			0	uk	QUOTIENT(Numerator; Denominator)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	uk	Returns the integer part of \<emph\>Numerator\</emph\> divided by \<emph\>Denominator\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7985168				0	uk	QUOTIENT is equivalent to \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(numerator/denominator)\</item\>, except that it may report errors with different error codes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144674	656			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144687	657			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=QUOTIENT(11;3)\</item\> returns 3. The remainder of 2 is lost.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144702				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>RADIANS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;degrees, into radians\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
