helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158055	380			0	uk	RADIANS(Number)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158069	381			0	uk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the angle in degrees to be converted to radians.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id876186				0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RADIANS(90)\</item\> returns 1.5707963267949, which is PI/2 to Calc's accuracy.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158121				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>ROUND function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158121	398			0	uk	ROUND				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158150	399			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number to a certain number of decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158169	400			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158182	401			0	uk	ROUND(Number; Count)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158196	402			0	uk	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds to the nearest integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds to the nearest 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id599688				0	uk	This function rounds to the nearest number. See ROUNDDOWN and ROUNDUP for alternatives.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145863	404			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145876	405			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.348;2)\</item\> returns 2.35				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145899	406			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(-32.4834;3)\</item\> returns -32.483. Change the cell format to see all decimals.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1371501				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.348;0)\</item\> returns 2.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id4661702				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.5)\</item\> returns 3. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7868892				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 1000.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145991				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDDOWN function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145991	24			0	uk	ROUNDDOWN				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146020	25			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ABRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number down, toward zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146037	26			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146051	27			0	uk	ROUNDDOWN(Number; Count)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146064	28			0	uk	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded down (towards zero) to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds down to an integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds down to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	uk	This function rounds towards zero. See ROUNDUP and ROUND for alternatives.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163164	30			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163178	31			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(1.234;2)\</item\> returns 1.23.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5833307				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(45.67;0)\</item\> returns 45.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7726676				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(-45.67)\</item\> returns -45.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3729361				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 900.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163268				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDUP function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163268	140			0	uk	ROUNDUP				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163297	141			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_AUFRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number up, away from zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163315	142			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163328	143			0	uk	ROUNDUP(Number; Count)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163342	144			0	uk	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded up (away from zero) to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds up to an integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds up to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9573961				0	uk	This function rounds away from zero. See ROUNDDOWN and ROUND for alternatives.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163381	146			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144786	147			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(1.1111;2)\</item\> returns 1.12.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7700430				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(1.2345;1)\</item\> returns 1.3.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1180455				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(45.67;0)\</item\> returns 46.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3405560				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(-45.67)\</item\> returns -46.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3409527				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 1000.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144877				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>SIN function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144877	408			0	uk	SIN				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144906	409			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SIN\"\>Returns the sine of the given angle (in radians).\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144923	410			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144937	411			0	uk	SIN(Number)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144950	412			0	uk	Returns the (trigonometric) sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8079470				0	uk	To return the sine of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144969	413			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144983	414			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SIN(PI()/2)\</item\> returns 1, the sine of PI/2 radians.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3916440				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SIN(RADIANS(30))\</item\> returns 0.5, the sine of 30 degrees.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163397				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>SINH function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163397	418			0	uk	SINH				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163426	419			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SINHYP\"\>Returns the hyperbolic sine of a number.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163444	420			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163457	421			0	uk	SINH(Number)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163471	422			0	uk	Returns the hyperbolic sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163491	423			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163504	424			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SINH(0)\</item\> returns 0, the hyperbolic sine of 0.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163596				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>SUM function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;numbers in cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163596	428			0	uk	SUM				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163625	429			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMME\"\>Adds all the numbers in a range of cells.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163643	430			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163656	431			0	uk	SUM(Number1; Number2; ...; Number30)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163671	432			0	uk	\<emph\>Number 1 to Number 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments whose sum is to be calculated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163690	433			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163704	434			0	uk	If you enter the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>; \<item type=\"input\"\>3 \</item\>and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\> in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 9 will be returned as the result.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151740	556			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM(A1;A3;B5)\</item\> calculates the sum of the three cells. \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM (A1:E10)\</item\> calculates the sum of all cells in the A1 to E10 cell range.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151756	619			0	uk	Conditions linked by AND can be used with the function SUM() in the following manner:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151774	620			0	uk	Example assumption: You have entered invoices into a table. Column A contains the date value of the invoice, column B the amounts. You want to find a formula that you can use to return the total of all amounts only for a specific month, e.g. only the amount for the period >=2008-01-01 to <2008-02-01. The range with the date values covers A1:A40, the range containing the amounts to be totaled is B1:B40. C1 contains the start date, 2008\<item type=\"input\"\>-01-01\</item\>, of the invoices to be included and C2 the date, 2008\<item type=\"input\"\>-02-01\</item\>, that is no longer included.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151799	621			0	uk	Enter the following formula as an array formula:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151813	622			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)\</item\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151828	623			0	uk	In order to enter this as an array formula, you must press the Shift\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>+ Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+ Enter keys instead of simply pressing the Enter key to close the formula. The formula will then be shown in the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> bar enclosed in braces.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151869	624			0	uk	{=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)}				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151884	625			0	uk	The formula is based on the fact that the result of a comparison is 1 if the criterion is met and 0 if it is not met. The individual comparison results will be treated as an array and used in matrix multiplication, and at the end the individual values will be totaled to give the result matrix.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151957				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>SUMIF function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;specified numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151957	436			0	uk	SUMIF				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151986	437			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMMEWENN\"\>Adds the cells specified by a given criteria.\</ahelp\> This function is used to browse a range when you search for a certain value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152015	438			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152028	439			0	uk	SUMIF(Range; Criteria; SumRange)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152043	440			0	uk	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152062	441			0	uk	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> is the cell in which the search criterion is shown, or the search criterion itself. If the criteria is written into the formula, it has to be surrounded by double quotes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152083	442			0	uk	\<emph\>SumRange\</emph\> is the range from which values are summed. If this parameter has not been indicated, the values found in the Range are summed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8347422				0	uk	SUMIF supports the reference concatenation operator (~) only in the Criteria parameter, and only if the optional SumRange parameter is not given.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152110	443			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152148	626			0	uk	To sum up only negative numbers: \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIF(A1:A10;"<0")\</item\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIF(A1:A10;">0";B1:10)\</item\> - sums values from the range B1:B10 only if the corresponding values in the range A1:A10 are >0.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	uk	See COUNTIF() for some more syntax examples that can be used with SUMIF().				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151957K				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>SUMIFS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;specified numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151957K	436			0	uk	SUMIFS				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151986K				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMMEWNRNG\"\>Sum the values of cells in a range that meet multiple criteria in multiple ranges.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152015K				0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152028K				0	uk	SUMIFS( Reference R ; Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152043K				0	uk	Sums the value of cells in range R that meet the Criterion C1 in the reference range R1, and the Criterion C2 in the reference range R2, and so on. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152062K				0	uk	A \<emph\>Criterion\</emph\> is a single cell Reference, Number or Text. If the criterion is written into the formula, it has to be surrounded by double quotes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152083K				0	uk	All \<emph\>Reference\</emph\> ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152110K	443			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152148K				0	uk	Sum up cells in range A1:10 if the entries in B1:B10 are positive, and the entries in D1:D10 are the letter "A": \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIFS(A1:A10;B1:B10;">0";D1:D10;"A")\</item\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196K				0	uk	See COUNTIFS() for some more syntax examples that can be used with SUMIFS().				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152195				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>TAN function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
