helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152269	450			0	uk	Returns the (trigonometric) tangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5752128				0	uk	To return the tangent of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152287	451			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152301	452			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TAN(PI()/4) \</item\>returns 1, the tangent of PI/4 radians.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1804864				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TAN(RADIANS(45))\</item\> returns 1, the tangent of 45 degrees.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3165434				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>TANH function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
