helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228	6			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_CASE\"\>Distinguishes between uppercase and lowercase letters when filtering the data.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154908	7			0	uk	Range contains column labels				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768	8			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_HEADER\"\>Includes the column labels in the first row of a cell range.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155306	9			0	uk	Copy results to				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319	10			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:ED_COPY_AREA\"\>Select the check box, and then select the cell range where you want to display the filter results.\</ahelp\> You can also select a named range from the list.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272	11			0	uk	Regular expression				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576	12			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_REGEXP\"\>Allows you to use wildcards in the filter definition.\</ahelp\> For a list of the regular expressions that $[officename] supports, click \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"here\"\>here\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377	33			0	uk	If the \<emph\>Regular Expressions\</emph\> check box is selected, you can use regular expressions in the Value field if the Condition list box is set to '=' EQUAL or '<>' UNEQUAL. This also applies to the respective cells that you reference for an advanced filter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149958	34			0	uk	No duplication				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876	35			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_UNIQUE\"\>Excludes duplicate rows in the list of filtered data.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154018	40			0	uk	Keep filter criteria				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123	41			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_FILTER:BTN_DEST_PERS\"\>Select the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> check box, and then specify the destination range where you want to display the filtered data. If this box is checked, the destination range remains linked to the source range. You must have defined the source range under \<emph\>Data - Define range\</emph\> as a database range.\</ahelp\> Following this, you can reapply the defined filter at any time as follows: click into the source range, then choose \<emph\>Data - Refresh Range\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018	36			0	uk	Data range				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042	37			0	uk	Displays the cell range or the name of the cell range that you want to filter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Remove Filter				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040400.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter\"\>Remove Filter\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataFilterRemoveFilter\"\>Removes the filter from the selected cell range. To enable this command, click inside the cell area where the filter was applied.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	DAYS360 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148555				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>DAYS360 function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148555	124			0	uk	\<variable id=\"days360\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_days360.xhp\"\>DAYS360\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	125			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAGE360\"\>Returns the difference between two dates based on the 360 day year used in interest calculations.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155347	126			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3155313	127			0	uk	DAYS360("Date1"; "Date2"; Type)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263	128			0	uk	If \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is earlier than \<emph\>Date1\</emph\>, the function will return a negative number.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3151064	129			0	uk	The optional argument \<emph\>Type\</emph\> determines the type of difference calculation. If Type = 0 or if the argument is missing, the US method (NASD, National Association of Securities Dealers) is used. If Type <> 0, the European method is used.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148641	130			0	uk	Examples				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3156348	132			0	uk	=DAYS360("2000-01-01";NOW()) returns the number of interest days from January 1, 2000 until today.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Protect Document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060000.xhp\" name=\"Protect Document\"\>Protect Document\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153362	2			0	uk	The\<emph\> Protect Document \</emph\>command prevents changes from being made to cells in the sheets or to sheets in a document. As an option, you can define a password. If a password is defined, removal of the protection is only possible if the user enters the correct password.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147228	3			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060100.xhp\" name=\"Sheets\"\>Sheets\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768	4			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060200.xhp\" name=\"Documents\"\>Documents\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10622				0	uk	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp#cell_protect\"/\>				20220827 09:49:47
