helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153891	380			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_DISC\"\>Calculates the allowance (discount) of a security as a percentage.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153982	381			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149756	382			0	uk	DISC("Settlement"; "Maturity"; Price; Redemption; Basis)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156014	383			0	uk	            \<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154304	384			0	uk	            \<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159180	385			0	uk	            \<emph\>Price\</emph\> is the price of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147253	386			0	uk	            \<emph\>Redemption\</emph\> is the redemption value of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151174	387			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	388			0	uk	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the maturity date is 2001-11-15. The price (purchase price) is 97, the redemption value is 100. Using daily balance calculation (basis 3) how high is the settlement (discount)?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152797	389			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DISC("2001-01-25";"2001-11-15";97;100;3)\</item\> returns about 0.0372 or 3.72 per cent.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154695				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>DURATION_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Excel functions\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>durations;fixed interest securities\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154695	402			0	uk	DURATION_ADD				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145768	403			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_DURATION\"\>Calculates the duration of a fixed interest security in years.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153904	404			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153373	405			0	uk	DURATION_ADD("Settlement"; "Maturity"; Coupon; Yield; Frequency; Basis)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155397	406			0	uk	            \<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148558	407			0	uk	            \<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153096	408			0	uk	            \<emph\>Coupon\</emph\> is the annual coupon interest rate (nominal rate of interest)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154594	409			0	uk	            \<emph\>Yield\</emph\> is the annual yield of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149906	410			0	uk	            \<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146995	411			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148834	412			0	uk	A security is purchased on 2001-01-01; the maturity date is 2006-01-01. The Coupon rate of interest is 8%. The yield is 9.0%. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how long is the duration?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154902	413			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DURATION_ADD("2001-01-01";"2006-01-01";0.08;0.09;2;3)\</item\>         				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159147				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>annual net interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating; annual net interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>net annual interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>EFFECTIVE function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159147	88			0	uk	EFFECTIVE				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154204	89			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EFFEKTIV\"\>Returns the net annual interest rate for a nominal interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145417	90			0	uk	Nominal interest refers to the amount of interest due at the end of a calculation period. Effective interest increases with the number of payments made. In other words, interest is often paid in installments (for example, monthly or quarterly) before the end of the calculation period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150510	91			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148805	92			0	uk	EFFECTIVE(Nom; P)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149768	93			0	uk	            \<emph\>Nom\</emph\> is the nominal interest.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149334	94			0	uk	            \<emph\>P\</emph\> is the number of interest payment periods per year.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154223	95			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3144499	96			0	uk	If the annual nominal interest rate is 9.75% and four interest calculation periods are defined, what is the actual interest rate (effective rate)?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772	97			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=EFFECTIVE(9.75%;4)\</item\> = 10.11% The annual effective rate is therefore 10.11%.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147241				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>effective interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>EFFECT_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147241	414			0	uk	EFFECT_ADD				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147524	415			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_EFFECT\"\>Calculates the effective annual rate of interest on the basis of the nominal interest rate and the number of interest payments per annum.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364	416			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155118	417			0	uk	EFFECT_ADD(NominalRate; NPerY)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148907	418			0	uk	            \<emph\>NominalRate\</emph\> is the annual nominal rate of interest.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154274	419			0	uk	            \<emph\>NPerY \</emph\>is the number of interest payments per year.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149156	420			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3158426	421			0	uk	What is the effective annual rate of interest for a 5.25% nominal rate and quarterly payment.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148927	422			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=EFFECT_ADD(0.0525;4)\</item\> returns 0.053543 or 5.3543%.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149998				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; arithmetic-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>arithmetic-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>depreciations;arithmetic-degressive\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>DDB function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149998	99			0	uk	DDB				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159190	100			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GDA\"\>Returns the depreciation of an asset for a specified period using the arithmetic-declining method.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361	101			0	uk	Use this form of depreciation if you require a higher initial depreciation value as opposed to linear depreciation. The depreciation value gets less with each period and is usually used for assets whose value loss is higher shortly after purchase (for example, vehicles, computers). Please note that the book value will never reach zero under this calculation type.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156038	102			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3166452	103			0	uk	DDB(Cost; Salvage; Life; Period; Factor)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153237	104			0	uk	            \<emph\>Cost\</emph\> fixes the initial cost of an asset.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149787	105			0	uk	            \<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> fixes the value of an asset at the end of its life.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152945	106			0	uk	            \<emph\>Life\</emph\> is the number of periods (for example, years or months) defining how long the asset is to be used.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149736	107			0	uk	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> states the period for which the value is to be calculated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150243	108			0	uk	            \<emph\>Factor\</emph\> (optional) is the factor by which depreciation decreases. If a value is not entered, the default is factor 2.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159274	109			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152882	110			0	uk	A computer system with an initial cost of 75,000 currency units is to be depreciated monthly over 5 years. The value at the end of the depreciation is to be 1 currency unit. The factor is 2.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154106	111			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DDB(75000;1;60;12;2) \</item\>= 1,721.81 currency units. Therefore, the double-declining depreciation in the twelfth month after purchase is 1,721.81 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149962				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; geometric-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>geometric-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>depreciations;geometric-degressive\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>DB function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149962	113			0	uk	DB				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148989	114			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GDA2\"\>Returns the depreciation of an asset for a specified period using the double-declining balance method.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156213	115			0	uk	This form of depreciation is used if you want to get a higher depreciation value at the beginning of the depreciation (as opposed to linear depreciation). The depreciation value is reduced with every depreciation period by the depreciation already deducted from the initial cost.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149807	116			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349	117			0	uk	DB(Cost; Salvage; Life; Period; Month)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148462	118			0	uk	            \<emph\>Cost\</emph\> is the initial cost of an asset.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148658	119			0	uk	            \<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> is the value of an asset at the end of the depreciation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145371	120			0	uk	            \<emph\>Life\</emph\> defines the period over which an asset is depreciated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154608	121			0	uk	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the length of each period. The length must be entered in the same date unit as the depreciation period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150829	122			0	uk	            \<emph\>Month\</emph\> (optional) denotes the number of months for the first year of depreciation. If an entry is not defined, 12 is used as the default.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151130	123			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156147	124			0	uk	A computer system with an initial cost of 25,000 currency units is to be depreciated over a three year period. The salvage value is to be 1,000 currency units. One period is 30 days.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149513	125			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DB(25000;1000;36;1;6)\</item\> = 1,075.00 currency units				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159242	126			0	uk	The fixed-declining depreciation of the computer system is 1,075.00 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153948				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>IRR function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating;internal rates of return, regular payments\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>internal rates of return;regular payments\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153948	128			0	uk	IRR				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3143282	129			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_IKV\"\>Calculates the internal rate of return for an investment.\</ahelp\> The values represent cash flow values at regular intervals, at least one value must be negative (payments), and at least one value must be positive (income).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150599	130			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155427	131			0	uk	IRR(Values; Guess)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3144758	132			0	uk	            \<emph\>Values\</emph\> represents an array containing the values.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	133			0	uk	            \<emph\>Guess\</emph\> (optional) is the estimated value. An iterative method is used to calculate the internal rate of return. If you can provide only few values, you should provide an initial guess to enable the iteration.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151258	134			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150630	135			0	uk	Under the assumption that cell contents are A1=\<item type=\"input\"\>-10000\</item\>, A2=\<item type=\"input\"\>3500\</item\>, A3=\<item type=\"input\"\>7600\</item\> and A4=\<item type=\"input\"\>1000\</item\>, the formula \<item type=\"input\"\>=IRR(A1:A4)\</item\> gives a result of 11,33%.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151012				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; interests for unchanged amortization installments\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>interests for unchanged amortization installments\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>ISPMT function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151012	314			0	uk	ISPMT				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148693	315			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISPMT\"\>Calculates the level of interest for unchanged amortization installments.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154661	316			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146070	317			0	uk	ISPMT(Rate; Period; TotalPeriods; Invest)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672	318			0	uk	            \<emph\>Rate\</emph\> sets the periodic interest rate.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145777	319			0	uk	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the number of installments for calculation of interest.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153678	320			0	uk	            \<emph\>TotalPeriods\</emph\> is the total number of installment periods.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159390	321			0	uk	            \<emph\>Invest\</emph\> is the amount of the investment.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156162	322			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149558	323			0	uk	For a credit amount of 120,000 currency units with a two-year term and monthly installments, at a yearly interest rate of 12% the level of interest after 1.5 years is required.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150949	324			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=ISPMT(1%;18;24;120000)\</item\> = -300 currency units. The monthly interest after 1.5 years amounts to 300 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146812	426			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060119.xhp\" name=\"Forward to Financial Functions Part Two\"\>Financial Functions Part Two\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154411	427			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060118.xhp\" name=\"Forward to Financial Functions Part Three\"\>Financial Functions Part Three\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Protecting Sheet				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087	1			0	uk	Protecting Sheet				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Protects the cells in the current sheet from being modified.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Choose \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Protect Sheet\</emph\> dialog in which you then specify sheet protection with or without a password.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	5			0	uk	To protect cells from further editing, the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> check box must be checked on the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020600.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Cell Protection\"\>\<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>\</link\> tab page or on the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> context menu.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	8			0	uk	Unprotected cells or cell ranges can be set up on a protected sheet by using the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> and \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> menus: 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123	16			0	uk	Select the cells that will be unprotected				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329	17			0	uk	Select \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>. Unmark the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156384	18			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> menu, activate protection for the sheet. Effective immediately, only the cell range you selected in step 1 can be edited.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149566	9			0	uk	To later change an unprotected area to a protected area, select the range. Next, on the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> tab page, check the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box. Finally, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet \</emph\>menu. The previously editable range is now protected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964	10			0	uk	Sheet protection also affects the context menu of the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen. The \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> and \<emph\>Rename\</emph\> commands cannot be selected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301	19			0	uk	If a sheet is protected, you will not be able to modify or delete any Cell Styles.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656	3			0	uk	A protected sheet or cell range can no longer be modified until this protection is disabled. To disable the protection, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> command. If no password was set, the sheet protection is immediately disabled. If the sheet was password protected, the \<emph\>Remove Protection\</emph\> dialog opens, where you must enter the password.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149815	11			0	uk	Once saved, protected sheets can only be saved again by using the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> command.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206	4			0	uk	Password (optional)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990	7			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Allows you to enter a password to protect the sheet from unauthorized changes.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148700	12			0	uk	Complete protection of your work can be achieved by combining both options on the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\> menu, including password protection. To prohibit opening the document altogether, in the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> dialog mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> box before you click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	SECOND 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159390				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>SECOND function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159390	86			0	uk	\<variable id=\"second\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_second.xhp\"\>SECOND\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3148974	87			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SEKUNDE\"\>Returns the second for the given time value.\</ahelp\> The second is given as an integer between 0 and 59.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154362	88			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3148407	89			0	uk	SECOND(Number)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3155904	90			0	uk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a time value, is a decimal, for which the second is to be returned.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149992	91			0	uk	Examples				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3153350	93			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SECOND(NOW())\</item\> returns the current second				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3150831	94			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SECOND(C4)\</item\> returns 17 if contents of C4 = \<item type=\"input\"\>12:20:17\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Function List				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154126				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>formula list window\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>function list window\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting functions; function list window\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154126	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04080000.xhp\" name=\"Function List\"\>Function List\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151118	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"funktionslistetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_FUNCTIONLIST\"\>This command opens the \<emph\>Function List\</emph\> window, which displays all functions that can be inserted into your document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The \<emph\>Function List\</emph\> window is similar to the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab page of the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Function Wizard\"\>Function Wizard\</link\>. The functions are inserted with placeholders to be replaced with your own values.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576	3			0	uk	The \<emph\>Function List\</emph\> window is a resizable \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#andocken\" name=\"dockable window\"\>dockable window\</link\>. Use it to quickly enter functions in the spreadsheet. By double-clicking an entry in the functions list, the respective function is directly inserted with all parameters.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145799	4			0	uk	Category List				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153160	5			0	uk	Function List				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149412	6			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:FID_FUNCTION_BOX:LB_FUNC\"\>Displays the available functions.\</ahelp\> When you select a function, the area below the list box displays a short description. To insert the selected function double-click it or click the \<emph\>Insert Function into calculation sheet\</emph\> icon.				20220827 09:49:47
