helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145621	18			0	uk	\<variable id=\"datevalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_datevalue.xhp\"\>DATEVALUE\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145087	19			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DATWERT\"\>Returns the internal date number for text in quotes.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281	20			0	uk	The internal date number is returned as a number. The number is determined by the date system that is used by $[officename] to calculate dates.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200903491982				0	uk	If the text string also includes a time value, DATEVALUE only returns the integer part of the conversion.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156294	21			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149268	22			0	uk	DATEVALUE("Text")				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3154819	23			0	uk	         \<emph\>Text\</emph\> is a valid date expression and must be entered with quotation marks.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156309	24			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155841	25			0	uk	         \<emph\>=DATEVALUE("1954-07-20")\</emph\> yields 19925.				20220827 09:49:47
