helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3152945	223			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_WEEKNUM\"\>The result indicates the number of the calendar week for a date.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DD				0	uk	The WEEKNUM_ADD function is designed to calculate week numbers exactly as Microsoft Excel does. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weeknum.xhp\"\>WEEKNUM\</link\> function, or format your date cells using the WW formatting code, when you need ISO 8601 week numbers.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153745	224			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3153685	225			0	uk	WEEKNUM_ADD(Date; ReturnType)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3159277	226			0	uk	\<emph\>Date\</emph\> is the date within the calendar week.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknumadd.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098	227			0	uk	\<emph\>ReturnType\</emph\> is 1 for week beginning on a Sunday, 2 for week beginning on a Monday.				20220827 09:49:47
