helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3152815	7			0	uk	\<emph\>Year\</emph\> is an integer between 1583 and 9957 or between 0 and 99.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153222	174			0	uk	In \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General \</item\>you can set from which year a two-digit number entry is recognized as 20xx.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155817	8			0	uk	\<emph\>Month\</emph\> is an integer indicating the month.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153183	9			0	uk	\<emph\>Day\</emph\> is an integer indicating the day of the month.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260	10			0	uk	If the values for month and day are out of bounds, they are carried over to the next digit. If you enter \<item type=\"input\"\>=DATE(00;12;31)\</item\> the result will be 12/31/00. If, on the other hand, you enter \<item type=\"input\"\>=DATE(00;13;31)\</item\> the result will be 1/31/01.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147477	12			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3152589	16			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DATE(00;1;31)\</item\> yields 1/31/00 if the cell format setting is MM/DD/YY.				20220827 09:49:47
