helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148754K1	157			0	uk	AVERAGEIF				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138K1				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERTB\"\>Average the values of cells in a range that meet a criteria.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153326K1	159			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734K1				0	uk	AVERAGEIF( Reference R ; Criterion C [ ; Reference A ] )				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260K1				0	uk	 If reference A is omitted, averages the values of cells in the reference range R that meet the Criterion C. If reference A is given, averages the values of cells of a range that is constructed using the top left cell of reference A and applying the dimensions, shape and size, of reference R. Does not accept constant values as reference parameters.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145139K1				0	uk	If no cell in range R matches the Criterion C, an Error is returned. If no Numbers are in the range to be averaged, an Error is returned.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149504K1	162			0	uk	Examples				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864K1				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AVERAGEIF(A1:A50;">"0)\</item\> will return the average of A1:A50 of all positive values in the range.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148754K2				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>AVERAGEIFS function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148754K2	157			0	uk	AVERAGEIFS				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138K2				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERTC\"\>Average the values of cells that meet multiple criteria in multiple ranges.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153326K2	159			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734K2				0	uk	AVERAGEIFS( Reference A ; Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260K2				0	uk	Averages the values of cells in the reference range A that meet the Criterion C1 in the reference range R1 and the Criterion C2 in the reference range R2, and so on.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145139K2				0	uk	All reference ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned. A logical AND is applied between each array result of each selection; a cell of reference range A is evaluated only if the same position in each array is the result of a Criterion match. If no numbers are in the result set to be averaged, an Error is returned.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149504K2	162			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864K2				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AVERAGEIFS(A1:A50;B1:B25;">"0)\</item\> will return the average of A1:A50 if all cells in the range B1 to B25 are greater than 0.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153933				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>MODE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>most common value\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153933	43			0	uk	MODE				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085	44			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MODALWERT\"\>Returns the most common value in a data set.\</ahelp\> If there are several values with the same frequency, it returns the smallest value. An error occurs when a value doesn't appear twice.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153003	45			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155950	46			0	uk	MODE(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150337	47			0	uk	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153571	48			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153733	49			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MODE(A1:A50)\</item\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149879				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>NEGBINOMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>negative binomial distribution\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149879	51			0	uk	NEGBINOMDIST				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155437	52			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NEGBINOMVERT\"\>Returns the negative binomial distribution.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145351	53			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935	54			0	uk	NEGBINOMDIST(X; R; SP)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153044	55			0	uk	\<emph\>X\</emph\> represents the value returned for unsuccessful tests.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151018	56			0	uk	\<emph\>R\</emph\> represents the value returned for successful tests.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148878	57			0	uk	\<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of the success of an attempt.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149539	58			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148770	59			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NEGBINOMDIST(1;1;0.5)\</item\> returns 0.25.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155516				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>NORMINV function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>normal distribution;inverse of\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155516	61			0	uk	NORMINV				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154634	62			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NORMINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the normal cumulative distribution.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153227	63			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147534	64			0	uk	NORMINV(Number; Mean; StDev)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154950	65			0	uk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> represents the probability value used to determine the inverse normal distribution.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150690	66			0	uk	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> represents the mean value in the normal distribution.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148594	67			0	uk	\<emph\>StDev\</emph\> represents the standard deviation of the normal distribution.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155822	68			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153921	69			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NORMINV(0.9;63;5)\</item\> returns 69.41. If the average egg weighs 63 grams with a standard deviation of 5, then there will be 90% probability that the egg will not be heavier than 69.41 grams.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153722				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>NORMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>density function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153722	71			0	uk	NORMDIST				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	72			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NORMVERT\"\>Returns the density function or the normal cumulative distribution.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083282	73			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150613	74			0	uk	NORMDIST(Number; Mean; StDev; C)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149820	75			0	uk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value of the distribution based on which the normal distribution is to be calculated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146063	76			0	uk	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> is the mean value of the distribution.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156295	77			0	uk	\<emph\>StDev\</emph\> is the standard deviation of the distribution.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080	78			0	uk	\<emph\>C\</emph\> is optional. \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 0 calculates the density function, \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 calculates the distribution.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152972	79			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283	80			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NORMDIST(70;63;5;0)\</item\> returns 0.03.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149448	81			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NORMDIST(70;63;5;1)\</item\> returns 0.92.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152934				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>PEARSON function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
