helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387	134			0	uk	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> represents the array of data in the sample.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155589	135			0	uk	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> represents the type of quartile. (0 = MIN, 1 = 25%, 2 = 50% (MEDIAN), 3 = 75% and 4 = MAX.)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149103	136			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3159276	137			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=QUARTILE(A1:A50;2)\</item\> returns the value of which 50% of the scale corresponds to the lowest to highest values in the range A1:A50.				20220827 09:49:47
