helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151382	159			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153949	160			0	uk	How often can 2 objects be selected from a total of 11 objects?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	161			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PERMUTATIONA(11;2)\</item\> returns 121.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150622	162			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PERMUTATIONA(6;3)\</item\> returns 216. There are 216 different possibilities to put a sequence of 3 playing cards together out of six playing cards if every card is returned before the next one is drawn.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152952				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>PROB function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152952	164			0	uk	PROB				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154110	165			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WAHRSCHBEREICH\"\>Returns the probability that values in a range are between two limits.\</ahelp\> If there is no \<item type=\"literal\"\>End\</item\> value, this function calculates the probability based on the principle that the Data values are equal to the value of \<item type=\"literal\"\>Start\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146810	166			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3147330	167			0	uk	PROB(Data; Probability; Start; End)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573	168			0	uk	            \<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the array or range of data in the sample.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156334	169			0	uk	            \<emph\>Probability\</emph\> is the array or range of the corresponding probabilities.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151107	170			0	uk	            \<emph\>Start\</emph\> is the start value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153694	171			0	uk	            \<emph\>End\</emph\> (optional) is the end value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed. If this parameter is missing, the probability for the \<emph\>Start \</emph\>value is calculated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574	172			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666	173			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PROB(A1:A50;B1:B50;50;60)\</item\> returns the probability with which a value within the range of A1:A50 is also within the limits between 50 and 60. Every value within the range of A1:A50 has a probability within the range of B1:B50.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150941				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>WEIBULL function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150941	175			0	uk	WEIBULL				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154916	176			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WEIBULL\"\>Returns the values of the Weibull distribution.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372767				0	uk	The Weibull distribution is a continuous probability distribution, with parameters Alpha > 0 (shape) and Beta > 0 (scale). 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372777				0	uk	If C is 0, WEIBULL calculates the probability density function.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372743				0	uk	If C is 1, WEIBULL calculates the cumulative distribution function.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159393	177			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154478	178			0	uk	WEIBULL(Number; Alpha; Beta; C)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151317	179			0	uk	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value at which to calculate the Weibull distribution.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3158436	180			0	uk	            \<emph\>Alpha \</emph\>is the shape parameter of the Weibull distribution.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154668	181			0	uk	            \<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is the scale parameter of the Weibull distribution.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154825	182			0	uk	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> indicates the type of function.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153794	183			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3146077	184			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=WEIBULL(2;1;1;1)\</item\> returns 0.86.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372899				0	uk	See also the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Calc:_WEIBULL_function\"\>Wiki page\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Show Details (Pivot Table)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3344523				0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080700.xhp\"\>Show Details (Pivot Table)\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080700.xhp	0	help	par_id871303				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts a new "drill-down" sheet with more information about the current pivot table cell. You can also double-click a pivot table cell to insert the "drill-down" sheet. The new sheet shows a subset of rows from the original data source that constitutes the result data displayed in the current cell.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080700.xhp	0	help	par_id7132480				0	uk	Hidden items are not evaluated, the rows for the hidden items are included. Show Details is available only for pivot tables that are based on cell ranges or database data.				20220827 09:49:47
