helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_day.xhp	0	help	par_id3149443	110			0	uk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a time value, is a decimal, for which the day is to be returned.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_day.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163809	111			0	uk	Examples 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_day.xhp	0	help	par_id3151200	112			0	uk	DAY(1) returns 31 (since $[officename] starts counting at zero from December 30, 1899)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_day.xhp	0	help	par_id3154130	113			0	uk	DAY(NOW()) returns the current day.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_day.xhp	0	help	par_id3159190	114			0	uk	=DAY(C4) returns 5 if you enter 1901-08-05 in cell C4 (the date value might get formatted differently after you press Enter).				20220827 09:49:47
