helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149282	83			0	uk	The formula in cell B16 is =DCOUNT(A1:E10;0;A13:E14)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150962	192			0	uk	Database Function Parameters:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155837	84			0	uk	The following items are the parameter definitions for all database functions:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149453	85			0	uk	\<emph\>Database\</emph\> is the cell range defining the database.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151272	86			0	uk	\<emph\>DatabaseField\</emph\> specifies the column where the function operates on after the search criteria of the first parameter is applied and the data rows are selected. It is not related to the search criteria itself. Use the number 0 to specify the whole data range. \<variable id=\"quotes\"\>To reference a column by means of the column header name, place quotation marks around the header name. \</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147083	87			0	uk	\<emph\>SearchCriteria\</emph\> is the cell range containing search criteria. If you write several criteria in one row they are connected by AND. If you write the criteria in different rows they are connected by OR. Empty cells in the search criteria range will be ignored.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151188	188			0	uk	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - Calculate\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</link\> to define how $[officename] Calc acts when searching for identical entries.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3882869				0	uk	See also the Wiki page about \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Conditional_Counting_and_Summation\"\>Conditional Counting and Summation\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150882				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>DCOUNT function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>counting rows;with numeric values\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150882	88			0	uk	DCOUNT				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156133	89			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBANZAHL\"\>DCOUNT counts the number of rows (records) in a database that match the specified search criteria and contain numerical values.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156099	90			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153218	91			0	uk	DCOUNT(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153273	187			0	uk	For the DatabaseField parameter you can enter a cell to specify the column, or enter the number 0 for the entire database. The parameter cannot be empty. \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/01/04060101.xhp#quotes\"/\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154743	92			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153623	93			0	uk	In the example above (scroll up, please), we want to know how many children have to travel more than 600 meters to school. The result is to be stored in cell B16. Set the cursor in cell B16. Enter the formula \<item type=\"input\"\>=DCOUNT(A1:E10;0;A13:E14)\</item\> in B16. The \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> helps you to input ranges.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149142	94			0	uk	\<emph\>Database\</emph\> is the range of data to be evaluated, including its headers: in this case A1:E10. \<emph\>DatabaseField\</emph\> specifies the column for the search criteria: in this case, the whole database. \<emph\>SearchCriteria\</emph\> is the range where you can enter the search parameters: in this case, A13:E14.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145652	95			0	uk	To learn how many children in second grade are over 7 years of age, delete the entry >600 in cell D14 and enter \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\> in cell B14 under Grade, and enter \<item type=\"input\"\>>7\</item\> in cell C14 to the right. The result is 2. Two children are in second grade and over 7 years of age. As both criteria are in the same row, they are connected by AND.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156123				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>DCOUNTA function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>records;counting in Calc databases\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>counting rows;with numeric or alphanumeric values\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156123	97			0	uk	DCOUNTA				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156110	98			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBANZAHL2\"\>DCOUNTA counts the number of rows (records) in a database that match the specified search conditions, and contain numeric or alphanumeric values.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143228	99			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146893	100			0	uk	DCOUNTA(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149751	101			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153982	102			0	uk	In the example above (scroll up, please), you can search for the number of children whose name starts with an E or a subsequent letter. Edit the formula in B16 to read \<item type=\"input\"\>=DCOUNTA(A1:E10;"Name";A13:E14)\</item\>. Delete the old search criteria and enter \<item type=\"input\"\>>=E\</item\> under Name in field A14. The result is 5. If you now delete all number values for Greta in row 8, the result changes to 4. Row 8 is no longer included in the count because it does not contain any values. The name Greta is text, not a value. Note that the DatabaseField parameter must point to a column that can contain values.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147256				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>DGET function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>cell contents;searching in Calc databases\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching;cell contents in Calc databases\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147256	104			0	uk	DGET				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801	105			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBAUSZUG\"\>DGET returns the contents of the referenced cell in a database which matches the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\> In case of an error, the function returns either #VALUE! for no row found, or Err502 for more than one cell found.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159344	106			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154696	107			0	uk	DGET(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153909	108			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388	109			0	uk	In the above example (scroll up, please), we want to determine what grade a child is in, whose name was entered in cell A14. The formula is entered in cell B16 and differs slightly from the earlier examples because only one column (one database field) can be entered for \<emph\>DatabaseField\</emph\>. Enter the following formula:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153096	110			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DGET(A1:E10;"Grade";A13:E14)\</item\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150524	111			0	uk	Enter the name \<item type=\"input\"\>Frank\</item\> in A14, and you see the result 2. Frank is in second grade. Enter \<item type=\"input\"\>"Age"\</item\> instead of "Grade" and you will get Frank's age.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148833	112			0	uk	Or enter the value \<item type=\"input\"\>11\</item\> in cell C14 only, and delete the other entries in this row. Edit the formula in B16 as follows:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149912	113			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DGET(A1:E10;"Name";A13:E14)\</item\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148813	114			0	uk	Instead of the grade, the name is queried. The answer appears at once: Daniel is the only child aged 11.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149766				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>DMAX function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>maximum values in Calc databases\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching;maximum values in columns\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149766	115			0	uk	DMAX				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154903	116			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBMAX\"\>DMAX returns the maximum content of a cell (field) in a database (all records) that matches the specified search conditions.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771	117			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157	118			0	uk	DMAX(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145420	119			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148442	120			0	uk	To find out how much the heaviest child in each grade weighed in the above example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148804	121			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DMAX(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)\</item\>				20220827 09:49:47
