helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148462				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>DSTDEV function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>standard deviations in databases;based on a sample\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148462	145			0	uk	DSTDEV				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154605	146			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBSTDABW\"\>DSTDEV calculates the standard deviation of a population based on a sample, using the numbers in a database column that match the given conditions.\</ahelp\> The records are treated as a sample of data. That means that the children in the example represent a cross section of all children. Note that a representative result can not be obtained from a sample of less than one thousand.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149427	147			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148661	148			0	uk	DSTDEV(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153945	149			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149934	150			0	uk	To find the standard deviation of the weight for all children of the same age in the example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150630	151			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DSTDEV(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)\</item\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153536	152			0	uk	In row 14, under Age, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>7, 8, 9,\</item\> and so on, one after the other. The result shown is the standard deviation of the weight of all children of this age.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150429				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>DSTDEVP function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>standard deviations in databases;based on populations\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150429	153			0	uk	DSTDEVP				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145598	154			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBSTDABWN\"\>DSTDEVP calculates the standard deviation of a population based on all cells of a data range which match the search criteria.\</ahelp\> The records from the example are treated as the whole population.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145307	155			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484	156			0	uk	DSTDEVP(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20220827 09:49:47
