helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148742	343			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060103.xhp\" name=\"Back to Financial Functions Part One\"\>Back to Financial Functions Part One\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151341	344			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060118.xhp\" name=\"Forward to Financial Functions Part Three\"\>Forward to Financial Functions Part Three\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150026				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>PPMT function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150026	238			0	uk	PPMT				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146942	239			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KAPZ\"\>Returns for a given period the payment on the principal for an investment that is based on periodic and constant payments and a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150459	240			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146878	241			0	uk	PPMT(Rate; Period; NPer; PV; FV; Type)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151228	242			0	uk	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148887	243			0	uk	\<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the amortizement period. P = 1 for the first and P = NPer for the last period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148436	244			0	uk	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods during which annuity is paid.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153035	245			0	uk	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present value in the sequence of payments.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474	246			0	uk	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the desired (future) value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3144744	247			0	uk	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) defines the due date. F = 1 for payment at the beginning of a period and F = 0 for payment at the end of a period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067C				0	uk	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148582	248			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154811	249			0	uk	How high is the periodic monthly payment at an annual interest rate of 8.75% over a period of 3 years? The cash value is 5,000 currency units and is always paid at the beginning of a period. The future value is 8,000 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149246	250			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PPMT(8.75%/12;1;36;5000;8000;1)\</item\> = -350.99 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146139				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; total amortizement rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>total amortizement rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>amortization installment\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>repayment installment\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>CUMPRINC function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139	252			0	uk	CUMPRINC				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150140	253			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUMKAPITAL\"\>Returns the cumulative interest paid for an investment period with a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149188	254			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148733	255			0	uk	CUMPRINC(Rate; NPer; PV; S; E; Type)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864	256			0	uk	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3166052	257			0	uk	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the payment period with the total number of periods. NPER can also be a non-integer value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150007	258			0	uk	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the current value in the sequence of payments.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153112	259			0	uk	\<emph\>S\</emph\> is the first period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146847	260			0	uk	\<emph\>E\</emph\> is the last period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145167	261			0	uk	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the due date of the payment at the beginning or end of each period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154502	262			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153570	263			0	uk	What are the payoff amounts if the yearly interest rate is 5.5% for 36 months? The cash value is 15,000 currency units. The payoff amount is calculated between the 10th and 18th period. The due date is at the end of the period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149884	264			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CUMPRINC(5.5%/12;36;15000;10;18;0)\</item\> = -3669.74 currency units. The payoff amount between the 10th and 18th period is 3669.74 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150019				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>CUMPRINC_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150019	182			0	uk	CUMPRINC_ADD				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145246	183			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_CUMPRINC\"\> Calculates the cumulative redemption of a loan in a period.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153047	184			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3157970	185			0	uk	CUMPRINC_ADD(Rate; NPer; PV; StartPeriod; EndPeriod; Type)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145302	186			0	uk	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the interest rate for each period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017	187			0	uk	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of payment periods. The rate and NPER must refer to the same unit, and thus both be calculated annually or monthly.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620	188			0	uk	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the current value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145352	189			0	uk	\<emph\>StartPeriod\</emph\> is the first payment period for the calculation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3157986	190			0	uk	\<emph\>EndPeriod\</emph\> is the last payment period for the calculation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150570	191			0	uk	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the maturity of a payment at the end of each period (Type = 0) or at the start of the period (Type = 1).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150269	192			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774	193			0	uk	The following mortgage loan is taken out on a house:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150661	194			0	uk	Rate: 9.00 per cent per annum (9% / 12 = 0.0075), Duration: 30 years (payment periods = 30 * 12 = 360), NPV: 125000 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155512	195			0	uk	How much will you repay in the second year of the mortgage (thus from periods 13 to 24)?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149394	196			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CUMPRINC_ADD(0.0075;360;125000;13;24;0)\</item\> returns -934.1071				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149026	197			0	uk	In the first month you will be repaying the following amount:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154636	198			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CUMPRINC_ADD(0.0075;360;125000;1;1;0)\</item\> returns -68.27827				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155370				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; accumulated interests\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>accumulated interests\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>CUMIPMT function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155370	266			0	uk	CUMIPMT				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3158411	267			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUMZINSZ\"\>Calculates the cumulative interest payments, that is, the total interest, for an investment based on a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155814	268			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147536	269			0	uk	CUMIPMT(Rate; NPer; PV; S; E; Type)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150475	270			0	uk	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153921	271			0	uk	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the payment period with the total number of periods. NPER can also be a non-integer value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153186	272			0	uk	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the current value in the sequence of payments.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156259	273			0	uk	\<emph\>S\</emph\> is the first period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155990	274			0	uk	\<emph\>E\</emph\> is the last period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149777	275			0	uk	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the due date of the payment at the beginning or end of each period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153723	276			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147478	277			0	uk	What are the interest payments at a yearly interest rate of 5.5 %, a payment period of monthly payments for 2 years and a current cash value of 5,000 currency units? The start period is the 4th and the end period is the 6th period. The payment is due at the beginning of each period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819	278			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CUMIPMT(5.5%/12;24;5000;4;6;1)\</item\> = -57.54 currency units. The interest payments for between the 4th and 6th period are 57.54 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3083280				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>CUMIPMT_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083280	165			0	uk	CUMIPMT_ADD				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3152482	166			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_CUMIPMT\"\>Calculates the accumulated interest for a period.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149713	167			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145087	168			0	uk	CUMIPMT_ADD(Rate; NPer; PV; StartPeriod; EndPeriod; Type)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149277	169			0	uk	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the interest rate for each period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149270	170			0	uk	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of payment periods. The rate and NPER must refer to the same unit, and thus both be calculated annually or monthly.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3152967	171			0	uk	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the current value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156308	172			0	uk	\<emph\>StartPeriod\</emph\> is the first payment period for the calculation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149453	173			0	uk	\<emph\>EndPeriod\</emph\> is the last payment period for the calculation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150962	174			0	uk	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the maturity of a payment at the end of each period (Type = 0) or at the start of the period (Type = 1).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152933	175			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156324	176			0	uk	The following mortgage loan is taken out on a house:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147566	177			0	uk	Rate: 9.00 per cent per annum (9% / 12 = 0.0075), Duration: 30 years (NPER = 30 * 12 = 360), Pv: 125000 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151272	178			0	uk	How much interest must you pay in the second year of the mortgage (thus from periods 13 to 24)?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156130	179			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CUMIPMT_ADD(0.0075;360;125000;13;24;0)\</item\> returns -11135.23.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150764	180			0	uk	How much interest must you pay in the first month?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146857	181			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CUMIPMT_ADD(0.0075;360;125000;1;1;0)\</item\> returns -937.50.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150878				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>PRICE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>prices; fixed interest securities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sales values;fixed interest securities\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150878	9			0	uk	PRICE				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153210	10			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_PRICE\"\>Calculates the market value of a fixed interest security with a par value of 100 currency units as a function of the forecast yield.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154646	11			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3152804	12			0	uk	PRICE(Settlement; Maturity; Rate; Yield; Redemption; Frequency; Basis)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156121	13			0	uk	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983	14			0	uk	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153755	15			0	uk	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the annual nominal rate of interest (coupon interest rate)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155999	16			0	uk	\<emph\>Yield\</emph\> is the annual yield of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114	17			0	uk	\<emph\>Redemption\</emph\> is the redemption value per 100 currency units of par value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155846	18			0	uk	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153148	19			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150260	20			0	uk	A security is purchased on 1999-02-15; the maturity date is 2007-11-15. The nominal rate of interest is 5.75%. The yield is 6.5%. The redemption value is 100 currency units. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). With calculation on basis 0, the price is as follows:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147273	21			0	uk	=PRICE("1999-02-15"; "2007-11-15"; 0.0575; 0.065; 100; 2; 0) returns 95.04287.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151297				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>PRICEDISC function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>prices;non-interest-bearing securities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sales values;non-interest-bearing securities\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151297	22			0	uk	PRICEDISC				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155100	23			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_PRICEDISC\"\>Calculates the price per 100 currency units of par value of a non-interest- bearing security.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294	24			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146084	25			0	uk	PRICEDISC(Settlement; Maturity; Discount; Redemption; Basis)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3159179	26			0	uk	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154304	27			0	uk	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156014	28			0	uk	\<emph\>Discount\</emph\> is the discount of a security as a percentage.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147489	29			0	uk	\<emph\>Redemption\</emph\> is the redemption value per 100 currency units of par value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152794	30			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149198	31			0	uk	A security is purchased on 1999-02-15; the maturity date is 1999-03-01. Discount in per cent is 5.25%. The redemption value is 100. When calculating on basis 2 the price discount is as follows:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151178	32			0	uk	=PRICEDISC("1999-02-15"; "1999-03-01"; 0.0525; 100; 2) returns 99.79583.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154693				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>PRICEMAT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>prices;interest-bearing securities\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154693	33			0	uk	PRICEMAT				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153906	34			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_PRICEMAT\"\>Calculates the price per 100 currency units of par value of a security, that pays interest on the maturity date.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154933	35			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155393	36			0	uk	PRICEMAT(Settlement; Maturity; Issue; Rate; Yield; Basis)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153102	37			0	uk	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150530	38			0	uk	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149903	39			0	uk	\<emph\>Issue\</emph\> is the date of issue of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148828	40			0	uk	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the interest rate of the security on the issue date.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146993	41			0	uk	\<emph\>Yield\</emph\> is the annual yield of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150507	42			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154289	43			0	uk	Settlement date: February 15 1999, maturity date: April 13 1999, issue date: November 11 1998. Interest rate: 6.1 per cent, yield: 6.1 per cent, basis: 30/360 = 0.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154905	44			0	uk	The price is calculated as follows:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3158409	45			0	uk	=PRICEMAT("1999-02-15";"1999-04-13";"1998-11-11"; 0.061; 0.061;0) returns 99.98449888.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148448				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; durations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>durations;calculating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DURATION function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148448	280			0	uk	DURATION				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153056	281			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LAUFZEIT\"\>Calculates the number of periods required by an investment to attain the desired value.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145421	282			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148933	283			0	uk	DURATION(Rate; PV; FV)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148801	284			0	uk	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is a constant. The interest rate is to be calculated for the entire duration (duration period). The interest rate per period is calculated by dividing the interest rate by the calculated duration. The internal rate for an annuity is to be entered as Rate/12.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239	285			0	uk	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present (current) value. The cash value is the deposit of cash or the current cash value of an allowance in kind. As a deposit value a positive value must be entered; the deposit must not be 0 or <0.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515	286			0	uk	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> is the expected value. The future value determines the desired (future) value of the deposit.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153579	287			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148480	288			0	uk	At an interest rate of 4.75%, a cash value of 25,000 currency units and a future value of 1,000,000 currency units, a duration of 79.49 payment periods is returned. The periodic payment is the resulting quotient from the future value and the duration, in this case 1,000,000/79.49=12,850.20.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148912				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;linear depreciations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>depreciations;linear\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>linear depreciations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>straight-line depreciations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>SLN function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148912	290			0	uk	SLN				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149154	291			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LIA\"\>Returns the straight-line depreciation of an asset for one period.\</ahelp\>The amount of the depreciation is constant during the depreciation period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153240	292			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3166456	293			0	uk	SLN(Cost; Salvage; Life)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146955	294			0	uk	\<emph\>Cost\</emph\> is the initial cost of an asset.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149796	295			0	uk	\<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> is the value of an asset at the end of the depreciation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3166444	296			0	uk	\<emph\>Life\</emph\> is the depreciation period determining the number of periods in the depreciation of the asset.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155579	297			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098	298			0	uk	Office equipment with an initial cost of 50,000 currency units is to be depreciated over 7 years. The value at the end of the depreciation is to be 3,500 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153390	299			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SLN(50000;3,500;84)\</item\> = 553.57 currency units. The periodic monthly depreciation of the office equipment is 553.57 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153739				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>MDURATION function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Macauley duration\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153739	217			0	uk	MDURATION				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149923	218			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_MDURATION\"\>Calculates the modified Macauley duration of a fixed interest security in years.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149964	219			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148987	220			0	uk	MDURATION(Settlement; Maturity; Coupon; Yield; Frequency; Basis)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148619	221			0	uk	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149805	222			0	uk	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154338	223			0	uk	\<emph\>Coupon\</emph\> is the annual nominal rate of interest (coupon interest rate)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148466	224			0	uk	\<emph\>Yield\</emph\> is the annual yield of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149423	225			0	uk	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154602	226			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148652	227			0	uk	A security is purchased on 2001-01-01; the maturity date is 2006-01-01. The nominal rate of interest is 8%. The yield is 9.0%. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how long is the modified duration?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145378	228			0	uk	=MDURATION("2001-01-01"; "2006-01-01"; 0.08; 0.09; 2; 3) returns 4.02 years.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149242				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;net present values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>net present values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>NPV function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149242	301			0	uk	NPV				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145308	302			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NBW\"\>Returns the present value of an investment based on a series of periodic cash flows and a discount rate. To get the net present value, subtract the cost of the project (the initial cash flow at time zero) from the returned value.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149937	303			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153321	304			0	uk	NPV(Rate; Value1; Value2; ...)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150630	305			0	uk	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the discount rate for a period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150427	306			0	uk	\<emph\>Value1;...\</emph\> are up to 30 values, which represent deposits or withdrawals.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153538	307			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154800	308			0	uk	What is the net present value of periodic payments of 10, 20 and 30 currency units with a discount rate of 8.75%. At time zero the costs were paid as -40 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270	309			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NPV(8.75%;10;20;30)\</item\> = 49.43 currency units. The net present value is the returned value minus the initial costs of 40 currency units, therefore 9.43 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149484				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;nominal interest rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>nominal interest rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>NOMINAL function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149484	311			0	uk	NOMINAL				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149596	312			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NOMINAL\"\>Calculates the yearly nominal interest rate, given the effective rate and the number of compounding periods per year.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151252	313			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3152769	314			0	uk	NOMINAL(EffectiveRate; NPerY)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147521	315			0	uk	\<emph\>EffectiveRate\</emph\> is the effective interest rate				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156334	316			0	uk	\<emph\>NPerY\</emph\> is the number of periodic interest payments per year.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154473	317			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147091	318			0	uk	What is the nominal interest per year for an effective interest rate of 13.5% if twelve payments are made per year.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154831	319			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NOMINAL(13.5%;12)\</item\> = 12.73%. The nominal interest rate per year is 12.73%.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155123				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>NOMINAL_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
