helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154111	203			0	uk	\<emph\>FractionalDollar\</emph\> is a number given as a decimal fraction.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153695	204			0	uk	\<emph\>Fraction\</emph\> is a whole number that is used as the denominator of the decimal fraction.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153884	205			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150941	206			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DOLLARDE(1.02;16)\</item\> stands for 1 and 2/16. This returns 1.125.				20220827 09:49:47
