helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148974	321			0	uk	MIRR				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155497	322			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QIKV\"\>Calculates the modified internal rate of return of a series of investments.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154354	323			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148399	324			0	uk	MIRR(Values; Investment; ReinvestRate)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896	325			0	uk	\<emph\>Values\</emph\> corresponds to the array or the cell reference for cells whose content corresponds to the payments.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149998	326			0	uk	\<emph\>Investment\</emph\> is the rate of interest of the investments (the negative values of the array)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3159408	327			0	uk	\<emph\>ReinvestRate\</emph\>:the rate of interest of the reinvestment (the positive values of the array)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154714	328			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147352	329			0	uk	Assuming a cell content of A1 = \<item type=\"input\"\>-5\</item\>, A2 = \<item type=\"input\"\>10\</item\>, A3 = \<item type=\"input\"\>15\</item\>, and A4 = \<item type=\"input\"\>8\</item\>, and an investment value of 0.5 and a reinvestment value of 0.1, the result is 94.16%.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149323				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>YIELD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rates of return;securities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>yields, see also rates of return\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149323	129			0	uk	YIELD				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150643	130			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_YIELD\"\>Calculates the yield of a security.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149344	131			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149744	132			0	uk	YIELD(Settlement; Maturity; Rate; Price; Redemption; Frequency; Basis)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154526	133			0	uk	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153266	134			0	uk	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151284	135			0	uk	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the annual rate of interest.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147314	136			0	uk	\<emph\>Price\</emph\> is the price (purchase price) of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145156	137			0	uk	\<emph\>Redemption\</emph\> is the redemption value per 100 currency units of par value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3159218	138			0	uk	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147547	139			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151214	140			0	uk	A security is purchased on 1999-02-15. It matures on 2007-11-15. The rate of interest is 5.75%. The price is 95.04287 currency units per 100 units of par value, the redemption value is 100 units. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency = 2) and the basis is 0. How high is the yield?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154194	141			0	uk	=YIELD("1999-02-15"; "2007-11-15"; 0.0575 ;95.04287; 100; 2; 0) returns 0.065 or 6.50 per cent.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150100				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>YIELDDISC function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rates of return;non-interest-bearing securities\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
