helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150237	146			0	uk	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146924	147			0	uk	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151201	148			0	uk	\<emph\>Price\</emph\> is the price (purchase price) of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156049	149			0	uk	\<emph\>Redemption\</emph\> is the redemption value per 100 currency units of par value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154139	150			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3163815	151			0	uk	A non-interest-bearing security is purchased on 1999-02-15. It matures on 1999-03-01. The price is 99.795 currency units per 100 units of par value, the redemption value is 100 units. The basis is 2. How high is the yield?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155187	152			0	uk	=YIELDDISC("1999-02-15"; "1999-03-01"; 99.795; 100; 2) returns 0.052823 or 5.2823 per cent.				20220827 09:49:47
