helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3163717	163			0	uk	A security is purchased on 1999-03-15. It matures on 1999-11-03. The issue date was 1998-11-08. The rate of interest is 6.25%, the price is 100.0123 units. The basis is 0. How high is the yield?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155311	164			0	uk	=YIELDMAT("1999-03-15"; "1999-11-03"; "1998-11-08"; 0.0625; 100.0123; 0) returns 0.060954 or 6.0954 per cent.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149577				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;annuities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>annuities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PMT function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149577	330			0	uk	PMT				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563	331			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RMZ\"\>Returns the periodic payment for an annuity with constant interest rates.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145257	332			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147278	333			0	uk	PMT(Rate; NPer; PV; FV; Type)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147291	334			0	uk	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148641	335			0	uk	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the number of periods in which annuity is paid.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156360	336			0	uk	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present value (cash value) in a sequence of payments.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154920	337			0	uk	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the desired value (future value) to be reached at the end of the periodic payments.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156434	338			0	uk	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the due date for the periodic payments. Type=1 is payment at the beginning and Type=0 is payment at the end of each period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_idN11645				0	uk	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152358	339			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222	340			0	uk	What are the periodic payments at a yearly interest rate of 1.99% if the payment time is 3 years and the cash value is 25,000 currency units. There are 36 months as 36 payment periods, and the interest rate per payment period is 1.99%/12.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155943	341			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PMT(1.99%/12;36;25000)\</item\> = -715.96 currency units. The periodic monthly payment is therefore 715.96 currency units.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155799				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>TBILLEQ function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>treasury bills;annual return\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>annual return on treasury bills\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155799	58			0	uk	TBILLEQ				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154403	59			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_TBILLEQ\"\>Calculates the annual return on a treasury bill ().\</ahelp\> A treasury bill is purchased on the settlement date and sold at the full par value on the maturity date, that must fall within the same year. A discount is deducted from the purchase price.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155080	60			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224	61			0	uk	TBILLEQ(Settlement; Maturity; Discount)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156190	62			0	uk	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153827	63			0	uk	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150310	64			0	uk	\<emph\>Discount\</emph\> is the percentage discount on acquisition of the security.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150324	65			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153173	66			0	uk	Settlement date: March 31 1999, maturity date: June 1 1999, discount: 9.14 per cent.				20220827 09:49:47
