helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3158417	148			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_FORMEL\"\>Displays the formula of a formula cell as a text string.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154954	149			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147535	150			0	uk	FORMULA(Reference)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3014313				0	uk	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is a reference to a cell containing a formula.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id8857081				0	uk	An invalid reference or a reference to a cell with no formula results in the error value #N/A.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152820	151			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179	152			0	uk	If cell A8 contains the formula \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM(1;2;3)\</item\> then				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153923	153			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FORMULA(A8)\</item\> returns the text =SUM(1;2;3).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155409				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>ISREF function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references;testing cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell contents;testing for references\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155409	37			0	uk	ISREF				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153723	38			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTBEZUG\"\>Tests if the argument is a reference.\</ahelp\> Returns TRUE if the argument is a reference, returns FALSE otherwise. When given a reference this function does not examine the value being referenced.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147175	39			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149821	40			0	uk	ISREF(Value)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3146152	41			0	uk	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the value to be tested, to determine whether it is a reference.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083448	42			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154317	43			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISREF(C5)\</item\> returns the result TRUE because C5 is a valid reference.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id9728072				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISREF("abcdef")\</item\> returns always FALSE because a text can never be a reference.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id2131544				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISREF(4)\</item\> returns FALSE.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id4295480				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISREF(INDIRECT("A6"))\</item\> returns TRUE, because INDIRECT is a function that returns a reference.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3626819				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISREF(ADDRESS(1; 1; 2;"Sheet2"))\</item\> returns FALSE, because ADDRESS is a function that returns a text, although it looks like a reference.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154812				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>ISERR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error codes;controlling\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154812	45			0	uk	ISERR				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149282	46			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISTFEHL\"\>Tests for error conditions, except the #N/A error value, and returns TRUE or FALSE.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149450	47			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156312	48			0	uk	ISERR(Value)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3146857	49			0	uk	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is any value or expression which is tested to see whether an error value other than #N/A is present.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153212	50			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153276	51			0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISERR(C8)\</item\> where cell C8 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>=1/0\</item\> returns TRUE, because 1/0 is an error.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id8456984				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISERR(C9)\</item\> where cell C9 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>=NA()\</item\> returns FALSE, because ISERR() ignores the #N/A error.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147081				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>ISERROR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recognizing;general errors\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
