helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147372	14			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3157996	15			0	uk	NOT(LogicalValue)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148766	16			0	uk	            \<emph\>LogicalValue\</emph\> is any value to be complemented.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149884	17			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150132	18			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=NOT(A)\</item\>. If A=TRUE then NOT(A) will evaluate FALSE.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148394				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>OR function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148394	20			0	uk	OR				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060	61			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ODER\"\>Returns TRUE if at least one argument is TRUE.\</ahelp\> This function returns the value FALSE, if all the arguments have the logical value FALSE.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771	62			0	uk	The arguments are either logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3) containing logical values.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153546	63			0	uk	When a function expects a single value, but you entered a cell range, then the value from the cell range is taken that is in the same column or row as the formula.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149027	64			0	uk	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155517	22			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150468	23			0	uk	OR(LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155819	24			0	uk	            \<emph\>LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30\</emph\> are conditions to be checked. All conditions can be either TRUE or FALSE. If a range is entered as a parameter, the function uses the value from the range that is in the current column or row.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153228	25			0	uk	Examples:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154870	26			0	uk	The logical values of entries 12<11; 13>22, and 45=45 are to be checked.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155371	27			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OR(12<11;13>22;45=45)\</item\> returns TRUE.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3158412	59			0	uk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OR(FALSE;TRUE)\</item\> returns TRUE.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148394K				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>XOR function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
