helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060K				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ODER\"\>Returns the exclusive "or" of arguments.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771K	62			0	uk	The arguments are either numbers, logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149027K				0	uk	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155517K	22			0	uk	Syntax				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150468K				0	uk	XOR(Value1; Value2 ...Value30)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155819K	24			0	uk	\<emph\>Value1; Value2 ...Value30\</emph\> are added modulo 2. TRUE is returned if the result of this addition is 1;FALSE is returned if the result of this addition is 0.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153228K				0	uk	Examples:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155371K				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=XOR(12<11;13>22;10)\</item\> returns TRUE since this converts to (1+0+10) mod 2 = 0				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3158412K				0	uk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=XOR(FALSE;TRUE)\</item\> returns TRUE.				20220827 09:49:47
