helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10929				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Remove\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10953				0	uk	Using the Page Break Preview to Edit Print Ranges				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093E				0	uk	In the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, print ranges as well as page break regions are outlined by a blue border and contain a centered page number in gray. Nonprinting areas have a gray background.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143	8			0	uk	To define a new page break region, drag the border to a new location. When you define a new page break region, an automatic page break is replaced by a manual page break.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10930				0	uk	To View and Edit Print Ranges				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10937				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082A				0	uk	To change the default zoom factor of the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, double click the percentage value on the \<emph\>Status\</emph\> bar, and select a new zoom factor.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10836				0	uk	Edit the print range.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10944				0	uk	To change the size of a print range, drag a border of the range to a new location.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075	12			0	uk	To delete a manual page break that is contained in a print range, drag the border of the page break outside of the print range.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10948				0	uk	To clear a print range, drag a border of the range onto the opposite border of the range.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	uk	To exit the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
