helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Calculating With Formulas				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>formulas;calculating with\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; with formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;formula calculation\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411	20			0	uk	\<variable id=\"formulas\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formulas.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Formulas\"\>Calculating With Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281	21			0	uk	All formulas begin with an equals sign. The formulas can contain numbers, text, arithmetic operators, logic operators, or functions.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272	39			0	uk	Remember that the basic arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /) can be used in formulas using the "Multiplication and Division before Addition and Subtraction" rule. Instead of writing =SUM(A1:B1) you can write =A1+B1.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119	42			0	uk	Parentheses can also be used. The result of the formula =(1+2)*3 produces a different result than =1+2*3.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156285	23			0	uk	Here are a few examples of $[officename] Calc formulas:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015	24			0	uk	=A1+10				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972	25			0	uk	Displays the contents of cell A1 plus 10.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643	45			0	uk	=A1*16%				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255	46			0	uk	Displays 16% of the contents of A1.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146917	47			0	uk	=A1 * A2				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146315	48			0	uk	Displays the result of the multiplication of A1 and A2.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022	26			0	uk	=ROUND(A1;1)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363	27			0	uk	Displays the contents of cell A1 rounded to one decimal place.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150209	28			0	uk	=EFFECTIVE(5%;12)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883	29			0	uk	Calculates the effective interest for 5% annual nominal interest with 12 payments a year.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114	33			0	uk	=B8-SUM(B10:B14)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486	34			0	uk	Calculates B8 minus the sum of the cells B10 to B14.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152890	35			0	uk	=SUM(B8;SUM(B10:B14))				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171	36			0	uk	Calculates the sum of cells B10 to B14 and adds the value to B8.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109	30			0	uk	It is also possible to nest functions in formulas, as shown in the example. You can also nest functions within functions. The Function Wizard assists you with nested functions.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213	44			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060100.xhp\" name=\"Functions list\"\>Functions list\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869	43			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"AutoPilot: Functions\"\>Function Wizard\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Inserting and Editing Comments				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153968				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>comments; on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>remarks on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>displaying; comments\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968	31			0	uk	\<variable id=\"note_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/note_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Comments\"\>Inserting and Editing Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440	32			0	uk	You can assign a comment to each cell by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Comment\</emph\>\</link\>. The comment is indicated by a small red square, the comment indicator, in the cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	34			0	uk	The comment is visible whenever the mouse pointer is over the cell, provided you have activated \<emph\>Help - Tips\</emph\> or - \<emph\>Extended Tips\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575	33			0	uk	When you select the cell, you can choose \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> from the context menu of the cell. Doing so keeps the comment visible until you deactivate the \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> command from the same context menu.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958	35			0	uk	To edit a permanently visible comment, just click in it. If you delete the entire text of the comment, the comment itself is deleted.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	uk	Move or resize each comment as you like.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	uk	Format each comment by specifying background color, transparency, border style, and text alignment. Choose the commands from the context menu of the comment.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764	38			0	uk	To show or hide the comment indicator, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and mark or unmark the \<emph\>Comment indicator\</emph\> check box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715	39			0	uk	To display a help tip for a selected cell, use \<emph\>Data - Validity - Input Help\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	36			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>Insert - Comment\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155686				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; moving cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; moving by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;moving by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;cells by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cells, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id986358				0	uk	\<variable id=\"move_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/move_dragdrop.xhp\"\>Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2760093				0	uk	When you drag-and-drop a selection of cells on a Calc sheet, the cells normally overwrite the existing cells in the area where you drop. This is the normal \<emph\>overwrite mode\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9527268				0	uk	When you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while releasing the mouse button, you enter the \<emph\>insert mode\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id79653				0	uk	In insert mode, the existing cells where you drop will be shifted to the right or to the bottom, and the dropped cells are inserted into the now empty positions without overwriting. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8676717				0	uk	The surrounding box of the moved cells looks different in insert mode. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3968932				0	uk	In overwrite mode you see all four borders around the selected area. In insert mode you see only the left border when target cells will be shifted to the right. You see only the upper border when target cells will be shifted down. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id7399517				0	uk	Whether the target area will be shifted to the right or to the bottom depends on the distance between source and target cells, if you move within the same sheet. It depends on the number of horizontal or vertical cells in the moved area, if you move to a different sheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8040406				0	uk	If you move cells in insert mode within the same row (only horizontally), then after insertion of the cells, all cells will be shifted to the left to fill the source area.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2586748				0	uk	In both modes, you can hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key, or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys while you release the mouse button to insert a copy or a link, respectively.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5814081				0	uk	Keys pressed while releasing the mouse button				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6581316				0	uk	Result				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9906613				0	uk	No key				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2815637				0	uk	Cells are moved and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells are emptied.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6161687				0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4278389				0	uk	Cells are copied and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2805566				0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5369121				0	uk	Links to the source cells are inserted and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9518723				0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	uk	Cells are moved and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells are emptied, except if you move within the same rows on the same sheet. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4021423				0	uk	If you move within the same rows on the same sheet, the cells in the target area shift to the right, and then the whole row shifts to fill the source area.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2783898				0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>keys				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2785119				0	uk	Cells are copied and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id584124				0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5590990				0	uk	Links to the source cells are inserted and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Rotating Text				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>cells; rotating text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rotating; text in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; writing vertically\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151112	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"text_rotate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_rotate.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Text\"\>Rotating Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171	2			0	uk	Select the cells whose text you want to rotate.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133	3			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854	4			0	uk	Click the \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> tab.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426	5			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Text orientation\</emph\> area use the mouse to select in the preview wheel the direction in which the text is to be rotated. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456	7			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells\"\>Format - Cells\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	8			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Alignment\"\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Using Scenarios				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149664				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>scenarios; creating/editing/deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;scenarios\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;scenarios in Navigator\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"scenario\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/scenario.xhp\" name=\"Using Scenarios\"\>Using Scenarios\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869	2			0	uk	A $[officename] Calc scenario is a set of cell values that can be used within your calculations. You assign a name to every scenario on your sheet. Define several scenarios on the same sheet, each with some different values in the cells. Then you can easily switch the sets of cell values by their name and immediately observe the results. Scenarios are a tool to test out "what-if" questions.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149255	15			0	uk	Creating Your Own Scenarios				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704	16			0	uk	To create a scenario, select all the cells that provide the data for the scenario. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020	17			0	uk	Select the cells that contain the values that will change between scenarios. To select multiple cells, hold down the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</item\>key as you click each cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150364	18			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Scenarios\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Create Scenario\</emph\> dialog appears.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426	19			0	uk	Enter a name for the new scenario and leave the other fields unchanged with their default values. Close the dialog with OK. Your new scenario is automatically activated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664	3			0	uk	Using Scenarios				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415	11			0	uk	Scenarios can be selected in the Navigator:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752	12			0	uk	Open the Navigator with the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id1593676\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_navigator.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1593676\"\>Navigator icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the Standard bar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	13			0	uk	Click the \<emph\>Scenarios\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id7617114\" src=\"sc/res/imglst/navipi/na07.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7617114\"\>Scenarios icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the Navigator.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256	14			0	uk	In the Navigator, you see the defined scenarios with the comments that were entered when the scenarios were created.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id1243629				0	uk	Double-click a scenario name in the Navigator to apply that scenario to the current sheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id9044770				0	uk	To delete a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3674123				0	uk	To edit a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3424481				0	uk	To hide the border of a set of cells that are part of a scenario, open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog for each scenario that affects the cells and clear the Display border checkbox. Hiding the border also removes the listbox on the sheet where you can choose the scenarios.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368	22			0	uk	If you want to know which values in the scenario affect other values, choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Trace Dependents\</emph\>. You see arrows to the cells that are directly dependent on the current cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484	29			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Creating Scenarios\"\>Creating Scenarios\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Applying Multiple Operations				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147559				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>multiple operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations;two variables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-classified tables\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559	5			0	uk	\<variable id=\"multioperation\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multioperation.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Operations\"\>Applying Multiple Operations\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171	1			0	uk	Multiple Operations in Columns or Rows				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id4123966				0	uk	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Multiple Operations\</item\> command provides a planning tool for "what if" questions. In your spreadsheet, you enter a formula to calculate a result from values that are stored in other cells. Then, you set up a cell range where you enter some fixed values, and the Multiple Operations command will calculate the results depending on the formula.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424	2			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the formula that applies to the data range. In the \<emph\>Column input cell/Row input cell\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the corresponding cell that is part of the formula. This can be explained best by examples:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153	7			0	uk	Examples				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189	8			0	uk	You produce toys which you sell for $10 each. Each toy costs $2 to make, in addition to which you have fixed costs of $10,000 per year. How much profit will you make in a year if you sell a particular number of toys?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id6478774				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id1621753\" src=\"res/helpimg/what-if.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1621753\"\>what-if sheet area\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145239	41			0	uk	Calculating With One Formula and One Variable				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146888	42			0	uk	To calculate the profit, first enter any number as the quantity (items sold) - in this example 2000. The profit is found from the formula Profit=Quantity * (Selling price - Direct costs) - Fixed costs. Enter this formula in B5.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875	43			0	uk	In column D enter given annual sales, one below the other; for example, 500 to 5000, in steps of 500.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3159115	44			0	uk	Select the range D2:E11, and thus the values in column D and the empty cells alongside in column E.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149723	45			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149149	46			0	uk	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas \</emph\>field, click cell B5.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355	47			0	uk	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the variable in the formula, which is replaced by the selected column values.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149009	48			0	uk	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You see the profits for the different quantities in column E.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148725	49			0	uk	Calculating with Several Formulas Simultaneously				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880	50			0	uk	Delete column E.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154675	51			0	uk	Enter the following formula in C5: = B5 / B4. You are now calculating the annual profit per item sold.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148885	52			0	uk	Select the range D2:F11, thus three columns.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474	53			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154846	54			0	uk	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, select cells B5 through C5.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931	55			0	uk	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3150862	56			0	uk	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will now see the profits in column E and the annual profit per item in column F.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139	3			0	uk	Multiple Operations Across Rows and Columns				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584	4			0	uk	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> allows you to carry out joint multiple operations for columns and rows in so-called cross-tables. The formula cell has to refer to both the data range arranged in rows and the one arranged in columns. Select the range defined by both data ranges and call the multiple operation dialog. Enter the reference to the formula in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field. The \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> and the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> fields are used to enter the reference to the corresponding cells of the formula.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149949	57			0	uk	Calculating with Two Variables				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154808	58			0	uk	Consider columns A and B of the sample table above. You now want to vary not just the quantity produced annually, but also the selling price, and you are interested in the profit in each case.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149731	59			0	uk	Expand the table shown above. D2 through D11 contain the numbers 500, 1000 and so on, up to 5000. In E1 through H1 enter the numbers 8, 10, 15 and 20.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3152810	95			0	uk	Select the range D1:H11.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153620	96			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981	97			0	uk	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, click cell B5.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113	98			0	uk	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B1. This means that B1, the selling price, is the horizontally entered variable (with the values 8, 10, 15 and 20).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154049	99			0	uk	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click in B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the vertically entered variable.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149141	100			0	uk	Close the dialog with OK. You see the profits for the different selling prices in the range E2:H11.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155104	101			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12060000.xhp\" name=\"Multiple operations\"\>Multiple operations\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
