helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427	7			0	uk	The \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function inserts a combo box on one or more data columns that lets you select the records (rows) to be displayed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576	9			0	uk	Select the columns you want to use AutoFilter on.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157	10			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>. The combo box arrows are visible in the first row of the range selected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	11			0	uk	Run the filter by clicking the drop-down arrow in the column heading and choosing an item.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064	13			0	uk	Only those rows whose contents meet the filter criteria are displayed. The other rows are filtered. You can see if rows have been filtered from the discontinuous row numbers. The column that has been used for the filter is identified by a different color for the arrow button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id9216589				0	uk	When you apply an additional AutoFilter on another column of a filtered data range, then the other combo boxes list only the filtered data.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	12			0	uk	To display all records again, select the "all\<emph\>"\</emph\> entry in the AutoFilter combo box. If you choose "Standard\<emph\>"\</emph\>, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Standard Filter\</item\> dialog appears, allowing you to set up a standard filter. Choose "Top 10" to display the highest 10 values only. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340	19			0	uk	To stop using AutoFilter, reselect all cells selected in step 1 and once again choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id4303415				0	uk	To assign different AutoFilters to different sheets, you must first define a database range on each sheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236	14			0	uk	The arithmetic functions also take account of the cells that are not visible due to an applied filter. For example, a sum of an entire column will also total the values in the filtered cells. Apply the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\> function if only the cells visible after the application of a filter are to be taken into account.				20220827 09:49:47
