helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Deactivating Automatic Changes\"\>Deactivating Automatic Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442	2			0	uk	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. You can immediately undo any automatic changes with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273	3			0	uk	The following shows you how to deactivate and reactivate the automatic changes in $[officename] Calc:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748	4			0	uk	Automatic Text or Number Completion				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730	5			0	uk	When making an entry in a cell, $[officename] Calc automatically suggests matching input found in the same column. This function is known as \<emph\>AutoInput\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878	6			0	uk	To turn the AutoInput on and off, set or remove the check mark in front of \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</emph\>\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146972	21			0	uk	Automatic Conversion to Date Format				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	22			0	uk	$[officename] Calc automatically converts certain entries to dates. For example, the entry \<emph\>1.1\</emph\> may be interpreted as January 1 of the current year, according to the locale settings of your operating system, and then displayed according to the date format applied to the cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267	23			0	uk	To ensure that an entry is interpreted as text, add an apostrophe at the beginning of the entry. The apostrophe is not displayed in the cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043	7			0	uk	Quotation Marks Replaced by Custom Quotes				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333	9			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Localized Options\</emph\> tab and unmark \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565	11			0	uk	Cell Content Always Begins With Uppercase				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001	13			0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab. Unmark \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Capitalize first letter of every sentence\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
