helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Protecting Cells from Changes				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>protecting;cells and sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell protection; enabling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; hiding for printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; sheet protection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas;hiding\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119	5			0	uk	\<variable id=\"cell_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Cells from Changes\"\>Protecting Cells from Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368	17			0	uk	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can protect sheets and the document as a whole. You can choose whether the cells are protected against accidental changes, whether the formulas can be viewed from within Calc, whether the cells are visible or whether the cells can be printed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145261	18			0	uk	Protection can be provided by means of a password, but it does not have to be. If you have assigned a password, protection can only be removed once the correct password has been entered.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576	19			0	uk	Note that the cell protection for cells with the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute is only effective when you protect the whole sheet. In the default condition, every cell has the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute. Therefore you must remove the attribute selectively for those cells where the user may make changes. You then protect the whole sheet and save the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	uk	These protection features are just switches to prevent accidental action. The features are not intended to provide any secure protection. For example, by exporting a sheet to another file format, a user may be able to surpass the protection features. There is only one secure protection: the password that you can apply when saving an OpenDocument file. A file that has been saved with a password can be opened only with the same password.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	uk	Select the cells that you want to specify the cell protection options for.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149019	7			0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> and click the \<emph\>Cell Protection\</emph\> tab.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985	9			0	uk	Select the protection options that you want. All options will be applied only after you protect the sheet from the Tools menu - see below.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id31529866655				0	uk	Uncheck \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to allow the user to change the currently selected cells.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152898	10			0	uk	Select \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to prevent changes to the contents and the format of a cell. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069A				0	uk	Select \<emph\>Hide formula\</emph\> to hide and to protect formulas from changes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A1				0	uk	Select \<emph\>Hide when printing\</emph\> to hide protected cells in the printed document. The cells are not hidden onscreen.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152872	11			0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362	12			0	uk	Apply the protection options.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	uk	To protect the cells from being changed / viewed / printed according to your settings in the \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> dialog, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C7				0	uk	To protect the structure of the document, for example the count, \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\"\>names\</link\>, and order of the sheets, from being changed, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CF				0	uk	(Optional) Enter a password.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	uk	If you forget your password, you cannot deactivate the protection. If you only want to protect cells from accidental changes, set the sheet protection, but do not enter a password.				20220827 09:49:47
