helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>csv files;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; importing/exporting as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exporting;formulas as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;csv files with formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"csv_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_formula.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Text Files\"\>Importing and Exporting CSV Text Files with Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402	2			0	uk	Comma separated values (CSV) files are text files that contain the cell contents of a single sheet. Commas, semicolons, or other characters can be used as the field delimiters between the cells. Text strings are put in quotation marks, numbers are written without quotation marks.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715	15			0	uk	To Import a CSV File				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709	16			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445	17			0	uk	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> field, select the format "Text CSV". Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When a file has the .csv extension, the file type is automatically recognized.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565	18			0	uk	You will see the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255	19			0	uk	If the csv file contains formulas, but you want to import the results of those formulas, then choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022	3			0	uk	To Export Formulas and Values as CSV Files				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342	4			0	uk	Click the sheet to be written as a csv file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423	5			0	uk	If you want to export the formulas as formulas, for example, in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111	6			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150200	7			0	uk	Under \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484	8			0	uk	If you want to export the calculation results instead of the formulas, do not mark \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148702	9			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912	10			0	uk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> field select the format "Text CSV".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978	13			0	uk	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869	23			0	uk	From the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialog that appears, select the character set and the field and text delimiters for the data to be exported, and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781	12			0	uk	If the numbers use commas as decimal separators or thousands separators, do not select the comma as the field delimiter. If the text contains double quotation marks, you must select the single quotation mark as separator.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150050	14			0	uk	If necessary, after you have saved, clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box to see the calculated results in the table again.				20220827 09:49:47
