helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120	15			0	uk	You can use the keyboard in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Outline\"\>Outline\</link\>:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394	16			0	uk	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F6\</item\> until the vertical or horizontal outline window has the focus.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379	17			0	uk	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons from top to bottom or from left to right.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	18			0	uk	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons in the opposite direction.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149403	19			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+1 to Command+8\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+8\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - show all levels up to the specified number; hide all higher levels.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329	20			0	uk	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>+\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>-\</item\> to show or hide the focused outline group.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	21			0	uk	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to activate the focused button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253	22			0	uk	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\>, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow to cycle through all buttons in the current level.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147343	8			0	uk	Selecting a Drawing Object or a Graphic				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AA				0	uk	Choose View - Toolbars - Drawing to open the Drawing toolbar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333	7			0	uk	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> until the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar is selected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345	4			0	uk	If the selection tool is active, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. This selects the first drawing object or graphic in the sheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159240	3			0	uk	With \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 you set the focus to the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379	2			0	uk	Now you can use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to select the next drawing object or graphic and \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to select the previous one.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Pivot Table				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150448				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; introduction\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot, see pivot table function\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150448	7			0	uk	\<variable id=\"datapilot\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot.xhp\" name=\"Pivot Table\"\>Pivot Table\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024	2			0	uk	The \<emph\>pivot table\</emph\> (formerly known as \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\>) allows you to combine, compare, and analyze large amounts of data. You can view different summaries of the source data, you can display the details of areas of interest, and you can create reports.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069	9			0	uk	A table that has been created as a \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090000.xhp\" name=\"pivot table\"\>pivot table\</link\> is an interactive table. Data can be arranged, rearranged or summarized according to different points of view.				20220827 09:49:47
