helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"row_height\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/row_height.xhp\" name=\"Changing Row Height or Column Width\"\>Changing Row Height or Column Width\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017	2			0	uk	You can change the height of the rows with the mouse or through the dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702	3			0	uk	What is described here for rows and row height applies accordingly for columns and column width.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963	4			0	uk	Using the mouse to change the row height or column width				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020	5			0	uk	Click the area of the headers on the separator below the current row, keep the mouse button pressed and drag up or down in order to change the row height.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3159237	6			0	uk	Select the optimal row height by double-clicking the separator below the row.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154659	7			0	uk	Using the dialog to change the row height or column width				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150367	8			0	uk	Click the row so that you achieve the focus.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3166432	9			0	uk	Start the context menu on the header at the left-hand side.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519	10			0	uk	You will see the commands \<emph\>Row Height\</emph\> and \<emph\>Optimal row height\</emph\>. Choosing either opens a dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487	11			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340100.xhp\" name=\"Row height\"\>Row height\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3149408	12			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Optimal row height\"\>Optimal row height\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	13			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340200.xhp\" name=\"Column width\"\>Column width\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815	14			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Optimal column width\"\>Optimal column width\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Applying Multiple Sheets				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154759				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; selecting multiple\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>appending sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154759	9			0	uk	\<variable id=\"multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multitables.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Sheets\"\>Applying Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576	10			0	uk	Inserting a Sheet				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731	4			0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Sheet\</item\> to insert a new sheet or an existing sheet from another file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203598				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog box where you can assign macros to sheet events.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203523				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a window where you can assign a color to the sheet tab.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id050920091402035				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to select all sheets in the document.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914020391				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to deselect all sheets in the document, except the current sheet.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491	11			0	uk	Selecting Multiple Sheets				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251	6			0	uk	The sheet tab of the current sheet is always visible in white in front of the other sheet tabs. The other sheet tabs are gray when they are not selected. By clicking other sheet tabs while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>you can select multiple sheets.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	uk	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600	12			0	uk	Undoing a Selection				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	13			0	uk	To undo the selection of a sheet, click its sheet tab again while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. The sheet that is currently visible cannot be removed from the selection.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382	15			0	uk	Calculating Across Multiple Sheets				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333	16			0	uk	You can refer to a range of sheets in a formula by specifying the first and last sheet of the range, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.A1) \</item\>sums up all A1 cells on Sheet1 through Sheet3.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Finding and Replacing in Calc				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id3769341				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding;formulas/values/text/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;multiple cell texts\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149204				0	uk	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Calc\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9363689				0	uk	In spreadsheet documents you can find words, formulas, and styles. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all matching cells at once, then apply another format or replace the cell content by other content.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3610644				0	uk	The Find & Replace dialog				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	uk	Cells can contain text or numbers that were entered directly as in a text document. But cells can also contain text or numbers as the result of a calculation. For example, if a cell contains the formula =1+2 it displays the result 3. You must decide whether to search for the 1 respective 2, or to search the 3.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2423780				0	uk	To find formulas or values				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	uk	You can specify in the Find & Replace dialog either to find the parts of a formula or the results of a calculation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	uk	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	uk	Select "Formulas" or "Values" in the \<emph\>Search in\</emph\> list box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	uk	With "Formulas" you will find all parts of the formulas. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	uk	With "Values" you will find the results of the calculations. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	uk	Cell contents can be formatted in different ways. For example, a number can be formatted as a currency, to be displayed with a currency symbol. You see the currency symbol in the cell, but you cannot search for it.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id7359233				0	uk	Finding text				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	uk	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	uk	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	uk	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Calc will select the next cell that contains your text. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found cell. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	uk	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F) to find the next cell without opening the dialog. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	uk	By default, Calc searches the current sheet. Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\>, then enable \<emph\>Search in all sheets\</emph\> to search through all sheets of the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	uk	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Calc selects all cells that contain your entry. Now you can for example set all found cells to bold, or apply a Cell Style to all at once.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8531449				0	uk	The Navigator				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>View - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	uk	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	uk	Use the Navigator for inserting objects and links within the same document or from other open documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Printing Sheets in Landscape Format				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing in landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing; landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape printing\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"print_landscape\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_landscape.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\"\>Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257	2			0	uk	In order to print a sheet you have a number of interactive options available under \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>. Drag the delimiter lines to define the range of printed cells on each page.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963	15			0	uk	To print in landscape format, proceed as follows:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020	3			0	uk	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786	4			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089	5			0	uk	The command is not visible if the sheet has been opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430	6			0	uk	Select the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab. Select the \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\> paper format and click OK.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150885	7			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288	8			0	uk	Depending on the printer driver and the operating system, it may be necessary to click the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button and to change your printer to landscape format there.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404	9			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>dialog in the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page, select the contents to be printed:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	10			0	uk	               \<emph\>All sheets\</emph\> - All sheets will be printed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148871	12			0	uk	               \<emph\>Selected sheets\</emph\> - Only the selected sheets will be printed. All sheets whose names (at the bottom on the sheet tabs) are selected will be printed. By pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while clicking a sheet name you can change this selection.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3764763				0	uk	               \<emph\>Selected cells\</emph\> - All selected cells are printed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id5538804				0	uk	From all the paper pages that result from the above selection, you can select the range of paper pages to be printed:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id14343				0	uk	               \<emph\>All pages\</emph\> - Print all resulting pages.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699	11			0	uk	               \<emph\>Pages\</emph\> - Enter the pages to be printed. The pages will also be numbered from the first sheet onwards. If you see in the Page Break Preview that Sheet1 will be printed on 4 pages and you want to print the first two pages of Sheet2, enter 5-6 here.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3145076	13			0	uk	If under \<emph\>Format - Print ranges\</emph\> you have defined one or more print ranges, only the contents of these print ranges will be printed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019	14			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
