helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id8049867				0	uk	You can select adjacent cells, then merge them into a single cell. Conversely, you can take a large cell that has been created by merging single cells, and divide it back into individual cells.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200913480176				0	uk	When you copy cells into a target range containing merged cells, the target range gets unmerged first, then the copied cells are pasted in. If the copied cells are merged cells, they retain their merge state.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id235602				0	uk	Merging Cells				20220827 09:49:47
