helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441	15			0	uk	\<variable id=\"cellreferences_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences_url.xhp\" name=\"Referencing URLs\"\>Referencing URLs\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id1955626				0	uk	For example, if you found an Internet page containing current stock exchange information in spreadsheet cells, you can load this page in $[officename] Calc by using the following procedure:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993	39			0	uk	In a $[officename] Calc document, position the cursor in the cell into which you want to insert the external data.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384	40			0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Link to External Data\</item\>. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External Data\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152892	41			0	uk	Enter the URL of the document or Web page in the dialog. The URL must be in the format: http://www.my-bank.com/table.html. The URL for local or local area network files is the path seen in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068	42			0	uk	$[officename] loads the Web page or file in the "background", that is, without displaying it. In the large list box of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\> dialog, you can see the name of all the sheets or named ranges you can choose from.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914	43			0	uk	Select one or more sheets or named ranges. You can also activate the automatic update function every "n" seconds and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979	44			0	uk	The contents will be inserted as a link in the $[officename] Calc document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768	30			0	uk	Save your spreadsheet. When you open it again later, $[officename] Calc will update the linked cells following an inquiry.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204	38			0	uk	Under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - General\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</item\>\</link\> you can choose to have the update, when opened, automatically carried out either always, upon request or never. The update can be started manually in the dialog under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Links\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Applying Filters				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153896				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>filters; applying/removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows;removing/redisplaying with filters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;filters\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896	70			0	uk	\<variable id=\"filters\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp\" name=\"Applying Filters\"\>Applying Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869	2			0	uk	Filters and advanced filters allow you to work on certain filtered rows (records) of a data range. In the spreadsheets in $[officename] there are various possibilities for applying filters.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131	3			0	uk	One use for the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function is to quickly restrict the display to records with identical entries in a data field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119	4			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog, you can also define ranges which contain the values in particular data fields. You can use the standard filter to connect the conditions with either a logical AND or a logical OR operator.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010	5			0	uk	The \<emph\>Advanced filter\</emph\> allows up to a total of eight filter conditions. With advanced filters you enter the conditions directly into the sheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id9384746				0	uk	To remove a filter, so that you see all cells again, click inside the area where the filter was applied, then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	uk	When you select multiple rows from an area where a filter was applied, then this selection can include rows that are visible and rows that are hidden by the filter. If you then apply formatting, or delete the selected rows, this action then applies only to the visible rows. The hidden rows are not affected. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id218817				0	uk	This is the opposite to rows that you have hidden manually by the \<emph\>Format - Rows - Hide Rows\</emph\> command. Manually hidden rows are deleted when you delete a selection that contains them.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Calculating With Dates and Times				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146120				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>dates; in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>times; in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;date and time formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>current date and time values\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146120	11			0	uk	\<variable id=\"calc_date\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_date.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Dates and Times\"\>Calculating With Dates and Times\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320	12			0	uk	In $[officename] Calc, you can perform calculations with current date and time values. As an example, to find out exactly how old you are in seconds or hours, follow the following steps:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150750	13			0	uk	In a spreadsheet, enter your birthday in cell A1.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3145642	14			0	uk	Enter the following formula in cell A3: \<item type=\"literal\"\>=NOW()-A1\</item\>            				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3149020	52			0	uk	After pressing the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key you will see the result in date format. Since the result should show the difference between two dates as a number of days, you must format cell A3 as a number.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	53			0	uk	Place the cursor in cell A3, right-click to open a context menu and choose \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343	54			0	uk	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format Cells\</item\> dialog appears. On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> tab, the "Number" category will appear already highlighted. The format is set to "General", which causes the result of a calculation containing date entries to be displayed as a date. To display the result as a number, set the number format to "-1,234" and close the dialog with the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\> button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001	15			0	uk	The number of days between today's date and the specified date is displayed in cell A3.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304	16			0	uk	Experiment with some additional formulas: in A4 enter =A3*24 to calculate the hours, in A5 enter =A4*60 for the minutes, and in A6 enter =A5*60 for seconds. Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key after each formula.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3149207	17			0	uk	The time since your date of birth will be calculated and displayed in the various units. The values are calculated as of the exact moment when you entered the last formula and pressed the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key. This value is not automatically updated, although "Now" continuously changes. In the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> menu, the menu item \<emph\>Cell Contents - AutoCalculate\</emph\> is normally active; however, automatic calculation does not apply to the function NOW. This ensures that your computer is not solely occupied with updating the sheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Filter: Applying Advanced Filters				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148798				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>filters;defining advanced filters \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148798	18			0	uk	\<variable id=\"specialfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/specialfilter.xhp\" name=\"Filter: Applying Advanced Filters\"\>Filter: Applying Advanced Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785	19			0	uk	Copy the column headers of the sheet ranges to be filtered into an empty area of the sheet, and then enter the criteria for the filter in a row beneath the headers. Horizontally arranged data in a row will always be logically connected with AND, and vertically arranged data in a column will always be logically connected with OR.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142	20			0	uk	Once you have created a filter matrix, select the sheet ranges to be filtered. Open the \<emph\>Advanced Filter\</emph\> dialog by choosing \<emph\>Data - Filter - Advanced Filter\</emph\>, and define the filter conditions.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	21			0	uk	Then click OK, and you will see that only the rows from the original sheet whose contents have met the search criteria are still visible. All other rows are temporarily hidden and can be made to reappear with the \<emph\>Format - Row - Show \</emph\>command.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	22			0	uk	 \<emph\>Example\</emph\> 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427	23			0	uk	Load a spreadsheet with a large number of records. We are using a fictional \<emph\>Turnover\</emph\> document, but you can just as easily use any other document. The document has the following layout:				20220827 09:49:47
