helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155957	66			0	uk	<160000				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153566	67			0	uk	Specify that only rows which either have the value \<item type=\"literal\"\>January\</item\> in the \<emph\>Month\</emph\> cells OR a value of under 160000 in the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> cells will be displayed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147372	68			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - Advanced Filter\</emph\>, and then select the range A20:E22. After you click OK, only the filtered rows will be displayed. The other rows will be hidden from view.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	19xx/20xx Years				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150439				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>years; 2-digits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dates; 19xx/20xx\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439	18			0	uk	\<variable id=\"year2000\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/year2000.xhp\" name=\"19xx/20xx Years\"\>19xx/20xx Years\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116	17			0	uk	The year in a date entry is often entered as two digits. Internally, the year is managed by $[officename] as four digits, so that in the calculation of the difference from 1/1/99 to 1/1/01, the result will correctly be two years.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011	19			0	uk	Under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\> you can define the century that is used when you enter a year with only two digits. The default is 1930 to 2029.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010	20			0	uk	This means that if you enter a date of 1/1/30 or higher, it will be treated internally as 1/1/1930 or higher. All lower two-digit years apply to the 20xx century. So, for example, 1/1/20 is converted into 1/1/2020.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Selecting Themes for Sheets				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>theme selection for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layout;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	6			0	uk	\<variable id=\"design\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/design.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Themes for Sheets\"\>Selecting Themes for Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	13			0	uk	$[officename] Calc comes with a predefined set of formatting themes that you can apply to your spreadsheets.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	16			0	uk	It is not possible to add themes to Calc, and they cannot be modified. However, you can modify their styles after you apply them to a spreadsheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757	17			0	uk	Before you format a sheet with a theme, you have to apply at least one custom cell style to the cells on the sheet. You can then change the cell formatting by selecting and applying a theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	18			0	uk	To apply a custom cell style to a cell, you can open the Styles and Formatting window and, in its lower list box, set the Custom Styles view. A list of the existing custom defined cell styles will be displayed. Double click a name from the Styles and Formatting window to apply this style to the selected cells.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963	19			0	uk	To apply a theme to a spreadsheet:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	15			0	uk	Click the \<emph\>Choose Themes\</emph\> icon in the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> bar. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488	20			0	uk	The \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog appears. This dialog lists the available themes for the whole spreadsheet and the Styles and Formatting window lists the custom styles for specific cells.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	9			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Theme Selection \</emph\>dialog, select the theme that you want to apply to the spreadsheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090	21			0	uk	Click OK				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150201	22			0	uk	As soon as you select another theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog, some of the properties of the custom style will be applied to the current spreadsheet. The modifications will be immediately visible in your spreadsheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146979	12			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/02/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Theme selection\"\>Theme selection\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Referencing a Cell in Another Document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>sheet references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; to cells in other sheets/documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; operating in another document\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents;references\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436	9			0	uk	\<variable id=\"cellreferences\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Other Sheets\"\>Referencing Other Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9663075				0	uk	In a sheet cell you can show a reference to a cell in another sheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id1879329				0	uk	In the same way, a reference can also be made to a cell from another document provided that this document has already been saved as a file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id7122409				0	uk	To Reference a Cell in the Same Document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id2078005				0	uk	Open a new, empty spreadsheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id4943693				0	uk	By way of example, enter the following formula in cell A1 of Sheet1:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9064302				0	uk	               \<item type=\"literal\"\>=Sheet2.A1\</item\>            				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7609790				0	uk	Click the \<emph\>Sheet2\</emph\> tab at the bottom of the spreadsheet. Set the cursor in cell A1 there and enter text or a number.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id809961				0	uk	If you switch back to Sheet1, you will see the same content in cell A1 there. If the contents of Sheet2.A1 change, then the contents of Sheet1.A1 also change.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id9209570				0	uk	To Reference a Cell in Another Document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5949278				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>, to load an existing spreadsheet document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8001953				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, to open a new spreadsheet document. Set the cursor in the cell where you want to insert the external data and enter an equals sign to indicate that you want to begin a formula.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8571123				0	uk	Now switch to the document you have just loaded. Click the cell with the data that you want to insert in the new document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8261665				0	uk	Switch back to the new spreadsheet. In the input line you will now see how $[officename] Calc has added the reference to the formula for you. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5888241				0	uk	The reference to a cell of another document contains the name of the other document in single inverted commas, then a hash #, then the name of the sheet of the other document, followed by a point and the name of the cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7697683				0	uk	Confirm the formula by clicking the green check mark.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7099826				0	uk	If you drag the box in the lower right corner of the active cell to select a range of cells, $[officename] automatically inserts the corresponding references in the adjacent cells. As a result, the sheet name is preceded with a "$" sign to designate it as an absolute reference.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id674459				0	uk	If you examine the name of the other document in this formula, you will notice that it is written as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>. This means that you can also enter a URL from the Internet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Importing and Exporting dBASE Files 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id1226844				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;spreadsheets to dBASE\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dBASE import/export\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; importing from/exporting to dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;importing dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	uk	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBASE Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	uk	You can open and save data in the dBASE file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBASE database is a folder that contains files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBASE file from %PRODUCTNAME.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	uk	To Import a dBASE File Into a Spreadsheet				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	uk	Locate the *.dbf file that you want to import. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	uk	The \<emph\>Import dBASE files\</emph\> dialog opens.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	uk	The dBASE file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074E				0	uk	If you want to save the spreadsheet as a dBASE file, do not alter or delete the first row in the imported file. This row contains information that is required by a dBASE database.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	uk	To Import a dBASE File Into a Database Table				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	uk	A %PRODUCTNAME Base database table is actually a link to an existing database.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10796				0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - New - Database\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	uk	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialog, enter a name for the database.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10792				0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079A				0	uk	In the \<emph\>Database type \</emph\>box of the \<emph\>Database Properties\</emph\> dialog, select "dBASE".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AE				0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B6				0	uk	Locate the directory that contains the dBASE file, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F1				0	uk	To Save a Spreadsheet as a dBASE File				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10800				0	uk	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> box, select "dBASE file".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	uk	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, type a name for the dBASE file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10801				0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10808				0	uk	Only the data on the current sheet is exported.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Validity of Cell Contents				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156442				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>values; limiting on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>limits; specifying value limits on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>permitted cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error messages; defining for incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>actions in case of incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help tips; defining text for cell input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments;help text for cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining input help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>macros; running when incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; validity check\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442	22			0	uk	\<variable id=\"validity\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/validity.xhp\" name=\"Validity of Cell Contents\"\>Validity of Cell Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283	2			0	uk	For each cell, you can define entries to be valid. Invalid entries to a cell will be rejected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252	3			0	uk	The validity rule is activated when a new value is entered. If an invalid value has already been inserted into the cell, or if you insert a value in the cell either with drag-and-drop or by copying and pasting, the validity rule will not take effect.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id5174718				0	uk	You can choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective\</emph\> at any time and choose the command \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>\<emph\>Mark Invalid Data\</emph\>\</link\> to display which cells contain invalid values.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155603	5			0	uk	Using Cell Contents Validity				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959	6			0	uk	Select the cells for which you want to define a new validity rule.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837	8			0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Validity\</item\>. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156020	9			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> tab page, enter the conditions for new values entered into cells. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159208	10			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Allow\</emph\> field, select an option.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011	11			0	uk	If you select "Whole Numbers", values such as "12.5" are not allowed. Choosing "Date" allows date information both in the local date format as well as in the form of a \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"serial date\"\>serial date\</link\>. Similarly, the "Time" condition permits time values such as "12:00" or serial time numbers. "Text Length" stipulates that cells are allowed to contain text only.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id9224829				0	uk	Select "List" to enter a list of valid entries.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149317	13			0	uk	Select the next condition under \<emph\>Data\</emph\>. According to what you choose, additional options will be selectable.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389	15			0	uk	After you have determined the conditions for cell validity, you can use the other two tab pages to create message boxes:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159261	16			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Input Help\</emph\> tab page, enter the title and the text of the tip, which will then be displayed if the cell is selected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396	17			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page, select the action to be carried out in the event of an error.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3147416	18			0	uk	If you select "Stop" as the action, invalid entries are not accepted, and the previous cell contents are retained.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3150033	19			0	uk	Select "Warning" or "Information" to display a dialog in which the entry can either be canceled or accepted.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947	20			0	uk	If you select "Macro", then by using the \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> button you can specify a macro to be run in the event of an error.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149011	35			0	uk	To display the error message, select \<emph\>Show error message when invalid values are entered\</emph\>. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148586	21			0	uk	After changing the action for a cell on the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page and closing the dialog with OK, you must first select another cell before the change takes effect.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3154805	30			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Validity\"\>Data - Validity\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Naming Cells				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; defining for cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>values; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>constants definition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variables; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell ranges; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;names for cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>addressing; by defined names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell names; defining/addressing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; by defined names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>allowed cell names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>renaming;cells\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"value_with_name\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/value_with_name.xhp\" name=\"Naming Cells\"\>Naming Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id4391918				0	uk	Allowed names				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id2129581				0	uk	Names in Calc can contain letters, numeric characters, and some special characters. Names must start with a letter or an underline character.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id1120029				0	uk	Allowed special characters:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3362224				0	uk	underline (_) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4891506				0	uk	period (.) - allowed within a name, but not as first or last character				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id2816553				0	uk	blank ( ) - allowed within a name, but not as first or last character, and not for a cell range				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id328989				0	uk	Names must not be the same as cell references. For example, the name A1 is invalid because A1 is a cell reference to the top left cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id32898987				0	uk	Names must not start with the letter R followed by a number. See the ADDRESS function for more information.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4769737				0	uk	Names for cell ranges must not include blanks. Blanks are allowed within names for single cells, sheets and documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id1226233				0	uk	Naming cells and formulas				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id5489364				0	uk	A good way of making the references to cells and cell ranges in formulas legible is to give the ranges names. For example, you can name the range A1:B2 \<emph\>Start\</emph\>. You can then write a formula such as "=SUM(Start)". Even after you insert or delete rows or columns, $[officename] still correctly assigns the ranges identified by name. Range names must not contain any spaces.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id953398				0	uk	For example, it is much easier to read a formula for sales tax if you can write "= Amount * Tax_rate" instead of "= A5 * B12". In this case, you would name cell A5 "Amount" and cell B12 "Tax_rate."				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4889675				0	uk	Use the \<emph\>Define Names\</emph\> dialog to define names for formulas or parts of formulas you need more often. In order to specify range names,				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954	3			0	uk	Select a cell or range of cells, then choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Define Names\</emph\> dialog appears.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283	4			0	uk	Type the name of the selected area in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> field. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>. The newly defined name appears in the list below. Click OK to close the dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id5774101				0	uk	You can also name other cell ranges in this dialog by entering the name in the field and then selecting the respective cells.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942	5			0	uk	If you type the name in a formula, after the first few characters entered you will see the entire name as a tip.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	6			0	uk	Press the Enter key in order to accept the name from the tip.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749	7			0	uk	If more than one name starts with the same characters, you can scroll through all the names using the Tab key.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711	8			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04070100.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Names - Define\"\>Insert - Names - Define\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
