helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	5			0	uk	\<variable id=\"consolidate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/consolidate.xhp\" name=\"Consolidating Data\"\>Consolidating Data\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191	34			0	uk	During consolidation, the contents of the cells from several sheets will be combined in one place.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id892056				0	uk	To Combine Cell Contents				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	6			0	uk	Open the document that contains the cell ranges to be consolidated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154513	7			0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Consolidate\</item\> to open the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345	8			0	uk	From the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\> box select a source cell range to consolidate with other areas.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209	9			0	uk	If the range is not named, click in the field next to the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\>. A blinking text cursor appears. Type a reference for the first source data range or select the range with the mouse.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529	10			0	uk	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert the selected range in the \<emph\>Consolidation areas\</emph\> field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153816	11			0	uk	Select additional ranges and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> after each selection.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157983	12			0	uk	Specify where you want to display the result by selecting a target range from the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150215	13			0	uk	If the target range is not named, click in the field next to \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> and enter the reference of the target range. Alternatively, you can select the range using the mouse or position the cursor in the top left cell of the target range.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813	14			0	uk	Select a function from the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> box. The function specifies how the values of the consolidation ranges are linked. The "Sum" function is the default setting.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149315	15			0	uk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to consolidate the ranges.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	uk	Additional Settings				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147250	16			0	uk	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog to display additional settings:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156400	17			0	uk	Select \<emph\>Link to source data\</emph\> to insert the formulas that generate the results in the target range, rather than the actual results. If you link the data, any values modified in the source range are automatically updated in the target range.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538	18			0	uk	The corresponding cell references in the target range are inserted in consecutive rows, which are automatically ordered and then hidden from view. Only the final result, based on the selected function, is displayed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149945	19			0	uk	Under \<emph\>Consolidate by\</emph\>, select either \<emph\>Row labels\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column labels\</emph\> if the cells of the source data range are not to be consolidated corresponding to the identical position of the cell in the range, but instead according to a matching row label or column label.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871	20			0	uk	To consolidate by row labels or column labels, the label must be contained in the selected source ranges.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150478	21			0	uk	The text in the labels must be identical, so that rows or columns can be accurately matched. If the row or column label does not match any that exist in the target range, it will be appended as a new row or column.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147468	22			0	uk	The data from the consolidation ranges and target range will be saved when you save the document. If you later open a document in which consolidation has been defined, this data will again be available.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153039	33			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Consolidate\"\>Data - Consolidate\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Cells in Currency Format				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156329				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>currency formats; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>international currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; currency formats in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies; default currencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329	46			0	uk	\<variable id=\"currency_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/currency_format.xhp\" name=\"Cells in Currency Format\"\>Cells in Currency Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968	47			0	uk	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can give numbers any currency format. When you click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Currency\</item\> icon\<image id=\"img_id3150791\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_currencyfield.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150791\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar to format a number, the cell is given the default currency format set under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010	48			0	uk	Exchanging of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc documents can lead to misunderstandings, if your \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc document is loaded by a user who uses a different default currency format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442	52			0	uk	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can define that a number that you have formatted as "1,234.50 €", still remains in euros in another country and does not become dollars.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075	49			0	uk	You can change the currency format in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format Cells\</item\> dialog (choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</item\> tab) by two country settings. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\> combo box select the basic setting for decimal and thousands separators. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box you can select the currency symbol and its position.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749	50			0	uk	For example, if the language is set to "Default" and you are using a German locale setting, the currency format will be "1.234,00 €". A point is used before the thousand digits and a comma before the decimal places. If you now select the subordinate currency format "$ English (US)" from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box, you will get the following format: "$ 1.234,00". As you can see, the separators have remained the same. Only the currency symbol has been changed and converted, but the underlying format of the notation remains the same as in the locale setting.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640	51			0	uk	If, under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\>, you convert the cells to "English (US)", the English-language locale setting is also transferred and the default currency format is now "$ 1,234.00".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255	53			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Formatting Numbers With Decimals				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145367				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;formatting decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults; number formats in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places;formatting numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers with decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;adding/deleting decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; adding/deleting decimal places in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places; adding/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367	4			0	uk	\<variable id=\"format_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers With Decimals\"\>Formatting Numbers With Decimals\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576	5			0	uk	Enter a number into the sheet, for example, 1234.5678. This number will be displayed in the default number format, with two decimal places. You will see 1234.57 when you confirm the entry. Only the display in the document will be rounded off; internally, the number retains all four decimal places after the decimal point.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012	12			0	uk	To format numbers with decimals:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394	6			0	uk	Set the cursor at the number and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> to start the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157	9			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab you will see a selection of predefined number formats. In the bottom right in the dialog you will see a preview of how your current number would look if you were to give it a particular format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3149021\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_numberformatincdecimals.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149021\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3149256	10			0	uk	If you only want to modify the number of the decimal places displayed, the easiest method is to use the \<emph\>Number Format: Add Decimal Place\</emph\> or \<emph\>Number Format: Delete Decimal Place\</emph\> icons on the Formatting Bar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>HTML WebQuery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; inserting in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external data; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; inserting external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>web pages; importing data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebQuery filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources; external data\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"webquery\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/webquery.xhp\" name=\"Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\"\>Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131	3			0	uk	With the help of the \<emph\>Web Page Query ($[officename] Calc)\</emph\> import filter, you can insert tables from HTML documents in a Calc spreadsheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575	4			0	uk	You can use the same method to insert ranges defined by name from a Calc or Microsoft Excel spreadsheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	5			0	uk	The following insert methods are available:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146976	6			0	uk	Inserting by Dialog				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319	7			0	uk	Set the cell cursor at the cell where the new content will be inserted.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	8			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Link to External Data\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\"\>External Data\</link\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958	9			0	uk	Enter the URL of the HTML document or the name of the spreadsheet. Press Enter when finished. Click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open a file selection dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400	10			0	uk	In the large list box of the dialog, select the named ranges or tables you want to insert.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064	11			0	uk	You can also specify that the ranges or tables are updated every n seconds.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443	30			0	uk	The import filter can create names for cell ranges on the fly. As much formatting as possible is retained, while the filter intentionally does not load any images.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149021	12			0	uk	Inserting by Navigator				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965	14			0	uk	Open two documents: the $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in which the external data is to be inserted (target document) and the document from which the external data derives (source document).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205	16			0	uk	In the target document open the Navigator.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990	18			0	uk	In the lower combo box of the Navigator select the source document. The Navigator now shows the range names and database ranges or the tables contained in the source document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148842	20			0	uk	In the Navigator select the \<emph\>Insert as link\</emph\> drag mode \<image id=\"img_id3152985\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20238.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152985\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978	22			0	uk	Drag the desired external data from the Navigator into the target document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768	23			0	uk	If you have loaded an HTML document with the \<emph\>Web Page Query\</emph\> filter as the source document, you will find the tables in the Navigator, named continuously from "HTML_table1" onwards, and also two range names that have been created:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152873	24			0	uk	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_all\</item\> - designates the entire document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149897	25			0	uk	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_tables\</item\> - designates all HTML tables in the document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149126	26			0	uk	Editing the external data				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3159228	27			0	uk	Open \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\>. Here you can edit the link to the external data.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154650	28			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External data dialog\"\>External data dialog\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Creating Pivot Tables				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148491				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; calling up and applying\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148491	7			0	uk	\<variable id=\"datapilot_createtable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_createtable.xhp\" name=\"Creating Pivot Tables\"\>Creating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023	8			0	uk	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264	9			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Create\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Select Source\</emph\> dialog appears. Choose \<emph\>Current selection\</emph\> and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The table headings are shown as buttons in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. Drag these buttons as required and drop them into the layout areas "Page Fields", "Column Fields", "Row Fields" and "Data Fields".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	10			0	uk	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id7599414				0	uk	Drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the generated pivot table. The listbox can be used to filter the pivot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the generated pivot table to use another page field as a filter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011	11			0	uk	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	16			0	uk	By double-clicking on one of the fields in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area you can call up the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	17			0	uk	Use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Field\</item\> dialog to select the calculations to be used for the data. To make a multiple selection, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key while clicking the desired calculation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329	13			0	uk	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	14			0	uk	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338	15			0	uk	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialog to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020	18			0	uk	Exit the Pivot Table dialog by pressing OK. A \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button will now be inserted, or a page button for every data field that you dropped in the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area. The pivot table is inserted further down.				20220827 09:49:47
