helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153194				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; spreadsheet preview\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>previews;page breaks for printing\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153194	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"print_exact\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_exact.xhp\" name=\"Defining Number of Pages for Printing\"\>Defining Number of Pages for Printing\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771	2			0	uk	If a sheet is too large for a single printed page, $[officename] Calc will print the current sheet evenly divided over several pages. Since the automatic page break does not always take place in the optimal position, you can define the page distribution yourself.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155	3			0	uk	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012	4			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	5			0	uk	You will see the automatic distribution of the sheet across the print pages. The automatically created print ranges are indicated by dark blue lines, and the user-defined ones by light blue lines. The page breaks (line breaks and column breaks) are marked as black lines.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578	6			0	uk	You can move the blue lines with the mouse. You will find further options in the Context menu, including adding an additional print range, removing the scaling and inserting additional manual line and column breaks.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	7			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Unprotecting Cells				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153252				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>cell protection; unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protecting; unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153252	14			0	uk	\<variable id=\"cell_unprotect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_unprotect.xhp\" name=\"Unprotecting Cells\"\>Unprotecting Cells\</link\> \</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112	15			0	uk	Click the sheet for which you want to cancel the protection.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656	16			0	uk	Select \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, then choose \<emph\>Sheet\</emph\> or \<emph\>Document\</emph\> to remove the check mark indicating the protected status.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171	17			0	uk	If you have assigned a password, enter it in this dialog and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771	18			0	uk	The cells can now be edited, the formulas can be viewed, and all cells can be printed until you reactivate the protection for the sheet or document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Entering Formulas 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>formula bar; input line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input line in formula bar\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; inputting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868	9			0	uk	\<variable id=\"formula_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Formulas\"\>Entering Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6848353				0	uk	You can enter formulas in several ways: using the icons, or by typing on the keyboard, or by a mixture of both methods.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364	10			0	uk	Click the cell in which you want to enter the formula.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012	11			0	uk	Click the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> icon on the Formula Bar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441	12			0	uk	You will now see an equals sign in the input line and you can begin to input the formula.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	3			0	uk	After entering the required values, press Enter or click \<emph\>Accept\</emph\> to insert the result in the active cell. If you want to clear your entry in the input line, press Escape or click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394	8			0	uk	You can also enter the values and the formulas directly into the cells, even if you cannot see an input cursor. Formulas must always begin with an equals sign.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id4206976				0	uk	You can also press the + or - key on the numerical keyboard to start a formula. NumLock must be "on". For example, press the following keys in succession:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	uk	+ 5 0 - 8 Enter				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8171330				0	uk	You see the result \<item type=\"literal\"\>42\</item\> in the cell. The cell contains the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=+50-8\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	6			0	uk	If you are editing a formula with references, the references and the associated cells will be highlighted with the same color. You can now resize the reference border using the mouse, and the reference in the formula displayed in the input line also changes. \<emph\>Show references in color\</emph\> can be deactivated under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210	7			0	uk	\<variable id=\"tip\"\>If you would like to view the calculation of individual elements of a formula, select the respective elements and press F9. For example, in the formula =SUM(A1:B12)*SUM(C1:D12) select the section SUM(C1:D12) and press F9 to view the subtotal for this area. \</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304	5			0	uk	If an error occurs when creating the formula, an \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error message\"\>error message\</link\> appears in the active cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993	13			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Formula bar\"\>Formula bar\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Copying to Multiple Sheets				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>copying;values, to multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;values in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;inserting in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\> 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	3			0	uk	\<variable id=\"edit_multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/edit_multitables.xhp\" name=\"Copying to Multiple Sheets\"\>Copying to Multiple Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	6			0	uk	In $[officename] Calc, you can insert values, text or formulas that are simultaneously copied to other selected sheets of your document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768	8			0	uk	Select all desired sheets by holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key and clicking the corresponding register tabs that are still gray at the bottom margin of the workspace. All selected register tabs are now white.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	uk	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435	7			0	uk	Now when you insert values, text or formulas into the active sheet, they will also appear in the identical positions in the other selected sheets. For example, data entered in cell A1 of the active sheet is automatically entered into cell A1 of any other seleted sheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	User Defined Borders in Cells 				20220827 09:49:47
