helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5383465				0	uk	You cannot apply borders to multiple selections.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7790154				0	uk	Default Settings				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2918485				0	uk	Click one of the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icons to set or reset multiple borders.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	uk	The thin gray lines inside an icon show the borders that will be reset or cleared.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5212561				0	uk	The dark lines inside an icon show the lines that will be set using the selected line style and color.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4818872				0	uk	The thick gray lines inside an icon show the lines that will not be changed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id8989226				0	uk	Examples				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id622577				0	uk	Select a block of about 8x8 cells, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8119754				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id7261268\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_5.png\" width=\"1.0937in\" height=\"0.2189in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7261268\"\>default icon row of Borders tab page\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8964201				0	uk	Click the left icon to clear all lines. This removes all outer borders, all inner lines, and all diagonal lines.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6048463				0	uk	Click the second icon from the left to set an outer border and to remove all other lines.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1495406				0	uk	Click the rightmost icon to set an outer border. The inner lines are not changed, except the diagonal lines, which will be removed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9269386				0	uk	Now you can continue to see which lines the other icons will set or remove.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3593554				0	uk	User Defined Settings				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4018066				0	uk	In the \<emph\>User defined\</emph\> area, you can click to set or remove individual lines. The preview shows lines in three different states. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8004699				0	uk	Repeatedly click an edge or a corner to switch through the three different states.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8037659				0	uk	Line types				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2305978				0	uk	Image				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8716086				0	uk	Meaning				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3978087				0	uk	A black line				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4065065				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id9379863\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_7.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9379863\"\>solid line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6987823				0	uk	A black line sets the corresponding line of the selected cells. The line is shown as a dotted line when you choose the 0.05 pt line style. Double lines are shown when you select a double line style.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1209143				0	uk	A gray line				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6653340				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id6972563\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_gray.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6972563\"\>gray line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2278817				0	uk	A gray line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5374919				0	uk	A white line				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id52491				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3801080\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_white.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3801080\"\>white line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id372325				0	uk	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7282937				0	uk	Examples				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4230780				0	uk	Select a single cell, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1712393				0	uk	Click the lower edge to set a very thin line as a lower border. All other lines will be removed from the cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5149693				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id9467452\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_6.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9467452\"\>setting a thin lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5759453				0	uk	Choose a thicker line style and click the lower edge. This sets a thicker line as a lower border.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6342051				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id7431562\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_7.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7431562\"\>setting a thick line as a border\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5775322				0	uk	Click the second \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icon from the left to set all four borders. Then repeatedly click the lower edge until a white line is shown. This removes the lower border.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2882778				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id8155766.00000001\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_8.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8155766.00000001\"\>removing lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8102053				0	uk	You can combine several line types and styles. The last image shows how to set thick outer borders (the thick black lines), while any diagonal lines inside the cell will not be touched (gray lines).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2102420				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id5380718\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_9.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5380718\"\>advanced example for cell borders\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
