helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147560	67			0	uk	\<variable id=\"integer_leading_zero\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/integer_leading_zero.xhp\" name=\"Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\"\>Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194	55			0	uk	There are various ways to enter integers starting with a zero:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119	56			0	uk	Enter the number as text. The easiest way is to enter the number starting with an apostrophe (for example, \<item type=\"input\"\>'0987\</item\>). The apostrophe will not appear in the cell, and the number will be formatted as text. Because it is in text format, however, you cannot calculate with this number.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013	57			0	uk	Format a cell with a number format such as \<item type=\"input\"\>\\0000\</item\>. This format can be assigned in the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> field under the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab, and defines the cell display as "always put a zero first and then the integer, having at least three places, and filled with zeros at the left if less than three digits".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158	58			0	uk	If you want to apply a numerical format to a column of numbers in text format (for example, text "000123" becomes number "123"), do the following:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377	59			0	uk	Select the column in which the digits are found in text format. Set the cell format in that column as "Number".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	60			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>               				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	61			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>^[0-9]\</item\>               				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	62			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>&\</item\>               				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	63			0	uk	Check \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>               				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	64			0	uk	Check \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>               				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	65			0	uk	Click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>               				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Renaming Sheets				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150398				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>renaming;sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;renaming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;renaming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398	11			0	uk	\<variable id=\"rename_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\" name=\"Renaming Sheets\"\>Renaming Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131	12			0	uk	Click the name of the sheet that you want to change.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976	13			0	uk	Open the context menu and choose the \<emph\>Rename Sheet\</emph\> command. A dialog box appears where you can enter a new name.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	15			0	uk	Enter a new name for the sheet and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667	27			0	uk	Alternatively, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option key\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click on any sheet name and enter the new name directly.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502833				0	uk	Sheet names can contain almost any character. Some naming restrictions apply when you want to save the spreadsheet to Microsoft Excel format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050283				0	uk	When saving to Microsoft Excel format, the following characters are not allowed in sheet names:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050281				0	uk	colon :				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502897				0	uk	back slash \\				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050299				0	uk	forward slash /				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502913				0	uk	question mark ?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050298				0	uk	asterisk *				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502969				0	uk	left square bracket [				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502910				0	uk	right square bracket ]				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502971				0	uk	single quote ' as the first or last character of the name				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050307				0	uk	In cell references, a sheet name has to be enclosed in single quotes ' if the name contains other characters than alphanumeric or underscore. A single quote contained within a name has to be escaped by doubling it (two single quotes). For example, you want to reference the cell A1 on a sheet with the following name:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503071				0	uk	This year's sheet				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503054				0	uk	The reference must be enclosed in single quotes, and the one single quote inside the name must be doubled:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503069				0	uk	'This year''s sheet'.A1				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155444	16			0	uk	The name of a sheet is independent of the name of the spreadsheet. You enter the spreadsheet name when you save it for the first time as a file. The document can contain up to 256 individual sheets, which can have different names.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Formatting Bar				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200911433792				0	uk	\<link href=\"text/schart/main0202.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Bar\"\>Formatting Bar\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200911433835				0	uk	The Formatting Bar is shown when a chart is set to edit mode. Double-click a chart to enter edit mode. Click outside the chart to leave edit mode.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200911433878				0	uk	You can edit the formatting of a chart using the controls and icons on the Formatting Bar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300436				0	uk	Select Chart Element				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300479				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the element from the chart that you want to format. The element gets selected in the chart preview. Click Format Selection to open the properties dialog for the selected element.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300555				0	uk	Format Selection				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300539				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the properties dialog for the selected element.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300545				0	uk	Chart Type				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300594				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Chart Type dialog.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300537				0	uk	Chart Data Table				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300699				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Data Table dialog where you can edit the chart data.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300672				0	uk	Horizontal Grid On/Off				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300630				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Horizontal Grid On/Off icon on the Formatting bar toggles the visibility of the grid display for the Y axis.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300738				0	uk	Legend On/Off				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id081020090230076				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To show or hide a legend, click Legend On/Off on the Formatting bar.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id0810200902300785				0	uk	Scale Text				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300784				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Rescales the text in the chart when you change the size of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	hd_id081020090230087				0	uk	Automatic Layout				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0202.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902300834				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Moves all chart elements to their default positions inside the current chart. This function does not alter the chart type or any other attributes other than the position of elements.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	$[officename] Chart Features				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150543	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/schart/main0503.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Chart Features\"\>$[officename] Chart Features\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	2			0	uk	Charts allow you to present data so that it is easy to visualize.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	6			0	uk	You can create a chart from source data in a Calc spreadsheet or a Writer table. When the chart is embedded in the same document as the data, it stays linked to the data, so that the chart automatically updates when you change the source data.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153143	7			0	uk	Chart Types				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112	8			0	uk	Choose from a variety of 3D charts and 2D charts, such as bar charts, line charts, stock charts. You can change chart types with a few clicks of the mouse.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149665	10			0	uk	Individual Formatting				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441	11			0	uk	You can customize individual chart elements, such as axes, data labels, and legends, by right-clicking them in the chart, or with toolbar icons and menu commands.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Charts in $[officename]				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148664				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>charts; overview\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HowTos for charts\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148664	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"chart_main\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/main0000.xhp\" name=\"Charts in $[officename]\"\>Using Charts in %PRODUCTNAME\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"chart\"\>$[officename] lets you present data graphically in a chart, so that you can visually compare data series and view trends in the data. You can insert charts into spreadsheets, text documents, drawings, and presentations. \</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153143	5			0	uk	Chart Data				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id5181432				0	uk	Charts can be based on the following data:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7787102				0	uk	Spreadsheet values from Calc cell ranges				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7929929				0	uk	Cell values from a Writer table				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id4727011				0	uk	Values that you enter in the Chart Data Table dialog (you can create these charts in Writer, Draw, or Impress, and you can copy and paste them also to Calc)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id76601				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Creates a chart in the current document. To use a continuous range of cells as the data source for your chart, click inside the cell range, and then choose this command. Alternatively, select some cells and choose this command to create a chart of the selected cells.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5345011				0	uk	To insert a chart				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5631580				0	uk	To edit a chart				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7911008				0	uk	Click a chart to edit the object properties:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id9844660				0	uk	Size and position on the current page.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id8039796				0	uk	Alignment, text wrap, outer borders, and more.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7986693				0	uk	Double-click a chart to enter the chart edit mode:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id2350840				0	uk	Chart data values (for charts with own data).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id3776055				0	uk	Chart type, axes, titles, walls, grid, and more.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id8442335				0	uk	Double-click a chart element in chart edit mode:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id4194769				0	uk	Double-click an axis to edit the scale, type, color, and more.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id8644672				0	uk	Double-click a data point to select and edit the data series to which the data point belongs.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id6574907				0	uk	With a data series selected, click, then double-click a single data point to edit the properties of this data point (for example, a single bar in a bar chart).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id1019200902360575				0	uk	Double-click the legend to select and edit the legend. Click, then double-click a symbol in the selected legend to edit the associated data series.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7528916				0	uk	Double-click any other chart element, or click the element and open the Format menu, to edit the properties.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id8420667				0	uk	Click outside the chart to leave the current edit mode.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id4923856				0	uk	To print a chart in high quality, you can export the chart to a PDF file and print that file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200912061033				0	uk	In chart edit mode, you see the \<link href=\"text/schart/main0202.xhp\"\>Formatting Bar\</link\> for charts near the upper border of the document. The Drawing Bar for charts appears near the lower border of the document. The Drawing Bar shows a subset of the icons from the \<link href=\"text/simpress/main0210.xhp\"\>Drawing\</link\> toolbar of Draw and Impress.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id0810200902080452				0	uk	You can right-click an element of a chart to open the context menu. The context menu offers many commands to format the selected element.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id081020090354489				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Formats the selected title.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
