helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Chart Type Pie 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	bm_id7621997				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>donut charts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pie charts;types\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chart types;pie/donut\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	hd_id3365276				0	uk	\<variable id=\"type_pie\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_pie.xhp\"\>Chart Type Pie\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id245979				0	uk	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	hd_id5799432				0	uk	Pie				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	uk	A pie chart shows values as circular sectors of the total circle. The length of the arc, or the area of each sector, is proportional to its value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	uk	Pie - this subtype shows sectors as colored areas of the total pie, for one data column only. In the created chart, you can click and drag any sector to separate that sector from the remaining pie or to join it back.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	uk	Exploded pie - this subtype shows the sectors already separated from each other. In the created chart, you can click and drag any sector to move it along a radial from the pie's center.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	uk	Donut - this subtype can show multiple data columns. Each data column is shown as one donut shape with a hole inside, where the next data column can be shown. In the created chart, you can click and drag an outer sector to move it along a radial from the donut's center.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	uk	Exploded donut - this subtype shows the outer sectors already separated from the remaining donut. In the created chart, you can click and drag an outer sector to move it along a radial from the donut's center.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Chart Type Bubble				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	bm_id2183975				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>bubble charts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chart types;bubble\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	hd_id1970722				0	uk	\<variable id=\"type_bubble\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_bubble.xhp\"\>Chart Type Bubble\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	par_id40589				0	uk	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	hd_id0526200904491284				0	uk	Bubble				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	par_id0526200904491222				0	uk	A bubble chart shows the relations of three variables. Two variables are used for the position on the X-axis and Y-axis, while the third variable is shown as the relative size of each bubble.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	par_id0526200906040162				0	uk	The data series dialog for a bubble chart has an entry to define the data range for the Bubble Sizes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Chart Type Column and Line 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id5976744				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>column and line charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;column and line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combination charts\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8596453				0	uk	\<variable id=\"type_column_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_line.xhp\"\>Chart Type Column and Line\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id4818567				0	uk	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id2451551				0	uk	Column and Line				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3101901				0	uk	A Column and Line chart is a combination of a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_bar.xhp\"\>Column chart\</link\> with a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_line.xhp\"\>Line chart\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7910397				0	uk	Select one of the variants				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5244300				0	uk	Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn side by side so that you can easily compare their values.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7163609				0	uk	Stacked Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn stacked above each other, so that the height of a column visualizes the sum of the data values.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1842097				0	uk	You can insert a second y-axis with \<link href=\"text/schart/01/04040000.xhp\"\>Insert - Axes\</link\> after you finish the wizard.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8297677				0	uk	To specify a data range				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8871120				0	uk	The leftmost columns (or the top rows) of the selected data range provide the data that are shown as Columns objects. The other columns or rows of the data range provide the data for the Lines objects. You can change this assignment in the \<emph\>Data Series\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2952055				0	uk	Select the data range.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id594500				0	uk	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1944944				0	uk	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id6667683				0	uk	Organizing data series				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7616809				0	uk	In the Data Series list box you see a list of all data series in the current chart.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9770195				0	uk	The column data series are positioned at the top of the list, the line data series at the bottom of the list.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1446272				0	uk	To organize the data series, select an entry in the list.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3779717				0	uk	Click Add to add another data series below the selected entry. The new data series has the same type as the selected entry.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5056611				0	uk	Click Remove to remove the selected entry from the Data Series list.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7786492				0	uk	Use the Up and Down arrow buttons to move the selected entry in the list up or down. This way you can convert a Column data series to a List data series and back. This does not change the order in the data source table, but changes only the arrangement in the chart.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id265816				0	uk	Editing data series				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6768700				0	uk	Click an entry in the list to view and edit the properties for that entry.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1924497				0	uk	In the Data Ranges list box you see the role names and cell ranges of the data series components. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5081942				0	uk	Click an entry, then edit the contents in the text box below. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2958464				0	uk	The label next to the text box states the currently selected role. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id883816				0	uk	Enter the range or click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5091708				0	uk	The range for a data role, like Y-Values, must not include a label cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id974456				0	uk	Editing categories or data labels				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2767113				0	uk	Enter or select a cell range that will be used as text for categories or data labels. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id301828				0	uk	The values in the Categories range will be shown as labels on the x axis.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8996246				0	uk	Inserting chart elements				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5729544				0	uk	Use the Chart Elements page of the Chart Wizard to insert any of the following elements:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2932828				0	uk	Chart titles				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9449446				0	uk	Legend				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8122196				0	uk	Visible grid lines				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	uk	For additional elements use the Insert menu of the chart in edit mode. There you can define the following elements:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9141819				0	uk	Secondary axes				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	uk	Minor grids				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	uk	Data labels				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	uk	Statistics, for example mean values, y error bars and trend lines				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7889950				0	uk	To set different data labels for each data series, use the properties dialog of the data series.				20220827 09:49:47
