helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119	4			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Numbers\"\>Numbers\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Data Point				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010100.xhp\" name=\"Data Point\"\>Data Point\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577	2			0	uk	This dialog allows you to change the properties of a selected data point. The dialog appears when there is only one data point selected when you choose \<emph\>Format - Format Selection\</emph\>. Some of the menu entries are only available for 2D or 3D charts.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149121	3			0	uk	Any changes made only affect this one data point. For example, if you edit the color of a bar, only the color of that bar will be different.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Grids				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>axes; inserting grids\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids; inserting in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434	1			0	uk	Grids				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"gitter\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>You can divide the axes into sections by assigning gridlines to them. This allows you to get a better overview of the chart, especially if you are working with large charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The Y axis major grid is activated by default.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156286	3			0	uk	Major grids				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154511	4			0	uk	Defines the axis to be set as the major grid.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400	5			0	uk	X axis				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749	6			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_X_MAIN\"\>Adds gridlines to the X axis of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754	7			0	uk	\<variable id=\"sytextxgitter\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleGridHorizontal\"\>The \<emph\>Horizontal Grid On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar toggles the visibility of the grid display for the X axis. Note: This only works if the \<emph\>Minor grid\</emph\> check boxes in \<emph\>Insert - Grids\</emph\> are cleared.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Otherwise, the minor grid remains visible when the major grid is turned off.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228	8			0	uk	Y axis				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004	9			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Y_MAIN\"\>Adds gridlines to the Y axis of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150344	10			0	uk	\<variable id=\"sytextygitter\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleGridVertical\"\>The \<emph\>Vertical Grid On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar toggles the visibility of the grid display for the Y axis. Note: This only works if the X-axis \<emph\>Minor grid\</emph\> is not selected in \<emph\>Insert - Grids\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Otherwise, the minor grid remains visible when the major grid is turned off.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166430	11			0	uk	Z axis				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155378	12			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Z_MAIN\"\>Adds gridlines to the Z axis of the chart.\</ahelp\> This option is only available if you're working with 3D charts.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146978	13			0	uk	Minor grids				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156449	14			0	uk	Use this area to assign a minor grid for each axis. Assigning minor grids to the axis reduces the distance between the major grids.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153308	15			0	uk	X axis				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148704	16			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_X_HELP\"\>Adds gridlines that subdivide the X axis into smaller sections.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153917	17			0	uk	Y axis				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154536	18			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Y_HELP\"\>Adds gridlines that subdivide the Y axis into smaller sections.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148607	19			0	uk	Z axis				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153247	20			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Z_HELP\"\>Adds gridlines that subdivide the Z axis into smaller sections.\</ahelp\> This option is only available if you're working with 3D charts.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Data Series				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150449	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010200.xhp\" name=\"Data Series\"\>Data Series\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	2			0	uk	Use this to change the properties of a selected data series. This dialog appears when one data series is selected when you choose \<emph\>Format - Format Selection\</emph\>. Some of the menu entries are only available for 2D or 3D charts.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015	4			0	uk	Any changes made here affect the entire data series. For example, if you change the color, all elements belonging to this data series will change color.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146916	3			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Y Error Bars\"\>Y Error Bars\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Trend Lines 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	bm_id1744743				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;regression curves\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>regression curves in charts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>trend lines in charts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>mean value lines in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id5409405				0	uk	\<variable id=\"regression\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050100.xhp\"\>Trend Lines\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7272255				0	uk	\<variable id=\"trendlinestext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Trend lines can be added to all 2D chart types except for Pie and Stock charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id143436				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>No trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5716727				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>A linear trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5840021				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>A logarithmic trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9417096				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>An exponential trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8482924				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>A power trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8962370				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the trend line equation next to the trend line.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id6889858				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the coefficient of determination next to the trend line.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8398998				0	uk	If you insert a trend line to a chart type that uses categories, like \<emph\>Line \</emph\>or \<emph\>Column, \</emph\>then the numbers 1, 2, 3, \<emph\>…\</emph\> are used as x-values to calculate the trend line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5676747				0	uk	To insert trend lines for all data series, double-click the chart to enter edit mode. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Trend Lines\</item\>, then select the type of trend line from None, Linear, Logarithmic, Exponential, or Power trend line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4349192				0	uk	To insert a trend line for a single data series, select the data series in the chart, right-click to open the context menu, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Trend Line\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9337443				0	uk	To delete a single trend line or mean value line, click the line, then press the Del key.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4529251				0	uk	To delete all trend lines, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Trend Lines\</item\>, then select \<emph\>None\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id296334				0	uk	A trend line is shown in the legend automatically.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4072084				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Mean Value Lines are special trend lines that show the mean value. Use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Mean Value Lines\</item\> to insert mean value lines for data series.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9569689				0	uk	The trend line has the same color as the corresponding data series. To change the line properties, select the trend line and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Format Selection - Line\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id846888				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To show the trend line equation, select the trend line in the chart, right-click to open the context menu, and choose \<emph\>Insert Trend Line Equation\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8962065				0	uk	When the chart is in edit mode, %PRODUCTNAME gives you the equation of the trend line and the coefficient of determination R². Click on the trend line to see the information in the status bar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id1328470				0	uk	For a category chart (for example a line chart), the trend line information is calculated using numbers 1, 2, 3, … as x-values. This is also true if your data series uses other numbers as names for the x-values. For such charts the XY chart type might be more suitable.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8092593				0	uk	To show the equation and the coefficient of determination, select the trend line and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Format Selection - Equation\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7971434				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enable Show equation to see the equation of the trend line.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id558793				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enable Show Coefficient of Determination to see the determination coefficient of the trend line.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7735221				0	uk	You can also calculate the parameters using Calc functions as follows.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id5744193				0	uk	The linear regression equation				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9251991				0	uk	The \<emph\>linear regression\</emph\> follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=m*x+b\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7951902				0	uk	m = SLOPE(Data_Y;Data_X) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id6637165				0	uk	b = INTERCEPT(Data_Y ;Data_X) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7879268				0	uk	Calculate the coefficient of determination by				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9244361				0	uk	r² = RSQ(Data_Y;Data_X) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id2083498				0	uk	Besides m, b and r² the array function \<emph\>LINEST\</emph\> provides additional statistics for a regression analysis.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id2538834				0	uk	The logarithm regression equation				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id394299				0	uk	The \<emph\>logarithm regression\</emph\> follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=a*ln(x)+b\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id2134159				0	uk	a = SLOPE(Data_Y;LN(Data_X)) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5946531				0	uk	b = INTERCEPT(Data_Y ;LN(Data_X)) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5649281				0	uk	r² = RSQ(Data_Y;LN(Data_X)) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id7874080				0	uk	The exponential regression equation				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4679097				0	uk	 For exponential trend lines a transformation to a linear model takes place. The optimal curve fitting is related to the linear model and the results are interpreted accordingly. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9112216				0	uk	The exponential regression follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=b*exp(a*x)\</item\> or \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=b*m^x\</item\>, which is transformed to \<item type=\"literal\"\>ln(y)=ln(b)+a*x\</item\> or \<item type=\"literal\"\>ln(y)=ln(b)+ln(m)*x\</item\> respectively.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4416638				0	uk	a = SLOPE(LN(Data_Y);Data_X) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id1039155				0	uk	The variables for the second variation are calculated as follows:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7184057				0	uk	m = EXP(SLOPE(LN(Data_Y);Data_X)) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id786767				0	uk	b = EXP(INTERCEPT(LN(Data_Y);Data_X)) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7127292				0	uk	Calculate the coefficient of determination by				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5437177				0	uk	r² = RSQ(LN(Data_Y);Data_X) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id6946317				0	uk	Besides m, b and r² the array function LOGEST provides additional statistics for a regression analysis.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id6349375				0	uk	The power regression equation				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id1857661				0	uk	 For \<emph\>power regression\</emph\> curves a transformation to a linear model takes place. The power regression follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=b*x^a\</item\> , which is transformed to \<item type=\"literal\"\>ln(y)=ln(b)+a*ln(x)\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8517105				0	uk	a = SLOPE(LN(Data_Y);LN(Data_X)) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9827265				0	uk	b = EXP(INTERCEPT(LN(Data_Y);LN(Data_X)) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id2357249				0	uk	r² = RSQ(LN(Data_Y);LN(Data_X)) 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id9204077				0	uk	Constraints				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7393719				0	uk	 The calculation of the trend line considers only data pairs with the following values:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7212744				0	uk	logarithm regression: only positive x-values are considered,				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id1664479				0	uk	exponential regression: only positive y-values are considered,				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8734702				0	uk	power regression: only positive x-values and positive y-values are considered.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id181279				0	uk	You should transform your data accordingly; it is best to work on a copy of the original data and transform the copied data.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id7907040				0	uk	The polynomial regression equation				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8918729				0	uk	A \<emph\>polynomial regression\</emph\> curve cannot be added automatically. You must calculate this curve manually. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id33875				0	uk	Create a table with the columns x, x², x³, … , xⁿ, y up to the desired degree n. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8720053				0	uk	Use the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=LINEST(Data_Y,Data_X)\</item\> with the complete range x to xⁿ (without headings) as Data_X. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5068514				0	uk	The first row of the LINEST output contains the coefficients of the regression polynomial, with the coefficient of xⁿ at the leftmost position.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8202154				0	uk	The first element of the third row of the LINEST output is the value of r². See the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#Section8\"\>LINEST\</link\> function for details on proper use and an explanation of the other output parameters.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4562211				0	uk	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\"\>Y Error Bars tab page\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
