helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id389721				0	uk	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id9826349				0	uk	Line				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2334665				0	uk	A line chart shows values as points on the y axis. The x axis shows categories. The y values of each data series can be connected by a line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8956572				0	uk	Points only - this subtype plots only points.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id500808				0	uk	Points and lines - this subtype plots points and connects points of the same data series by a line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8366649				0	uk	Lines only - this subtype plots only lines.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id476393				0	uk	3D lines - this subtype connects points of the same data series by a 3D line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2655720				0	uk	Mark \<emph\>Stack series\</emph\> to arrange the points' y values cumulative above each other. The y values no longer represent absolute values, except for the first column which is drawn at the bottom of the stacked points. If you select \<emph\>Percent\</emph\>, the y values are scaled as percentage of the category total.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3682058				0	uk	Mark \<emph\>Smooth lines\</emph\> to draw curves through the points instead of straight lines. Click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> for a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/smooth_line_properties.xhp\"\>dialog\</link\> to change the curves' properties.				20220827 09:49:47
