helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3004547				0	uk	The open, low, high, and closing values of a row build together one data unit in the chart. A stock price data series consists of several rows containing such data units. The column containing the transaction volume builds an optional second data series.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	uk	Depending on the chosen variant, you do not need all columns.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id18616				0	uk	Stock Chart Variants				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	uk	Choose the \<emph\>Stock\</emph\> chart type on the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart wizard\</link\>. Then select one of the four variants.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id4569231				0	uk	Type 1				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	uk	Based on\<emph\> low\</emph\>         \<emph\>and high \</emph\>column the Type 1 shows the distance between bottom price (low) and top price (high) by a vertical line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	uk	Based on\<emph\> low, high,\</emph\> and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column Type 1 shows an additional horizontal mark \<emph\>for\</emph\> the closing price.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id5947141				0	uk	Type 2				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	uk	Based on \<emph\>open, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column Type 2 generates the traditional "candle stick" chart. Type 2 draws the vertical line between the bottom and top price and adds a rectangle in front, which visualizes the range between the opening and closing price. If you click on the rectangle you see more information in the status bar. %PRODUCTNAME uses different fill colors for rising values (the opening price is lower than the closing price) and falling values.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	uk	Type 3				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	uk	Based on \<emph\>volume, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column chart Type 3 draws a chart like Type 1, with additional columns for the transaction volume.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id4313791				0	uk	Type 4				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	uk	Based on all five data columns \<emph\>volume, open, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\>, Type 4 combines a chart of Type 2 with a column chart for the transaction volume.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	uk	Because measurement for transaction volume might be "units", a second y axis is introduced in chart Type 3 and Type 4. The price axis is shown on the right side and the volume axis on the left side.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id2318796				0	uk	Setting the Data Source				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id399182				0	uk	Charts based on its own data				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5298318				0	uk	To change the data series of a chart having its own data, choose \<link href=\"text/schart/01/03010000.xhp\"\>Chart Data Table\</link\> from the View menu or from the context menu of the chart in edit mode.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	uk	In an embedded chart data table, the data series are always organized in columns.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	uk	For a new stock chart first use a column chart. Add the columns you need and enter your data in the order which is shown in the example, omitting any columns not required for the desired variant. Use Move Series Right to change the column order. Close the chart data table. Now use the Chart Type dialog to change to the stock chart variant. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6182744				0	uk	If you have already got a stock chart and you want to change the variant, then first change the chart type to a column chart, add or remove columns so that it fits to the variant, and then change the chart type back to a stock chart.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	uk	Do not write the name of a data series in a row. Write the name into the field above the role name.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	uk	The order of the rows determines how the categories are arranged in the chart. Use Move Row Down to change the order.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id888698				0	uk	Charts based on Calc or Writer tables				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	uk	You can choose or alter a data range on the second page of the Chart wizard or in the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_range.xhp\"\>Data Range\</link\> dialog. For fine tuning use the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_series.xhp\"\>Data Series\</link\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	uk	To specify a data range do one of the following:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	uk	Enter the data range in the text box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9759514				0	uk	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1614429				0	uk	As long as the syntax is not correct, %PRODUCTNAME shows the text in red.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1589098				0	uk	In Calc, click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog, then drag to select the data range. When you release the mouse, the data are entered. Click \<emph\>Select \</emph\>               \<emph\>data range\</emph\> again to add a data range. In the input field of the minimized dialog, click after the entry and type a semicolon. Then drag to select the next range.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id8746910				0	uk	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9636524				0	uk	Your stock chart data are "in columns", if the information in a row belongs to the same "candle stick".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id5675527				0	uk	Fine Tuning the Data Ranges of Table Based Stock Charts				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3486434				0	uk	You can organize data series and edit the source for parts of single data series on the third page of the Chart wizard or on the page Data Series in the Data Range dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id3068636				0	uk	Organize Data Series				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2480849				0	uk	In the \<emph\>data series\</emph\> area on the left side of the dialog, you can organize the data series of the actual chart. A stock chart has at least one data series containing the prices. It might have a second data series for transaction volume.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4181951				0	uk	If you have got more than one price data series, use the Up and Down arrow buttons to order them. The order determines the arrangement in the chart. Do the same for volume data series. You cannot switch price and volume data series.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2927335				0	uk	To remove a data series, select the data series in the list and click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2107303				0	uk	To add a data series, select one of the existing data series and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>. You get an empty entry below the selected one, which has the same type. If you have no price data series or no volume data series, you must first select a range for these series in the \<emph\>Data Range\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id4071779				0	uk	Setting Data Ranges				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7844477				0	uk	In the \<emph\>Data Ranges\</emph\> dialog you can set or change the data range of each component of the selected data series.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6478469				0	uk	In the upper list you see the role name of the components and the current values. When you have selected a role, you can change the value in the text box below the list. The label shows the selected role.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	uk	Enter the range into the text box or click on \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7985168				0	uk	Select Open Values, Close Values, High Values, and Low Values in any order. Specify only the ranges for those roles which you need for the chosen variant of the stock chart. The ranges need not be next to each other in the table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id876186				0	uk	Legend				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	uk	The legend displays the labels from the first row or column or from the special range that you have set in the \<emph\>Data Series\</emph\> dialog. If your chart does not contain labels, the legend displays text like "Row 1, Row 2, ...", or "Column A, Column B, ..." according to the row number or column letter of the chart data.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2377697				0	uk	The legend shows the value from the range, which you entered in the \<emph\>Range for Name\</emph\> field in the \<emph\>Data Range\</emph\> dialog. The default entry is the column header of the closing price column.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	uk	Select one of the position options. When the chart is finished, you can specify other positions using the Format menu.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Chart Wizard - Data Range				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	bm_id2429578				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>data ranges in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id8313852				0	uk	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_range\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_range.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Data Range\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8829309				0	uk	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can select one single source of data range. This range may consist of more than one rectangular range of cells.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Data Ranges dialog where you can edit Data Range and Data Series.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2025818				0	uk	Use the Chart Wizard - Data Series page if you need more control over the data ranges.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8466139				0	uk	This dialog is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id1877193				0	uk	To specify a data range				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5924863				0	uk	Select the data range. Do one of the following:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4357432				0	uk	Enter the data range in the text box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5626392				0	uk	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1363872				0	uk	In Calc, click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog, then drag over a cell area to select the data range.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6823938				0	uk	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1434369				0	uk	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	uk	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	uk	In the preview you can see how the final chart will look.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id379650				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the data range that you want to include in your chart. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id953703				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive rows in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data series will contain x-values for all series. All other data series are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4496597				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive columns in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data column will contain x-values for all series. All other data columns are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2898953				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first row in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first row in the range is used as categories. The remaining rows comprise the data series. If this check box is not selected, all rows are data series.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7546311				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first column in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first column in the range is used as categories. The remaining columns comprise the data columns. If this check box is not selected, all columns are data columns.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Chart Type Column and Bar				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	bm_id4919583				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>column charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bar charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;column and bar\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id649433				0	uk	\<variable id=\"type_column_bar\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_bar.xhp\"\>Chart Type Column and Bar\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id3430585				0	uk	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id9826960				0	uk	Column				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id2244026				0	uk	This type shows a bar chart or bar graph with vertical bars. The height of each bar is proportional to its value. The x axis shows categories. The y axis shows the value for each category.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id1281167				0	uk	Normal - this subtype shows all data values belonging to a category next to each other. Main focus is on the individual absolute values, compared to every other value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id3249000				0	uk	Stacked - this subtype shows the data values of each category on top of each other. Main focus is the overall category value and the individual contribution of each value within its category.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id6968901				0	uk	Percent - this subtype shows the relative percentage of each data value with regard to the total of its category. Main focus is the relative contribution of each value to the category's total.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	uk	You can enable a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D view\</link\> of the data values. The "realistic" scheme tries to give the best 3D look. The "simple" scheme tries to mimic the chart view of other Office products.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id7359233				0	uk	For 3D charts, you can select the shape of each data value from Box, Cylinder, Cone, and Pyramid.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id955839				0	uk	Bar				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id6596881				0	uk	This type shows a bar chart or bar graph with horizontal bars. The length of each bar is proportional to its value. The y axis shows categories. The x axis shows the value for each category.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id8750572				0	uk	The subtypes are the same as for the Column type.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Data Table				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150869	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/03010000.xhp\" name=\"Data Table\"\>Data Table\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramData\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Data Table \</emph\>dialog where you can edit the chart data.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667	51			0	uk	The\<emph\> Data Table \</emph\>dialog is not available if you insert a chart that is based on a Calc sheet or on a Writer table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id6746421				0	uk	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06990000.xhp\"\>To update a chart manually when a Writer table got changed\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id2565996				0	uk	Some changes will become visible only after you close and reopen the dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id6129947				0	uk	To change chart data				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id8141117				0	uk	When you create a chart that is based on default data, or when you copy a chart into your document, you can open the Data Table dialog to enter your own data. The chart responds to the data in a live preview.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id9487594				0	uk	Close the Chart Data dialog to apply all changes to the chart. Choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\> to cancel the changes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id4149906				0	uk	Insert or select a chart that is not based on existing cell data.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id6064943				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>View - Chart Data Table\</emph\> to open the Data Table dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	uk	The data series are organized in columns. The role of the left most column is set to categories or data labels respectively. The contents of the left most column are always formatted as text. You can insert more text columns to be used as hierarchical labels.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id9799798				0	uk	Click a cell in the dialog and change the contents. Click another cell to see the changed contents in the preview.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	uk	Enter the name of the data series in the text box above the column.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id743430				0	uk	Use the icons above the table to insert or delete rows and columns. For data series with multiple columns, only whole data series can be inserted or deleted. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	uk	The order of the data series in the chart is the same as in the data table. Use the \<emph\>Move Series Right\</emph\> icon to switch the current column with its neighbor on the right.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id9116794				0	uk	The order of the categories or data points in the chart is the same as in the data table. Use the \<emph\>Move Row Down\</emph\> icon to switch the current row with its neighbor below.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150297	20			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new row below the current row.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384	23			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new data series after the current column.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152297				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new text column after the current column for hierarchical axes descriptions.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159231	26			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the current row. It is not possible to delete the label row.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153336	29			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the current series or text column. It is not possible to delete the first text column.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id4089175				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Switches the current column with its neighbor at the right.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3949095				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Switches the current row with its neighbor below.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id6697286				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter names for the data series.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
