helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>Options\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155067	2			0	uk	Use this dialog to define some options that are available for specific chart types. The contents of the Options dialog vary with the chart type.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043	9			0	uk	Align data series to:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145228	10			0	uk	In this area you can choose between two Y axis scaling modes. The axes can only be scaled and given properties separately.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147346	4			0	uk	Primary Y axis				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005	15			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_OPTIONS:RBT_OPT_AXIS_1\"\>This option is active as default. All data series are aligned to the primary Y axis.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143221	5			0	uk	Secondary Y axis				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656	11			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_OPTIONS:RBT_OPT_AXIS_2\"\>Changes the scaling of the Y axis. This axis is only visible when at least one data series is assigned to it and the axis view is active.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166423	6			0	uk	Settings				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365	12			0	uk	Define the settings for a bar chart in this area. Any changes apply to all data series of the chart, not to the selected data only.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145584	7			0	uk	Spacing				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376	13			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_OPTIONS:MT_GAP\"\>Defines the spacing between the columns in percent.\</ahelp\> The maximal spacing is 600%.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145384	8			0	uk	Overlap				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156447	14			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_OPTIONS:MT_OVERLAP\"\>Defines the necessary settings for overlapping data series.\</ahelp\> You can choose between -100% and +100%.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153305	16			0	uk	Connection Lines				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868	17			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTIONS:CB_CONNECTOR\"\>For "stacked" and "percent" column (vertical bar) charts, mark this check box to connect the column layers that belong together with lines.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id9842219				0	uk	Show bars side by side				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id9800103				0	uk	If two axes are shown in a bar chart, and some data series are attached to the first axis, while some other data series are attached to the second axis, then both sets of data series are shown independently, overlapping each other.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2144535				0	uk	As a result, bars attached to the first y-axis are partly or completely hidden by bars attached to the second y-axis. To avoid this, enable the option to display bars side by side. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The bars from different data series are shown as if they were attached only to one axis.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id24414				0	uk	Clockwise direction				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2527237				0	uk	Available for pie and donut charts. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The default direction in which the pieces of a pie chart are ordered is counterclockwise. Enable the \<emph\>Clockwise direction\</emph\> checkbox to draw the pieces in opposite direction.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id401013				0	uk	Starting angle				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id761131				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Drag the small dot along the circle or click any position on the circle to set the starting angle of a pie or donut chart. The starting angle is the mathematical angle position where the first piece is drawn. The value of 90 degrees draws the first piece at the 12 o'clock position. A value of 0 degrees starts at the 3 o'clock position.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id553910				0	uk	In 3D pie and donut charts that were created with older versions of the software, the starting angle is 0 degrees instead of 90 degrees. For old and new 2D charts the default starting angle is 90 degrees.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id1414838				0	uk	When you change the starting angle or the direction, only current versions of the software show the changed values. Older versions of the software display the same document using the default values: Always counterclockwise direction and a starting value of 90 degrees (2D pie charts) or 0 degrees (3D pie charts).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3179723				0	uk	Degrees				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2164067				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the starting angle between 0 and 359 degrees. You can also click the arrows to change the displayed value.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524613				0	uk	Plot missing values				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524650				0	uk	Sometimes values are missing in a data series that is shown in a chart. You can select from different options how to plot the missing values. The options are available for some chart types only.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524823				0	uk	Leave gap				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524811				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, no data will be shown. This is the default for chart types Column, Bar, Line, Net.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524811				0	uk	Assume zero				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id030520091052489				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, the y-value will be shown as zero. This is the default for chart type Area.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524837				0	uk	Continue line				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524938				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, the interpolation from the neighbor values will be shown. This is the default for chart type XY.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524937				0	uk	Include values from hidden cells				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id030520091052494				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Check to also show values of currently hidden cells within the source cell range.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Smooth Line Properties				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	bm_id3803827				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>curves;properties in line charts/XY charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties;smooth lines in line charts/XY charts\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3050325				0	uk	Smooth Line Properties				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id9421979				0	uk	In a chart that displays lines (Line type or XY type), you can choose to show curves instead of straight lines. Some options control the properties of those curves.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id1228370				0	uk	To change line properties				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id1601611				0	uk	Select Cubic Spline or B-Spline.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id879848				0	uk	These are mathematical models that influence the display of the curves. The cubic spline line passes through all points, while the B-spline line connects the first and last point and passes by the intermediate points.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3464461				0	uk	Optionally set the resolution. A higher value leads to a smoother line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	uk	For B-spline lines optionally set the data points order.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3424481				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Apply a cubic spline model.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id1068758				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Apply a B-spline model.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id2320932				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Set the resolution.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id8638874				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Set the data points order.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Alignment				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>aligning;titles in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>titles;alignment (charts)\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05020101.xhp\" name=\"Alignment\"\>Alignment\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020101.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	2			0	uk	Modifies the alignment of the chart title.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	4			0	uk	Some of the options are not available for all types of labels. For example, there are different options for 2D and 3D object labels.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	3			0	uk	Please note that problems may arise in displaying labels if the size of your chart is too small. You can avoid this by either enlarging the view or decreasing the font size.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	3D View 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>3D charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; 3D views\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Illumination; 3D charts\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id3464461				0	uk	\<variable id=\"three_d_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D View\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	uk	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> or in the context menu of a chart you can choose a chart type. \<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog to edit the properties of a three dimensional view for Column, Bar, Pie, and Area charts. For Line and XY (Scatter) charts you can see 3D lines.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6942045				0	uk	The chart preview responds to the new settings that you enter in the dialog. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	uk	When you leave the dialog with OK, the settings are applied permanently. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	uk	When you leave the dialog with Cancel or Escape, the chart returns to the state when you opened the dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8081911				0	uk	For a 3D chart you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - 3D View\</item\> to set perspective, appearance and illumination.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id2924283				0	uk	Perspective				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	uk	Enter the values for rotation of the chart on the three axes and for a perspective view.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9999694				0	uk	Set all angles to 0 for a front view of the chart. Pie charts and donut charts are shown as circles.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2861720				0	uk	With Right-angled axes enabled, you can rotate the chart contents only in X and Y direction, that is, parallel to the chart borders.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	uk	An x value of 90, with y and z set to 0, provides a view from top down to the chart. With x set to -90, you see the bottom of the chart.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	uk	The rotations are applied in the order first x, then y, last z.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	uk	When shading is enabled and you rotate a chart, the lights are rotated as if they are fixed to the chart.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2578203				0	uk	The rotation axes always relate to the page, not to the chart's axes. This is different from some other chart programs.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4923245				0	uk	Select the Perspective check box to view the chart in central perspective as through a camera lens instead of using a parallel projection. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3416547				0	uk	Set the focus length with the spin button. 100% gives a perspective view where a far edge in the chart looks approximately half as big as a near edge.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	uk	Older versions of %PRODUCTNAME cannot display the percentage of perspective the same way as the current version.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7623828				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Right-angled axes is enabled, you can rotate the chart contents only in X and Y direction, that is, parallel to the chart borders. Right-angled axes is enabled by default for newly created 3D charts. Pie and Donut charts do not support right-angled axes.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the x axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5806756				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the y axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8915372				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the z axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6070436				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Mark the Perspective box to view the chart as through a camera lens. Use the spin button to set the percentage. With a high percentage nearer objects look bigger than more distant objects.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id7564012				0	uk	Appearance				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1186254				0	uk	Select a scheme from the list box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7432477				0	uk	By selecting a scheme, the check boxes and the light sources are set accordingly.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7141026				0	uk	If you mark or unmark a combination of check boxes that is not given by the Realistic or Simple scheme, you create a Custom scheme.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1579027				0	uk	Mark \<emph\>Shading\</emph\> to use the Gouraud method for rendering the surface, otherwise a flat method is used. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5624561				0	uk	The flat method sets a single color and brightness for each polygon. The edges are visible, soft gradients and spot lights are not possible. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5901058				0	uk	The Gouraud method applies gradients for a smoother, more realistic look.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8469191				0	uk	Mark \<emph\>Object Borders\</emph\> to draw lines along the edges.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4407483				0	uk	Mark \<emph\>Rounded Edges\</emph\> to smooth the edges of box shapes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8531449				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a scheme from the list box, or click any of the check boxes below.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Applies Gouraud shading if marked, or flat shading if unmarked.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows borders around the areas by setting the line style to Solid.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Edges are rounded by 5%.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id1939451				0	uk	Illumination				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	uk	Set the light sources for the 3D view.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6531266				0	uk	Click any of the eight buttons to switch a directed light source on or off.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6173894				0	uk	By default, the second light source is switched on. It is the first of seven "normal", uniform light sources. The light source number one projects a specular light with highlights.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	uk	For the selected light source, you can then choose a color and intensity in the list box just below the eight buttons. The brightness values of all lights are added, so use dark colors when you enable multiple lights.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3912778				0	uk	The small preview inside this tab page has two sliders to set the vertical and horizontal position of the selected light source. The light source always aims to the middle of the object.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	uk	The button in the corner of the small preview switches the internal illumination model between a sphere and a cube.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	uk	Use the Ambient light list box to define the ambient light which shines with a uniform intensity from all directions.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2423780				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Drag the right slider to set the vertical height and direction of the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Drag the bottom slider to set the horizontal position and direction of the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to switch between an illumination model of a sphere or a cube.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id533768				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to enable or disable the specular light source with highlights.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to enable or disable the uniform light source.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color for the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color using the color dialog.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color for the ambient light.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
