helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Axes				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153768				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>axes;formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768	1			0	uk	Axes				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"achsen\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramAxisAll\"\>Opens a dialog, where you can edit the properties of the selected axis.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The name of the dialog depends on the selected axis.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667	3			0	uk	The \<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Y axis\"\>Y axis\</link\> has an enhanced dialog. For X-Y charts, the X axis chart is also enhanced by the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040201.xhp\" name=\"Scaling\"\>\<emph\>Scaling\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159266	4			0	uk	Scaling the X axis is only possible in the X-Y chart type.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145230	5			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Character\"\>Character\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Chart Type Area				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	bm_id4130680				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>area charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;area\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	hd_id310678				0	uk	\<variable id=\"type_area\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_area.xhp\"\>Chart Type Area\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id916776				0	uk	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	hd_id961943				0	uk	Area				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	uk	An area chart shows values as points on the y axis. The x axis shows categories. The y values of each data series are connected by a line. The area between each two lines is filled with a color. The area chart's focus is to emphasize the changes from one category to the next.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	uk	Normal - this subtype plots all values as absolute y values. It first plots the area of the last column in the data range, then the next to last, and so on, and finally the first column of data is drawn. Thus, if the values in the first column are higher than other values, the last drawn area will hide the other areas.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id3640247				0	uk	Stacked - this subtypes plots values cumulatively stacked on each other. It ensures that all values are visible, and no data set is hidden by others. However, the y values no longer represent absolute values, except for the last column which is drawn at the bottom of the stacked areas.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id4585100				0	uk	Percent - this subtype plots values cumulatively stacked on each other and scaled as percentage of the category total.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Chart Type XY				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	bm_id84231				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>scatter charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XY charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;XY (scatter)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error indicators in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error bars in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>averages in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>statistics in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variances in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>standard deviation in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id9346598				0	uk	\<variable id=\"type_xy\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_xy.xhp\"\>Chart Type XY (Scatter)\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id2003845				0	uk	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id7757194				0	uk	XY (Scatter)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5977965				0	uk	An XY chart in its basic form is based on one data series consisting of a name, a list of x‑values, and a list of y‑values. Each value pair (x|y) is shown as a point in a coordinate system. The name of the data series is associated with the y‑values and shown in the legend.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	uk	Choose an XY chart for the following example tasks:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	uk	scale the x‑axis				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	uk	generate a parameter curve, for example a spiral				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	uk	draw the graph of a function				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7657399				0	uk	explore the statistical association of quantitative variables				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8925138				0	uk	Your XY chart may have more than one data series.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5461897				0	uk	XY Chart Variants				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8919339				0	uk	You can choose an XY chart variant on the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\>, or by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Chart Type \</item\>for a chart in edit mode.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4634235				0	uk	The chart is created with default settings. After the chart is finished, you can edit its properties to change the appearance. Line styles and icons can be changed on the \<emph\>Line\</emph\>tab page of the data series properties dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5482039				0	uk	Double-click any data point to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Series\</item\> dialog. In this dialog, you can change many properties of the data series.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id0805200810492449				0	uk	For 2D charts, you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Y Error Bars\</item\> to enable the display of error bars.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6221198				0	uk	You can enable the display of mean value lines and trend lines using commands on the Insert menu.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id1393475				0	uk	Points only				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6571550				0	uk	Each data point is shown by an icon. %PRODUCTNAME uses default icons with different forms and colors for each data series. The default colors are set in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Charts - Default Colors\</item\>. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5376140				0	uk	Lines Only				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4408093				0	uk	This variant draws straight lines from one data point to the next. The data points are not shown by icons. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7261268				0	uk	The drawing order is the same as the order in the data series. Mark \<emph\>Sort by X Values\</emph\> to draw the lines in the order of the x values. This sorting applies only to the chart, not to the data in the table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6949369				0	uk	Points and Lines				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9611499				0	uk	This variant shows points and lines at the same time.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6765953				0	uk	3D Lines				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7422711				0	uk	The lines are shown like tapes. The data points are not shown by icons. In the finished chart choose \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D View\</link\> to set properties like illumination and angle of view.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id239265				0	uk	Smooth Lines				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7957396				0	uk	Mark \<emph\>Smooth Lines\</emph\> to draw curves instead of straight line segments.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1202124				0	uk	Click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> to set details for the curves.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5989562				0	uk	\<emph\>Cubic Spline\</emph\> interpolates your data points with polynomials of degree 3. The transitions between the polynomial pieces are smooth, having the same slope and curvature. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6128421				0	uk	The \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> determines how many line segments are calculated to draw a piece of polynomial between two data points. You can see the intermediate points if you click any data point.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9280373				0	uk	\<emph\>B-Spline\</emph\> uses the data points as control points to form a B-spline curve. Those curves are built piecewise from polynomials. The \<emph\>Data points order\</emph\> sets the degree k of these polynomials. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Y Error Bars				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147428	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Y Error Bars\"\>Y Error Bars\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"statistik\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use the \<emph\>Y Error Bars\</emph\> dialog to display error bars for 2D charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3401287				0	uk	An error bar is an indicator line that spans over a range from y - NegativeErrorValue to y + PositiveErrorValue. In this term, y is the value of the data point. When "standard deviation" is selected, y is the mean value of the data series. NegativeErrorValue and PositiveErrorValue are the amounts calculated by the error bar function or given explicitly.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965	23			0	uk	The \<emph\>Insert - Y Error Bars\</emph\> menu command is only available for 2D charts.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150344	5			0	uk	Error category				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202	6			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Error category\</emph\> area, you can choose different ways to display the error category.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152989	7			0	uk	None				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409	8			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_STAT:RBT_NONE\"\>Does not show any error bars.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145117	17			0	uk	Constant value				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390	18			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_STAT:MTR_FLD_MINUS\"\>Displays constant values that you specify in the Parameters area.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159204	13			0	uk	Percentage				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150048	14			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_STAT:MTR_FLD_PERCENT\"\>Displays a percentage. The display refers to the corresponding data point. Set the percentage in the Parameters area.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id8977629				0	uk	Functions				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id7109286				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select a function to calculate the error bars.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id5154576				0	uk	Standard Error: Displays the standard error.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979	10			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Variance: Displays the variance calculated from the number of data points and respective values.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153249	12			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Standard Deviation: Displays the standard deviation (square root of the variance).\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149870	16			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Error Margin: Displays the highest error margin in percent according to the highest value of the data group. Set the percentage in the Parameters area.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id350962				0	uk	Cell Range				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6679586				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click Cell Range and then specify a cell range from which to take the positive and negative error bar values.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3872188				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click a button to shrink the dialog, then use the mouse to select the cell range in the spreadsheet. Click the button again to restore the dialog to full size.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id2633747				0	uk	From Data Table				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6633503				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a chart with its own data, the error bar values can be entered in the chart data table. The Data Table dialog shows additional columns titled Positive Y-Error-Bars and Negative Y-Error-Bars.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573839				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value to add to the displayed value as the positive error value.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573862				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value to subtract from the displayed value as the negative error value.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573844				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the address range from where to get the positive error values. Use the Shrink button to select the range from a sheet.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573970				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the address range from where to get the negative error values. Use the Shrink button to select the range from a sheet.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0428200810573977				0	uk	Same value for both				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573991				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enable to use the positive error values also as negative error values. You can only change the value of the "Positve (+)" box. That value gets copied to the "Negative (-)" box automatically.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156396	19			0	uk	Error indicator				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150539	20			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCH_CT_INDICATE2\"\>Specifies the error indicator.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
