helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Chart Wizard - Data Series				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	bm_id8641621				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>order of chart data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id6124149				0	uk	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_series\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_series.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Data Series\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9651478				0	uk	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can change the source range of all data series separately, including their labels. You can also change the range of the categories. You can first select the data range on the Data Range page and then remove unnecessary data series or add data series from other cells here.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id6326487				0	uk	If there seem to be too many options on this page, just define the data range on the Chart Wizard - Data Range page and skip this page.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id686361				0	uk	This dialog is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id9241615				0	uk	Organizing data series				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id7159337				0	uk	In the Data Series list box you see a list of all data series in the current chart.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4921720				0	uk	To organize the data series, select an entry in the list.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id6627094				0	uk	Click Add to add another data series below the selected entry. The new data series has the same type as the selected entry.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	uk	Click Remove to remove the selected entry from the Data Series list.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4443800				0	uk	Use the Up and Down arrow buttons to move the selected entry in the list up or down. This does not change the order in the data source table, but changes only the arrangement in the chart.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id9777520				0	uk	Editing data series				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id1474654				0	uk	Click an entry in the list to view and edit the properties for that entry.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4855189				0	uk	In the Data Ranges list box you see the role names and cell ranges of the data series components. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9475081				0	uk	Click an entry, then edit the contents in the text box below. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4695272				0	uk	The label next to the text box states the currently selected role. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3931699				0	uk	Enter the range or click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id8626667				0	uk	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id5971556				0	uk	The range for a data role, like Y-Values, must not include a label cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id7622608				0	uk	Editing categories or data labels				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9222693				0	uk	Enter or select a cell range that will be used as text for categories or data labels. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9500106				0	uk	Depending on the chart type, the texts are shown on the X axis or as data labels. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id5201879				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows a list of all data series in the chart. Click an entry to view and edit that data series. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert a new series into the list after the selected entry.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2571794				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows all the data ranges used by the data series that is selected in the Data Series list box. Each data range shows the role name and the source range address.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2254402				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the source range address from the second column of the Data Range list box. You can change the range in the text box or by dragging in the document. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2419507				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the source range address of the categories (the texts you can see on the x-axis of a category chart). For an XY-chart, the text box contains the source range of the data labels which are displayed for the data points. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id1091647				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Adds a new entry below the current entry in the Data Series list. If an entry is selected, the new data series gets the same chart type.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id8831446				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the selected entry from the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id7022309				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves up the selected entry in the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2844019				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves down the selected entry in the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
