helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040201.xhp\" name=\"Scale\"\>Scale\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013	2			0	uk	Controls the scaling of the X or Y axis.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576	79			0	uk	The axes are automatically scaled by $[officename] so that all values are optimally displayed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379	3			0	uk	To achieve specific results, you can manually change the axis scaling. For example, you can display only the top areas of the columns by shifting the zero line upwards.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154730	4			0	uk	Scale				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400	5			0	uk	You can enter values for subdividing axes in this area. You can automatically set the properties \<emph\>Minimum, Maximum, Major interval, Minor interval count\</emph\> and \<emph\>Reference value\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150751	6			0	uk	Minimum				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153713	7			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_MIN\"\>Defines the minimum value for the beginning of the axis.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156385	8			0	uk	Maximum				20220827 09:49:47
