helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146974				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>sectors of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>segments of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circle segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ellipses; segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing; sectors and segments\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974	30			0	uk	\<variable id=\"draw_sector\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/draw_sector.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Sectors and Segments\"\>Drawing Sectors and Segments\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	31			0	uk	The \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> toolbar contains tools for drawing ellipses and circles. You can also draw segments and sectors of circles and ellipses.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075	32			0	uk	To draw a sector of a circle or an ellipse:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	33			0	uk	Open the \<emph\>Ellipses\</emph\> toolbar and click one of the \<emph\>Circle Pie\</emph\> or \<emph\>Ellipse Pie\</emph\> icons \<image id=\"img_id3155768\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlepie_unfilled.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155768\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The mouse pointer changes to a cross hair with a small icon of a sector.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199	34			0	uk	Position the pointer at the edge of the circle you want to draw and drag to create the circle.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868	35			0	uk	To create a circle by dragging from the center, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3145361	36			0	uk	Release the mouse button when the circle has reached the size you want. A line corresponding to the circle radius appears in the circle.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872	37			0	uk	Position the pointer where you want to place the first boundary of the sector and click.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871	51			0	uk	As the radius line that follows the pointer is constrained to the circle boundaries, you can click anywhere in the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874	38			0	uk	Position the pointer where you want to place the second boundary of the sector and click. The completed sector is displayed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148581	41			0	uk	To draw a segment of a circle or ellipse, follow the steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3153084	42			0	uk	To draw an arc based on an ellipse, choose one of the arc icons and follow the same steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Grouping Objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; grouping\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793	26			0	uk	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/groups.xhp\" name=\"Grouping Objects\"\>Grouping Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728	27			0	uk	You can combine several objects into a group so that they act as a single object. You can move and transform all objects in a group as a single unit. You can also change the properties (for example, line size, fill color) of all objects in a group as a whole or for individual objects in a group. Groups can be temporary or assigned:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434	64			0	uk	Temporary - group only lasts as long as all of the combined objects are selected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	65			0	uk	Assigned - group lasts until it is ungrouped through a menu command.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252	66			0	uk	Groups can also be grouped in other groups. Actions applied to a group do not affect the relative position of the individual objects to each other in the group.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716	28			0	uk	To group objects:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3145643\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatgroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145643\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346	29			0	uk	Select the objects you want to group and choose \<emph\>Modify - Group\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485	30			0	uk	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147002	31			0	uk	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205	55			0	uk	Selecting Objects in a Group				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3155376\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_entergroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155376\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450	56			0	uk	You can select single objects in a group by entering the group. Double-click a group to enter it and click on the object to select it. You can also add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. The objects that are not part of the group are grayed out.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3155264\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_leavegroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155264\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213	58			0	uk	To exit a group, double-click anywhere outside it.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Defining Custom Colors				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149263				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>colors; defining and saving\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>user-defined colors\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>custom colors\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149263	7			0	uk	\<variable id=\"color_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/color_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Custom Colors\"\>Defining Custom Colors\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154511	8			0	uk	If you want, you can mix a custom color and add it to a color table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600	9			0	uk	To define a custom color				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327	25			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Colors\</emph\> tab. A table of the predefined colors is displayed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657	13			0	uk	Changes made to the standard color table are permanent and are saved automatically.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425	14			0	uk	Click a color in the table that is similar to the one you want to mix. The color appears in the upper preview box to the right of the table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992	15			0	uk	Select the RGB or CMYK color model in the box below the preview boxes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id4979705				0	uk	%PRODUCTNAME uses only the RGB color model for printing in color. The CMYK controls are provided only to ease the input of color values using CMYK notation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152987	16			0	uk	The RGB color model mixes red, green and blue light to create colors on a computer screen. In the RGB model, the three color components are additive and can have values ranging from 0 (black) to 255 (white). The CMYK color model combines Cyan (C), Magenta (M), Yellow (Y), and blacK (K, also used for "Key") to create colors for printing. The four colors of the CMYK models are subtractive and are defined as percentages. Black corresponds to 100 % and white to 0 %.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145386	17			0	uk	Enter a numeric value in the boxes next to the color components. The new color appears in the preview box directly above the color model box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152871	18			0	uk	You can also create a color using a color spectrum. Click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010501.xhp\" name=\"Color\"\>\<emph\>Color\</emph\>\</link\> dialog. Click a color. Use the Hue, Saturation, and Brightness boxes to adjust your color selection.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011	19			0	uk	Do one of the following:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3147244	26			0	uk	If you want to replace the color in the standard color table that your custom color is based on, click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116	20			0	uk	If you want to add your custom color to the standard color table, enter a name in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> text box and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145236	23			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/03170000.xhp\" name=\"Color bar\"\>Color bar\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Adding Text				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153144				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying;text from other documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pasting;text from other documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>legends; drawings\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153144	45			0	uk	\<variable id=\"text_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/text_enter.xhp\" name=\"Adding Text\"\>Adding Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	46			0	uk	There are several types of text you can add to a drawing or presentation: 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	uk	Text in a text box				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	uk	Text that changes character size to fill the frame size				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	uk	Text that is added to any drawing object by double-clicking the object				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10830				0	uk	Text that is copied from a Writer document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	uk	Text that is inserted from a text document or HTML document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202	48			0	uk	Adding a Text Box				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266	49			0	uk	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156450\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156450\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and move the mouse pointer to where you want to enter the text box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149052	50			0	uk	Drag a text box to the size you want in your document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3151194	51			0	uk	Type or paste your text into the text box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118	53			0	uk	Double-click the text to edit it or to format text properties, such as font size or font color. Click the border of the text box to edit the object properties, such as border color or arranging in front or behind other objects.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150437	54			0	uk	Fitting Text to Frames				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146877	56			0	uk	Create a text box as described in the steps above.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	uk	With the text object selected, choose \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Text\</emph\> dialog opens.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AF				0	uk	On the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> tab page, clear the \<emph\>Fit height to text\</emph\> checkbox, then select the \<emph\>Fit to frame\</emph\> checkbox. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id0610200902133994				0	uk	Now you can resize the text box to change the size and shape of the text characters.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155955	58			0	uk	Text Tied to a Graphic				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	uk	You can add text to any graphic after double-clicking the graphic.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	uk	To determine the position of the text, use the settings in \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147366	59			0	uk	For example, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Callouts\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154508\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_calloutshapes.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154508\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the Callouts toolbar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FD				0	uk	Select a callout and move the mouse pointer to where you want the callout to start.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150272	60			0	uk	Drag to draw the callout.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1978514				0	uk	Enter the text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091A				0	uk	Copying Text				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10921				0	uk	Select the text in your Writer document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10925				0	uk	Copy the text to the clipboard (\<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092D				0	uk	Click the page or slide where you want to paste the text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10931				0	uk	Paste the text using \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\> or \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093C				0	uk	Using \<emph\>Paste special\</emph\>, you can choose the text format to be pasted. Depending on formats, you can copy different text attributes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093F				0	uk	Importing Text				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10946				0	uk	Click the page or slide where you want to import the text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1094A				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10952				0	uk	Select a text file (*.txt) or an HTML file and click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Insert Text\</emph\> dialog opens. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to insert the text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149656	73			0	uk	\<variable id=\"align_arrange\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/align_arrange.xhp\" name=\"Arranging and Aligning Objects\"\>Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	bm_id3125863				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>arranging; objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;aligning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aligning;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863	17			0	uk	Arranging Objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3153727	18			0	uk	Each object that you place in your document is successively stacked on the preceding object. To re-arrange the stacking order of a selected object, proceed as follows.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	uk	Click the object whose position you want to change.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327	78			0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to bring up the context menu and choose one of the arrange options:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E6				0	uk	\<emph\>Bring to Front\</emph\> places the object on top of all other objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EC				0	uk	\<emph\>Bring Forward\</emph\> places the object one place forward in the stack of objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F2				0	uk	\<emph\>Send Backward\</emph\> places the object one place back in the stack of objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	uk	\<emph\>Send to Back\</emph\> places the object behind all other objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	uk	\<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\> places the object behind another object that you select				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766	79			0	uk	Arranging an Object Behind Another Object				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN10811				0	uk	Click the object whose position you want to change.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253	80			0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\>. The mouse pointer changes to a hand.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126	81			0	uk	Click the object behind which you want to place the selected object.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145789	20			0	uk	Reversing The Stacking Order of Two Objects				20220827 09:49:47
