helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Graphics Export Options				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150127				0	uk	Graphics Export Options				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3160463				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Defines graphics export options.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id1				0	uk	When you export graphical elements to a file, you can select the file type. For most supported file types a dialog opens where you can setup export options.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id2				0	uk	The following file types do not show an options dialog: PWP, RAS, SVG, TIFF, XPM.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3				0	uk	The other file types show options dialogs where you can set the width and height of the exported image.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id4				0	uk	Depending on the file type, you can specify some more options. Press Shift+F1 and hover over the control to see an extended help text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id388				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the measurement units.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151330				0	uk	Width				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154561				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Specifies the width.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156027				0	uk	Height				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Specifies the height.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150944				0	uk	Resolution				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150129				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the image resolution. Select the measurement units from the list box.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143534				0	uk	More options				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id10				0	uk	For JPEG files you can set the color depth and the quality.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id435923952				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the color depth from 8 bit grayscale or 24 bit true color.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id355152952				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the compression and quality for the export. Choose from a low quality with minimal file size, up to a high quality and big file size. A high compression means a low quality, a low compression means a high quality.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id11				0	uk	For BMP files you can set the compression and the RLE encoding.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id312346798				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Applies RLE (Run Length Encoding) to the BMP graphics.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id12				0	uk	For PBM, PGM, and PPM files you can set the encoding.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id344441				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in binary format. The resulting file is smaller than a text file.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3555783				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in ASCII text format. The resulting file is larger than a binary file.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id13				0	uk	For PNG files you can set the compression and the interlaced mode.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id35674840				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether the graphic is to be saved in interlaced mode.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id14				0	uk	For GIF files you can set the transparency and the interlaced mode.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id31456456938				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to save the background of the picture as transparent. Only objects will be visible in the GIF image. Use the Color Replacer to set the transparent color in the picture.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id15				0	uk	For EPS files you can set the preview, the color format, the compression, and the version.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147779948				0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>You must print an EPS file with a PostScript printer. Other printers will only print the embedded preview.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993155271				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether a preview image is exported in the TIFF format together with the actual PostScript file.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993144740	30			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether a monochrome preview graphic in EPSI format is exported together with the PostScript file. This format only contains printable characters from the 7-bit ASCII code.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993150935	12			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Compression is not available at this level. Select the Level 1 option if your PostScript printer does not offer the capabilities of Level 2.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993159201	14			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the Level 2 option if your output device supports colored bitmaps, palette graphics and compressed graphics.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id319947250	18			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in color.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993147088	20			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in grayscale tones.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id399153683	24			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>LZW compression is the compression of a file into a smaller file using a table-based lookup algorithm.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id319952780	26			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies that you do not wish to use compression.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147250				0	uk	See \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000020.xhp\" name=\"Import and Export Filter Information\"\>Import and Export Filter Information\</link\> for more information about filters.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	ASCII Filter Options				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146856	1			0	uk	ASCII Filter Options				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3153070	2			0	uk	You can specify which options, such as basic font, language, character set, or break, are imported or exported with a text document. The dialog appears when you load an ASCII file with the filter "Text Encoded" or when you save the document the first time, or when you "save as" with another name.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159217	3			0	uk	Properties				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577	4			0	uk	Defines the settings for importing or exporting your file. When exporting, only the character set and paragraph break can be defined.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146959	5			0	uk	Character set				20220827 09:49:47
