helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id314949588				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Determines how the number strings are imported.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id314949587				0	uk	If Language is set to Default (for CSV import) or Automatic (for HTML import), Calc will use the globally set language. If Language is set to a specific language, that language will be used when importing numbers.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id314949586				0	uk	When importing an HTML document, the Language selection can conflict with the global HTML option \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01030500.xhp\" name=\"Use\"\>Use 'English (USA)' locale for numbers\</link\>. The global HTML option is effective only when the Automatic language option is selected. If you select a specific language in the HTML Import Options dialog, the global HTML option is ignored.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154894	47			0	uk	From Row				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150247	48			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCDLG_ASCII:NF_AT_ROW\"\>Specifies the row where you want to start the import.\</ahelp\> The rows are visible in the preview window at the bottom of the dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
