helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Glossary of Internet Terms				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150702				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>Internet glossary\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>common terms;Internet glossary\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>glossaries;Internet terms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>terminology;Internet glossary\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150702	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp\" name=\"Glossary of Internet Terms\"\>Glossary of Internet Terms\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577	2			0	uk	If you are a newcomer to the Internet, you will be confronted with unfamiliar terms: browser, bookmark, e-mail, homepage, search engine, and many others. To make your first steps easier, this glossary explains some of the more important terminology you may find in the Internet, intranet, mail and news.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153146	36			0	uk	Frames				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3157909	37			0	uk	Frames are useful for designing the layout of \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\> pages. $[officename] uses floating frames into which you can place objects such as graphics, movie files and sound. The context menu of a frame shows the options for restoring or editing frame contents. Some of these commands are also listed in \<emph\>Edit - Object\</emph\> when the frame is selected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147077	43			0	uk	FTP				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335	44			0	uk	FTP stands for File Transfer Protocol and is the standard transfer protocol for files in the Internet. An FTP server is a program on a computer connected to the Internet which stores files to be transmitted with the aid of FTP. While FTP is responsible for transmitting and downloading Internet files, \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#http\" name=\"HTTP\"\>HTTP\</link\> (Hypertext Transfer Protocol) provides the connection setup and data transfer between WWW servers and clients.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145609				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609	56			0	uk	HTML				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3161459	57			0	uk	HTML (Hypertext Markup Language) is a document code language, which is used as the file format for WWW documents. It is derived from \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#sgml\" name=\"SGML\"\>SGML\</link\> and integrates text, graphics, videos and sound.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154346	58			0	uk	If you want to type HTML commands directly, for example when doing exercises from one of the many available HTML books, remember that HTML pages are pure text files. Save your document under the document type \<emph\>Text \</emph\>and give it the file name extension .HTML. Be sure there are no umlauts or other special characters of the extended character set. If you want to re-open this file in $[officename] and edit the HTML code, you must load it with the file type \<emph\>Text\</emph\> and not with the file type \<emph\>Web pages\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153960	244			0	uk	There are several references on the Internet providing an introduction to the HTML language.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147423	59			0	uk	HTTP				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379	60			0	uk	The Hypertext Transfer Protocol is a record of transmission of WWW documents between WWW servers (hosts) and browsers (clients).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149290				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149290	61			0	uk	Hyperlink				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420	62			0	uk	Hyperlinks are cross-references, highlighted in text in various colors and activated by mouse-click. With the aid of hyperlinks, readers can jump to specific information within a document as well as to related information in other documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281	63			0	uk	In $[officename] you can assign hyperlinks to text as well as to graphics and text frames (see the Hyperlink Dialog icon on the Standard bar).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152805				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>ImageMap; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152805	64			0	uk	ImageMap				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	65			0	uk	An ImageMap is a reference-sensitive graphic or text frame. You can click on defined areas of the graphic or text frame to go to a target (\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>), which is linked with the area. The reference areas, along with the linked URLs and corresponding text displayed when resting the mouse pointer on these areas, are defined in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\" name=\"ImageMap Editor\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153178	66			0	uk	There are two different types of ImageMaps. A Client Side ImageMap is evaluated on the client computer, which loaded the graphic from the Internet, while a Server Side ImageMap is evaluated on the server computer which provides the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\> page on the Internet. In server evaluation, clicking an ImageMap sends the relative coordinates of the cursor within the image to the server, and a dedicated program on the server responds. In the client evaluation, clicking a defined hotspot of the ImageMap activates the URL, as if it were a normal text link. The URL appears below the mouse pointer when passing across the ImageMap.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740	67			0	uk	As ImageMaps can be used in different ways, they can be stored in different formats.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146874	68			0	uk	ImageMap Formats				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3145153	69			0	uk	ImageMaps are basically divided between those that are analyzed on the server (i. e. your Internet provider) and those analyzed on the web browser of the reader's computer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152881				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>Server Side ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152881	70			0	uk	Server Side ImageMaps				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153057	71			0	uk	Server Side ImageMaps appear for the reader as a picture or frame on the page. Click on the ImageMap with the mouse, and the coordinates of the relative position are sent to the server. Aided by an extra program, the server then determines the next step to take. There are several incompatible methods to define this process, the two most common being:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147502	72			0	uk	W3C (CERN) HTTP Server (Format type: MAP - CERN)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011	73			0	uk	NCSA HTTP Server (Format type: MAP - NCSA)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149483	74			0	uk	$[officename] creates ImageMaps for both methods. Select the format from the \<emph\>File type \</emph\>list in the \<emph\>Save As \</emph\>dialog in the \<emph\>ImageMap Editor\</emph\>. Separate Map Files are created which you must upload to the server. You will need to ask your provider or network administrator which type of ImageMaps are supported by the server and how to access the evaluation program.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152418				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>Client Side ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152418	75			0	uk	Client Side ImageMap				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3151290	76			0	uk	The area of the picture or frame where the reader can click is indicated by the appearance of the linked \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\> when the mouse passes over the area. The ImageMap is stored in a layer below the picture and contains information about the referenced regions. The only disadvantage of Client Side ImageMaps is that older Web browsers cannot read them; a disadvantage that will, however, resolve itself in time.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	77			0	uk	When saving the ImageMap, select the file type \<emph\>SIP - StarView ImageMap\</emph\>. This saves the ImageMap directly in a format which can be applied to every active picture or frame in your document. However, if you just want to use the ImageMap on the current picture or text frame, you do not have to save it in any special format. After defining the regions, simply click \<emph\>Apply\</emph\>. Nothing more is necessary. Client Side ImageMaps saved in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\> format are inserted directly into the page in HTML code.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159125				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>Java; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159125	92			0	uk	Java				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188	93			0	uk	The Java programming language is a platform independent programming language that is especially suited for use in the Internet. Web pages and applications programmed with Java class files can be used on all modern operating systems. Programs using Java programming language are usually developed in a Java development environment and then compiled to a "byte code".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159153				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>plug-ins; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153	107			0	uk	Plug-In				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127	109			0	uk	Extensions providing additional functionality in Web browsers are referred to as Plug-Ins.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147484	108			0	uk	A Plug-In is a term used in various contexts:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3168608	172			0	uk	Plug-Ins in $[officename]				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149910	111			0	uk	You will notice in $[officename] that the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar changes after certain operations. For example, if you insert a formula into your text document, you see icons for editing the formula, in fact the same icons you see in formula documents. In this sense, we refer to the formula as a plug-in within the text document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148387	177			0	uk	Using Plug-Ins to extend your programs				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156737	114			0	uk	Plug-ins, generally speaking, are software additions to particular applications which provide enhanced functionality. Often import and export filters for various file formats are stored as plug-ins in a plug-in directory.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958	115			0	uk	Netscape web browser extensions produced by Netscape Communication Corporation are also called plug-ins. These are external programs mainly taken from the multimedia field and which communicate with the browser through standardized interfaces. These plug-ins can be linked to $[officename] documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149420	179			0	uk	Any Netscape plug-ins (32 bit) installed on your system are automatically recognized by $[officename].				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145647	127			0	uk	Proxy				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455	128			0	uk	A proxy is a computer in the network acting as a kind of clipboard for data transfer. Whenever you access the Internet from a company network and request a Web page that has already been read by a colleague, the proxy will be able to display the page much quicker, as long as it's still in the memory. All that has to be checked in this case is that the page stored in the proxy is the latest version. If this is the case, the page won't have to be downloaded from the much slower Internet but can be loaded directly from the proxy.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154729				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>SGML; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729	229			0	uk	SGML				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147330	230			0	uk	SGML stands for "Standard Generalized Markup Language". SGML is based on the idea that documents have structural and other semantic elements that can be described without reference to how such elements should be displayed. The actual display of such a document may vary, depending on the output medium and style preferences. In structured texts, SGML not only defines structures (in the DTD = Document Type Definition) but also ensures they are consistently used.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148747	231			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\> is a specialized application of SGML. This means that most Web browsers support only a limited range of SGML standards and that almost all SGML-enabled systems can produce attractive HTML pages.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153950				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>search engines; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153950	138			0	uk	Search Engines				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3157965	139			0	uk	A search engine is a service in the Internet based on a software program used to explore a vast amount of information using key words.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150751				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>tags; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150751	141			0	uk	Tags				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156360	142			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\> pages contain certain structural and formatting instructions called tags. Tags are code words enclosed by brackets in the document description language HTML. Many tags contain text or hyperlink references between the opening and closing brackets. For example, titles are marked by the tags <h1> at the beginning and </h1> at the end of the title. Some tags only appear on their own such as <br> for a line break or <img ...> to link a graphic.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153766				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>URL; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153766	145			0	uk	URL				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3152931	146			0	uk	The Uniform Resource Locator (URL) displays the address of a document or a server in the Internet. The general structure of a URL varies according to type and is generally in the form Service://Hostname:Port/Path/Page#Mark although not all elements are always required. An URL can be a FTP address, a WWW (HTTP) address, a file address or an e-mail address.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000408.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Help Menu				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000408.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154689	1			0	uk	Help Menu				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000408.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"content\"\>Choose \<emph\>Help - Contents\</emph\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000408.xhp	0	help	par_id3147240	14			0	uk	\<variable id=\"infoanwendung\"\>Choose \<emph\>Help - About \</emph\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME\</emph\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000408.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387	15			0	uk	Automatically after \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> is first started.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000408.xhp	0	help	par_id3153808	16			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Help - Registration\</emph\> (this is a direct link to an external website)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Conversion of measurement units				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147543				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>measurement units; converting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>units; converting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;metrics\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>metrics;converting\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147543	1			0	uk	Conversion of measurement units				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069F				0	uk	In some dialogs, you can enter measurement values into input boxes. If you just enter a numerical value, the default measurement unit is used.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A2				0	uk	You define the default measurement unit for Writer text documents in the dialog that you get by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</emph\>. For Calc, Draw, and Impress, you open a document of that type and then open the appropriate \<emph\>General\</emph\> page as for Writer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AD				0	uk	In input boxes for length units you can also add the unit abbreviation according to the following list:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	uk	Unit abbreviation				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	uk	Explanation				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C7				0	uk	mm				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	uk	Millimeter				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D4				0	uk	cm				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DA				0	uk	Centimeter				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E1				0	uk	in or "				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E7				0	uk	Inch				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EE				0	uk	pi				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F4				0	uk	Pica				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FB				0	uk	pt				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10701				0	uk	Point				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10704				0	uk	The following formulas convert the units:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	uk	1 cm = 10 mm				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070E				0	uk	1 inch = 2.54 cm				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10712				0	uk	1 inch = 6 Pica = 72 Point				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	uk	For example, in a text document, open \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</emph\>. To indent the current paragraph by one inch, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1 in\</item\> or \<item type=\"literal\"\>1"\</item\> into the "Before text" box. To indent the paragraph by 1 cm, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1 cm\</item\> into the input box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	uk	To input the maximum or minimum allowed value respectively, click the current value and then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Page Up\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Page Down\</item\> key.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Часто вживані кнопки				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152952	1			0	uk	Часто вживані кнопки				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147617	4			0	uk	Скасувати				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155913	5			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Clicking \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> closes a dialog without saving any changes made.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id2341685				0	uk	Завершити				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id6909390				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Applies all changes and closes the wizard.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147477	39			0	uk	Панелі інструментів				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149783	40			0	uk	By clicking the arrow next to some icons you open a toolbar. To move a toolbar, drag the title bar. As soon as you release the mouse button, the toolbar remains at the new position. Drag the title bar to another position, or drag to an edge of the window, where the toolbar will dock. Close a toolbar by clicking the Close Window icon. Make the toolbar visible again by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - (toolbar name)\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152414	79			0	uk	Лічильник				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id1094088				0	uk	У елементах керування форми кнопка лічильника є властивістю числового поля, поля валюти, поля дати чи поля часу. Якщо властивість "Кнопка лічильника" увімкнено, у поле відображається пара символів зі стрілками, що вказують у протилежні боки - вертикально або горизонтально.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id7493209				0	uk	In the Basic IDE, a spin button is the name used for the numerical field together with the two arrow symbols.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155599	78			0	uk	You can type a numerical value into the field next to the spin button, or select the value with the up-arrow or down-arrow symbols on the spin button. On the keyboard you can press the up arrow and down arrow keys to increase or reduce the value. You can press the Page Up and Page Down keys to set the maximum and minimum value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150264	38			0	uk	If the field next to the spin button defines numerical values, you can also define a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp#metrik\" name=\"measurement unit\"\>measurement unit\</link\>, for example, 1 cm or 5 mm, 12 pt or 2".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154232	76			0	uk	Перетворити				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983	77			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>При переході до наступного кроку у діалоговому вікні ця кнопка називається \<emph\>Далі\</emph\>. На останній сторінці помічника вона називається \<emph\>Перетворити\</emph\>. При натисканні на цю кнопку виконується перетворення.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145129	42			0	uk	Контекстне меню				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156553	44			0	uk	\<variable id=\"context\"\>To activate the context menu of an object, first click the object with the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>left\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> mouse button to select it, and then, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>while holding down the Ctrl key or the Command and Option keys, click the mouse button again\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\> click the right mouse button\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. Some context menus can be called even if the object has not been selected. Context menus are found just about everywhere in $[officename].\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180	24			0	uk	Видалити				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750	25			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected element or elements after confirmation.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147557	45			0	uk	Видалити				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338	46			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected element or elements without requiring confirmation.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148620	6			0	uk	Метрика				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	7			0	uk	В поля вводу можна вводить значення у різних одиницях виміру. Типово використовуються дюйм. Проте якщо потрібен інтервал рівно 1 см, введіть "1 см". Додаткові одиниці виміру доступні відповідно до контексту, наприклад 12 пт для інтервалу 12 пунктів. Якщо значення нової одиниці виміру є нереальним, програма буде використовувати попередньо визначене максимальне чи мінімальне значення.				20220827 09:49:47
