helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154926	17			0	uk	The exceptions that you define depend on the current language setting. If you want, you can change the language setting by selecting a different language in the \<emph\>Replacements and exceptions for language\</emph\> box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149205	15			0	uk	Replacements and exceptions for language:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027	16			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AUTOCORR_LANGUAGE\"\>Select the language for which you want to create or edit the replacement rules.\</ahelp\> $[officename] first searches for exceptions that are defined for the language at the current cursor position in the document, and then searches the remaining languages.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153681	3			0	uk	Abbreviations (no subsequent capital)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	4			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:EDIT:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:ED_ABBREV\"\>Type an abbreviation followed by a period, and then click \<emph\>New\</emph\>. This prevents $[officename] from automatically capitalizing the first letter of the word that comes after the period at the end of the abbreviation.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149751	13			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:LISTBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:LB_ABBREV\"\>Lists the abbreviations that are not automatically corrected.\</ahelp\> To remove an item from the list, select the item, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
