helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Number Format Codes				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153514				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>format codes; numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditions; in number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats; codes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;of currencies/date/time\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; date, time and currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Euro; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>times, formats\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153514	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"zahlenformatcodes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020301.xhp\" name=\"Number Format Codes\"\>Number Format Codes\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150467	88			0	uk	Number format codes can consist of up to three sections separated by a semicolon (;).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150146	108			0	uk	In a number format code with two sections, the first section applies to positive values and zero, and the second section applies to negative values.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3158442	109			0	uk	In a number format code with three sections, the first section applies to positive values, the second section to negative values, and the third section to the value zero.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3155069	110			0	uk	You can also assign conditions to the three sections, so that the format is only applied if a condition is met.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151262	229			0	uk	Decimal Places and Significant Digits				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153624	3			0	uk	Use zero (0) or the number sign (#) as placeholders in your number format code to represent numbers. The (#) only displays significant digits, while the (0) displays zeroes if there are fewer digits in the number than in the number format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153323	107			0	uk	Use question marks (?) to represent the number of digits to include in the numerator and the denominator of a fraction. Fractions that do not fit the pattern that you define are displayed as floating point numbers.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148440	4			0	uk	If a number contains more digits to the right of the decimal delimiter than there are placeholders in the format, the number is rounded accordingly. If a number contains more digits to the left of the decimal delimiter than there are placeholders in the format, the entire number is displayed. Use the following list as a guide for using placeholders when you create a number format code:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150902	86			0	uk	Placeholders				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3157896	87			0	uk	Explanation				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801	5			0	uk	#				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	6			0	uk	Does not display extra zeros.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	7			0	uk	0 (Zero)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774	8			0	uk	Displays extra zeros if the number has less places than zeros in the format.				20220827 09:49:47
