helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	22			0	uk	When you import an HTML containing these META tags, the contents of the tags are added to the corresponding $[officename] file property box. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id0926200812164481				0	uk	Keywords must be separated by commas. A keyword can contain white space characters or semicolons.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163822	12			0	uk	Import Tips				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155307	13			0	uk	When you import an HTML document, following META tags are automatically converted to $[officename] fields: <META HTTP-EQUIV="REFRESH"...> and <META NAME="..." ...> , where NAME equals to AUTHOR, CREATED, CHANGED, CHANGEDBY, DESCRIPTION, KEYWORDS or CLASSIFICATION.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3146146	15			0	uk	Scripts, comments, and META tags that are positioned directly before a TABLE tag are inserted in the first cell of the table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366	16			0	uk	Scripts and META tags in the header of an HTML document are imported and anchored to the first paragraph in the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885	14			0	uk	To set the options for importing HTML tags, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>. A known META tag contains either "HTTP-EQUIV" or "NAME", and are imported as $[officename] comments. The only exception is <META NAME="GENERATOR"...>, which is ignored.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163717	17			0	uk	Export Tips				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159180	19			0	uk	Comments and script fields at the beginning of the first paragraph in a document are exported to the header of an HTML document. If the document begins with a table, the first paragraph in the first cell of the table is exported to the header of the HTML document.				20220827 09:49:47
