helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154873	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/03110000.xhp\" name=\"Increase Spacing\"\>Increase Spacing\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156211	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ParaspaceIncrease\"\>Click the\<emph\> Increase Spacing \</emph\>icon to increase the paragraph spacing above the selected paragraph.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150178				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3152425\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_paraspaceincrease.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152425\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156411	3			0	uk	Increase Spacing				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\03110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391	4			0	uk	You can make additional adjustments to the spacing by selecting \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\"\>\<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</emph\>\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Special properties of a formatted field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>formatted fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774	131			0	uk	Special properties of a formatted field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	127			0	uk	\<emph\>Formatting\</emph\>: You can set the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>property by clicking the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button in the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> line of the \<emph\>Properties: Formatted Field\</emph\> dialog. The \<emph\>Number Format\</emph\> dialog appears.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443	128			0	uk	If the formatted field is connected to the text field of a database, the entries in this field will be treated as text. If the formatted field is connected to a field of the database that can be displayed as a number, the input is treated as numbers. The date and time are also handled internally as numbers.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150976	129			0	uk	\<emph\>Min. value\</emph\> and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>: You can enter the minimum and maximum numeric value for a formatted field. The min and max values determine the output of existing data (Example: Min. value is 5, the connected database field contains the integer value 3. The output is 5, but the value in the database is not modified) and the input of new data (Example: Max. value is 10 and you enter 20. The input is corrected and 10 is written in the database). If the fields are not filled in for \<emph\>Min. value \</emph\>and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>, no limits will be applied. For formatted fields that are connected to a database text field, these two values and the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> do not apply.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665	130			0	uk	\<emph\>Default value\</emph\>: This value is set for new records as the default value.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Insert Database Columns				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147000	1			0	uk	Insert Database Columns				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SbaBrwInsert\"\>\<variable id=\"datenintext\"\>Inserts all fields of the marked record into the current document at the cursor position.\</variable\>\</ahelp\> The icon is only visible if the current document is a text document or a spreadsheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154186				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3147291\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbabrwinsert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147291\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	3			0	uk	Data to Text				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577	4			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>In the data source browser, select the record that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon. The record is inserted in the document at the cursor position, with the contents of each individual field of the record copied to a table column. You can also select multiple records and transfer them into the document by clicking the \<emph\>Data to Text \</emph\>icon. Each individual record is then written to a new row.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	5			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In the data source browser, select the records that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon, or drag-and-drop data from the data source browser into the document. This opens the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog. Select whether the data should be inserted as a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070100.xhp\" name=\"table\"\>table\</link\>, as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070200.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> or as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070300.xhp\" name=\"text\"\>text\</link\>.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	6			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The preferences you set in the\<emph\> Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog are saved and will be active the next time the dialog is called. This save process is independent of the database and can record the preferences for a maximum of 5 databases.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326	7			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If data is inserted into the document as a table, the table properties are not saved along with the data in the document. If you select the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> function for formatting the table, $[officename] will note the name of the format template. This template will then be used automatically if you insert data as a table again, unless the preferences have been changed.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Mail & News				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147102	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070200.xhp\" name=\"Mail News\"\>Mail & News\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049	2			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Mail & News\</emph\> page in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> you can edit hyperlinks for e-mail or news addresses.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153528	3			0	uk	Mail & News				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153748	4			0	uk	E-mail				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	5			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_MAIL_RB_LINKTYP_MAIL\"\>Assigns the specified e-mail address to the hyperlink.\</ahelp\> Clicking the new hyperlink in the document will open a new message document, addressed to the receiver specified in the \<emph\>E-mail\</emph\> field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628	6			0	uk	News				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149955	7			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_MAIL_RB_LINKTYP_NEWS\"\>Assigns a news address to the hyperlink.\</ahelp\> Clicking the hyperlink in the document will open a new message document to the news group you entered in the \<emph\>Receiver\</emph\> field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149580	8			0	uk	Receiver				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665	9			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HYPERDLG_MAIL_PATH\"\>Specifies the full URL of the addressee, in the form mailto:name@provider.com or news:group.server.com.\</ahelp\> You can also use drag-and-drop.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143270	14			0	uk	Data Sources				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514	15			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_IMAGEBUTTON_RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_MAIL_BTN_ADRESSBOOK\"\>Hides or shows the data source browser.\</ahelp\> Drag the receiver's \<emph\>E-mail\</emph\> data field from the data source browser into the \<emph\>Receiver\</emph\> text field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153332	12			0	uk	Subject				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821	13			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_EDIT_RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_MAIL_ED_SUBJECT\"\>Specifies the subject that is inserted in the subject line of the new message document.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Events				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150499				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>forms; events\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>events;in forms\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170202.xhp\" name=\"Events\"\>Events\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3147043	2			0	uk	The \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab page, allows you to assign a macro to certain events which occur in a form.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	3			0	uk	To link an event with a macro, first write a macro that contains all the commands to be executed when the event happens. Then assign this macro to the respective event by clicking the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button beside the corresponding event. The \<emph\>Assign Macro\</emph\> dialog opens, where you can select the macro.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182	29			0	uk	The following actions can be configured individually, meaning that you can use your own dialogs to depict an action:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	30			0	uk	Displaying an error message,				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	31			0	uk	Confirming a delete process (for data records),				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541	32			0	uk	Querying parameters,				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3155261	33			0	uk	Checking input when saving a data record.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127	34			0	uk	For example, you can issue a "confirm deletion" request such as "Really delete customer xyz?" when deleting a data record.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200920562590				0	uk	The events that are shown in the Events dialog cannot be edited directly. You can delete an event from the list by pressing the Del key.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986	4			0	uk	The following lists and describes all events in a form that can be linked to a macro:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559	17			0	uk	Before update				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	56			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Before update event occurs before the control content changed by the user is written into the data source.\</ahelp\> The linked macro can, for example, prevent this action by returning "FALSE".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153779	19			0	uk	After update				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360	57			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_AFTERUPDATE\"\>The After update event occurs after the control content changed by the user has been written into the data source.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157909	36			0	uk	Prior to reset				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3155390	51			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVERESETTED\"\>The\<emph\> Prior to reset \</emph\>event occurs before a form is reset.\</ahelp\> The linked macro can, for example, prevent this action by returning "FALSE".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236	52			0	uk	A form is reset if one of the following conditions is met:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164	53			0	uk	The user presses an (HTML) button that is defined as a reset button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666	54			0	uk	A new and empty record is created in a form that is linked to a data source. For example, in the last record, the \<emph\>Next Record\</emph\> button may be pressed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156119	37			0	uk	After resetting				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563	55			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_RESETTED\"\>The\<emph\> After resetting \</emph\>event occurs after a form has been reset.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870	27			0	uk	Before submitting				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152	28			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_SUBMITTED\"\>The\<emph\> Before submitting \</emph\>event occurs before the form data is sent.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149167	5			0	uk	When loading				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423	6			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_LOADED\"\>The\<emph\> When loading \</emph\>event occurs directly after the form has been loaded.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148451	38			0	uk	Before reloading				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154218	39			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_RELOADING\"\>The\<emph\> Before reloading \</emph\>event occurs before the form is reloaded.\</ahelp\> The data content has not yet been refreshed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155102	40			0	uk	When reloading				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3157895	41			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_RELOADED\"\>The\<emph\> When reloading \</emph\>event occurs directly after the form has been reloaded.\</ahelp\> The data content has already been refreshed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152792	42			0	uk	Before unloading				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152598	43			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_UNLOADING\"\>The\<emph\> Before unloading \</emph\>event occurs before the form is unloaded; that is, separated from its data source.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154145	44			0	uk	When unloading				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638	45			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_UNLOADED\"\>The\<emph\> When unloading \</emph\>event occurs directly after the form has been unloaded; that is, separated from its data source.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147426	25			0	uk	Confirm deletion				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154988	26			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_CONFIRMDELETE\"\>The\<emph\> Confirm deletion \</emph\>event occurs as soon as data has been deleted from the form.\</ahelp\> For example, the linked macro can request confirmation in a dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149481	46			0	uk	Before record action				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156007	58			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVEROWCHANGE\"\>The\<emph\> Before record action \</emph\>event occurs before the current record is changed.\</ahelp\> For example, the linked macro can request confirmation in a dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145749	47			0	uk	After record action				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	59			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ROWCHANGE\"\>The\<emph\> After record action \</emph\>event occurs directly after the current record has been changed.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154012	48			0	uk	Before record change				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	60			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_POSITIONING\"\>The\<emph\> Before record change \</emph\>event occurs before the current record pointer is changed.\</ahelp\> For example, the linked macro can prevent this action by returning "FALSE".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157975	49			0	uk	After record change				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098	61			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_POSITIONED\"\>The\<emph\> After record change \</emph\>event occurs directly after the current record pointer has been changed.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151076	50			0	uk	Fill parameters				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	62			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVEPARAMETER\"\>The \<emph\>Fill parameters\</emph\> event occurs when the form to be loaded has parameters that must be filled out.\</ahelp\> For example, the data source of the form can be the following SQL command:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148773	63			0	uk	SELECT * FROM address WHERE name=:name				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149581	64			0	uk	Here :name is a parameter that must be filled out when loading. The parameter is automatically filled out from the parent form if possible. If the parameter cannot be filled out, this event is called and a linked macro can fill out the parameter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146926	9			0	uk	Error occurred				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485	10			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ERROROCCURED\"\>The\<emph\> Error occurred \</emph\>event is activated if an error occurs when accessing the data source.\</ahelp\> This applies to forms, list boxes and combo boxes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Apply Filter				20220827 09:49:47
