helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149119	20			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170903.xhp\" name=\"List Box Wizard: Field Link\"\>List Box Wizard: Field Link\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3159224	15			0	uk	Indicates through which fields tables of values and list tables are linked.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499	27			0	uk	The value table is the table of the current form where the list field is inserted. The list table is the table whose data is to be shown in the list field. Both tables must be linked over a mutual data field. These links are to be entered on this page of the wizard. The field names must not necessarily be the same (this depends upon how the field names are defined in both tables), but both fields must have the same field type.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180	16			0	uk	Value table field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789	17			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_COMBOBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_FIELDLINK_CMB_VALUELISTFIELD\"\>Specifies the current form data field which should be related to a field in the linked table.\</ahelp\> In addition, click the desired data field in the list field below.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3145669	25			0	uk	In \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control - Properties\"\>Control - Properties\</link\>, the specified field will appear as an entry in the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827	18			0	uk	List table field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391	19			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_COMBOBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_FIELDLINK_CMB_TABLEFIELD\"\>Specifies the linked table data field, which is related to the specified value table field.\</ahelp\> In addition, click the data field in the lower list field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	26			0	uk	In \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control - Properties\"\>Control - Properties\</link\>, the specified field will appear in the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page of a SQL statement under \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Run SQL command directly				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/14030000.xhp\" name=\"Run SQL command directly\"\>Run SQL command directly\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155364	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SbaNativeSql\"\>In Native SQL mode you can enter SQL commands that are not interpreted by $[officename], but are instead passed directly to the data source.\</ahelp\> If you do not display these changes in the design view, you cannot change back to the design view.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149999	5			0	uk	For native SQL, the SQL string is forwarded directly to the connected database system without a previous evaluation by $[officename]. For example, if you access a database through an ODBC interface, the SQL string is passed to the ODBC driver and processed by it.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3147226\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbanativesql.png\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147226\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155893	4			0	uk	Run SQL command directly				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535	3			0	uk	Click the icon again to return to normal mode, in which the changes in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"New Query Design\"\>New Query Design\</link\> are synchronized with the permitted changes through SQL.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Text running from left to right				20220827 09:49:47
