helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Setting Tabs				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148668	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/13010000.xhp\" name=\"Setting Tabs\"\>Setting Tabs\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873	2			0	uk	On the ruler, set the tabs for the current paragraph, or all selected paragraphs, using the mouse.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148520	3			0	uk	Initially the default tabs are shown on the horizontal ruler. Once you set a tab, only the default tabs to the right of the tab that you have set are available.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	General				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152551				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>submitting forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>get method for form transmissions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>post method for form transmissions\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>General\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539	23			0	uk	A form is a text document or spreadsheet with different form controls. If you create a form for a Web page, the user can enter data into it to send over the Internet. The data from the form controls of a form is transmitted to a server by specifying a URL and can be processed on the server.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149283	20			0	uk	Name				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789	24			0	uk	Specifies a name for the form. This name is used to identify the form in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152425	33			0	uk	URL				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226	34			0	uk	Specifies the URL to which the data of the completed form is to be transmitted.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154751	31			0	uk	Frame				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	32			0	uk	Defines the target frame in which the loaded URL is to appear.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152551	27			0	uk	Type of submission				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338	28			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SUBMIT_METHOD\"\>Specifies the method to transfer the completed form information.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145065	29			0	uk	Using the "Get" method, the data of every control is transmitted as an environment variable. They are appended to the URL in the form "?Control1=Content1&Control2=Content2&..."; the character string is analyzed by a program on the recipient's server.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443	30			0	uk	Using the "Post" method, a document is created from the content of the form that is sent to the specified URL.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275	26			0	uk	Submission encoding				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147	35			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SUBMIT_ENCODING\"\>Specifies the type for encoding the data transfer.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419	36			0	uk	Data transfer of control information				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153717	37			0	uk	When sending a form, all controls available in $[officename] are taken into consideration. The name of the control and the corresponding value, if available, are transmitted.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252	50			0	uk	Which values are transmitted in each case depends on the respective control. For text fields, the visible entries are transmitted; for list boxes, the selected entries are transmitted; for check boxes and option fields, the associated reference values are transmitted if these fields were activated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984	51			0	uk	How this information is transmitted depends on the selected transfer method (Get or Post) and the coding (URL or Multipart). If the Get method and URL encoding are selected, for example, value pairs in the form <Name>=<Value> are sent.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3157909	52			0	uk	In addition to the controls that are recognized in HTML, $[officename] offers other controls. It should be noted that, for fields with a specific numerical format, the visible values are not transmitted but rather fixed default formats. The following table shows how the data of the $[officename]-specific controls is transmitted:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153698	38			0	uk	Control				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562	39			0	uk	Value Pair				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153823	40			0	uk	Numeric field, currency field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734	41			0	uk	A decimal separator is always displayed as a period.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563	42			0	uk	Date field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794	43			0	uk	The date format is sent in a fixed format (MM-DD-YYYY), regardless of the user's local settings.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	44			0	uk	Time field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153779	45			0	uk	The time format is sent in a fixed format (HH:MM:SS), regardless of the user's local settings.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361	46			0	uk	Pattern field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419	47			0	uk	The values of pattern fields are sent as text fields, that is, the value visible in the form is sent.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	48			0	uk	Table control				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933	49			0	uk	From the table control, the individual columns are always transmitted. The name of the control, the name of the column, and the value of the column are sent. Using the Get method with URL encoding, the transmission is done in the form <Name of the table control>.<Name of the column>=<Value>, for example, with the value being dependent on the column.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\basicshapes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Basic Shapes				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\basicshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10557				0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/basicshapes.xhp\"\>Basic Shapes\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\basicshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10567				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Basic Shapes toolbar which you can use to insert graphics into your document.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\basicshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10591				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click an icon on the Basic Shapes toolbar, and then drag in the document to draw the shape.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\basicshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10594				0	uk	Some shapes have a handle which you can drag to change the properties of the shape. The mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol over these special handles.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Print File Directly				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153539				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>printing; directly\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153539	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Print File Directly\"\>Print File Directly\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PrintDefault\"\>Click the \<emph\>Print File Directly\</emph\> icon to print the active document with the current default print settings.\</ahelp\> These can be found in the \<emph\>Printer Setup\</emph\> dialog, which you can call with the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Printer Settings\"\>\<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\>\</link\> menu command.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275	3			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If you select text or a graphic and click the \<emph\>Print File Direct\</emph\> icon, you are prompted to print the selection or the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id9547105				0	uk	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer for your operating system, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10679				0	uk	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer that was specified in the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\"\>spadmin\</link\>, printer administration program, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Internet URLs				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154094	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/09020000.xhp\" name=\"Internet URLs\"\>Internet URLs\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFA_HYPERLINK_URL\"\>Allows you to either type a URL, or insert a URL from a document using drag-and-drop.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153894	5			0	uk	You can edit the URL and insert it at the current cursor position in the active document with the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> icon. The \<emph\>Link\</emph\> icon can only be activated if the \<emph\>URL Name\</emph\> field contains text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Insert Mode				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149748	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/20040000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Mode\"\>Insert Mode\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertMode\"\>Displays the current insert mode. You can toggle between INSRT = insert and OVER = overwrite.\</ahelp\>\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>This field is only active if the cursor is in the input line of the formula bar or in a cell. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154422	3			0	uk	Click in the field to toggle the modes (except in the $[officename] Basic IDE, where only the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> mode is active). If the cursor is positioned in a text document, you may also use the Insert key (if available on your keyboard) to toggle the modes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177	4			0	uk	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391	5			0	uk	\<emph\>Result\</emph\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149388	6			0	uk	INSRT				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147243	7			0	uk	In the insert mode, new text is inserted at the cursor position and the following text is shifted to the right. The cursor is displayed as a vertical line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539	8			0	uk	OVER				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156327	9			0	uk	In the overwrite mode, any existing text is replaced by new text. The cursor is displayed as a thick vertical line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Find Record				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146936				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; searching\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>forms; browsing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>records; searching in databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>searching; databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>databases; searching records\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146936	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"datensatzsuche\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"Find Record\"\>Find Record\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147588	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"suchentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RecSearch\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Searches database tables and forms.\</ahelp\> In forms or database tables, you can search through data fields, list boxes, and check boxes for specific values.\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355	3			0	uk	When searching a table, the data fields of the current table are searched. When searching in a form, the data fields of the table linked with the form are searched.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394	111			0	uk	The search described here is carried out by \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>. If you want to use the SQL server to search in a database, then you should use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12110000.xhp\" name=\"Form-based Filters\"\>Form-based Filters\</link\> icon on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Bar\"\>Form Bar\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095	110			0	uk	The search function is also available for table controls. When calling the search function from a table control, you can search each column of the table control corresponding to the database columns of the linked database table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267	112			0	uk	Search for				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	113			0	uk	Specifies the type of search.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153683	6			0	uk	Text:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	7			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORTEXT\"\>Enter the search term in the box or select it from the list.\</ahelp\> The text under the cursor is already copied into the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> combo box. Note that while running a search in a form, tabs and line breaks cannot be processed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539	8			0	uk	Your search terms will be saved as long as the table or the formula document is open. If you are running more than one search and you would like to repeat the search term, you can select a previously used search term from the combo box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662	114			0	uk	Field content is NULL				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153543	115			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORNULL\"\>Specifies that fields will be found that contain no data.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153717	116			0	uk	Field content is not NULL				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270	117			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORNOTNULL\"\>Specifies that fields will be found that contain data.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156153	9			0	uk	Where to search				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164	10			0	uk	Specifies the fields for the search.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154564	105			0	uk	Form				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176	106			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_LB_FORM\"\>Specifies the logical form in which you want the search to take place.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155434	107			0	uk	The\<emph\> Form \</emph\>combo box is only visible if the current document is a form document with more than one logical form. It does not appear during a search in tables or queries.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384	108			0	uk	Form documents may contain multiple logical forms. These are individual form components, which are each linked to a table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086	109			0	uk	The \<emph\>Form\</emph\> combo box contains the names of all logical forms for which controls exist.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159414	11			0	uk	All Fields				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896	12			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_ALLFIELDS\"\>Searches through all fields.\</ahelp\> If you are running a search in a table, all fields in the table will be searched. If you are running a search in a form, all fields of the logical form (entered under \<emph\>Form\</emph\>) will be searched. If you are running a search in a table control field, all columns that are linked to a valid database table field will be searched.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054	13			0	uk	Note that the fields of the current logical form do not have to be identical to the fields of the form document. If the form document contains fields that point to multiple data sources (that is, multiple logical forms), the \<emph\>All Fields\</emph\> option will only search for the fields linked to data sources in the form document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150865	15			0	uk	Single field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360	16			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SINGLEFIELD\"\>Searches through a specified data field.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154365	17			0	uk	Settings				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158408	18			0	uk	Defines settings to control the search.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149809	19			0	uk	Position				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673	20			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_POSITION\"\>Specifies the relationship of the search term and the field contents.\</ahelp\> The following options are available:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280	21			0	uk	anywhere in the field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145744	22			0	uk	Returns all fields containing the search pattern anywhere in the field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451	23			0	uk	beginning of field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429	24			0	uk	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the beginning of the field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131	74			0	uk	end of field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	75			0	uk	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the end of the field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317	25			0	uk	entire field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127	26			0	uk	Returns all fields containing the search pattern as an exact match to the contents of the field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886	27			0	uk	If the \<emph\>Wildcard expression\</emph\> check box is marked, this function is not available.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664	28			0	uk	Apply field format				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	29			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_FORMATTER\"\>Specifies that all field formats are considered when searching in the current document.\</ahelp\> Field formats are all visible formats that are created using the following possibilities:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103	78			0	uk	in table design mode for field properties,				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488	79			0	uk	in data source view on column formatting,				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152941	80			0	uk	in forms on control properties.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156736	81			0	uk	If the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> box is marked, the data source view of the table or form is searched using the formatting set there. If the box is not marked, the database is searched using the formatting saved in the database.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151280	82			0	uk	Example:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959	83			0	uk	You have a date field, which is saved in "DD.MM.YY" format in the database (for example, 17.02.65). The format of the entry is changed in the data source view to "DD MMM YYYY" (17 Feb 1965). Following this example, a record containing February 17 is only found when the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> option is on:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150593	84			0	uk	Apply field format				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145253	85			0	uk	Search pattern				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3083279	86			0	uk	on				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155850	87			0	uk	"Feb" is returned, but not "2".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148590	88			0	uk	off				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418	89			0	uk	"2" is returned, but not "Feb".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151321	90			0	uk	It is recommended that you always search using field formatting.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401	91			0	uk	The following examples show possible issues when searching without field formatting. These issues depend on the database used and only occur for certain internal default formatting:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971	92			0	uk	Search results				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154273	93			0	uk	Cause				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153836	94			0	uk	"5" returns "14:00:00" as a time				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156332	95			0	uk	Time fields are not defined for dBASE databases and must be simulated. To internally display the time "14:00:00", a 5 is necessary.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3157965	96			0	uk	"00:00:00" returns all records of a standard date field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146081	97			0	uk	The database stores a date value internally using a combined date/time field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	98			0	uk	"45.79" does not return "45.79" although the \<emph\>entire field\</emph\> option is selected under \<emph\>Position\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155518	99			0	uk	The view shown does not match what is stored internally. For example, if value 45.789 is stored in the database as a field of type Number/Double and the shown formatting is set to display only two decimals, "45.79" is only returned in searches with field formatting.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148481	100			0	uk	In this case, standard formatting is formatting that refers to the internally stored data. It is not always visible to the user, especially if it is used for simulating data types (for example, time fields in dBASE databases). This depends on the database used and the individual data type. Searching with field formatting is appropriate if you only want to find what is actually shown. This includes fields of type Date, Time, Date/Time and Number/Double.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507	31			0	uk	However, searching without \<emph\>Apply field format \</emph\>is appropriate for larger databases with no formatting issues, because it is faster.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153355	118			0	uk	If you are searching the values of check boxes, and \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> is on, then you will receive a "1" for marked check boxes, a "0" for unmarked check boxes, and an empty string for undefined (tristate) check boxes. If the search has been carried out with \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> set to off, you will see the language-dependent default values "TRUE" or "FALSE".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150995	119			0	uk	If you use \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> when searching in list boxes, you find the text displayed in list boxes. If you do not use \<emph\>Apply field format,\</emph\> you will find the contents corresponding to the standard field format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150387	32			0	uk	Match case				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267	33			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_CASE\"\>Specifies that upper and lower case are taken into consideration during the search.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145297	34			0	uk	Search backwards				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151249	35			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BACKWARD\"\>Specifies that the search process will run in reverse direction, from the last to the first record.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152484	36			0	uk	From top / From bottom				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316	37			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_STARTOVER\"\>Restarts the search. A forward search restarts with the first record. A backwards search restarts with the last record.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163724	38			0	uk	Wildcard expression				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255	64			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_WILDCARD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Allows a search with a * or ? wildcard.\</ahelp\> You can use the following wildcards:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146317	39			0	uk	Wildcards				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150298	40			0	uk	Meaning				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919	41			0	uk	Example				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158411	42			0	uk	?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874	43			0	uk	for exactly one arbitrary character				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365	44			0	uk	"?loppy" returns "Floppy"				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426	65			0	uk	"M?ller" returns, for example, Miller and Moller				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148803	45			0	uk	*				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156138	46			0	uk	for 0 or more arbitrary characters				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135	47			0	uk	"*-*" returns "ZIP-Drive" and "CD-ROM"				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582	66			0	uk	"M*er" returns all entries starting with an "M" and ending in "er" (for example, Miller, Moller, Mather)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145762	48			0	uk	If you want to search for the actual characters ? or *, preface them with a backslash: "\\?" or "\\*". However, this is only necessary when \<emph\>Wildcard expression\</emph\> is enabled. When the option is not enabled, the wildcard characters are processed like normal characters.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147130	49			0	uk	Regular expression				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982	50			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_REGULAR\"\>Searches with regular expressions.\</ahelp\> The same regular expressions that are supported here are also supported in the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Find & Replace dialog\"\>Find & Replace dialog\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154718	67			0	uk	Searching with regular expressions offers more options than searching with wildcard expressions. If you search with regular expressions, the following characters correspond to those used in searches with wildcards:				20220827 09:49:47
