helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147588	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/07070200.xhp\" name=\"Save Record\"\>Save Record\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07070200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163829				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>records; saving\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163829	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Saves the current database table record.\</ahelp\> The\<emph\> Save Record \</emph\>icon is found on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0212.xhp\" name=\"Database Bar\"\>Table Data bar\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152372	3			0	uk	Changes to the contents of a record are automatically saved as soon as you select another record. To save changes without selecting another record, click the \<emph\>Save Record\</emph\> icon.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Fields				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149991	1			0	uk	Fields				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149987				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>database contents; inserting as fields\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149987	8			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_RB_AS_FIELD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts data selected from the data source browser into the document as fields.\</ahelp\>In the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog, select the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\> to insert the selected data into the document as fields. These \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090006.xhp\" name=\"database fields\"\>database fields\</link\> work as wildcards for the individual database columns and can be used for form letters. Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Data to Fields\"\>\<emph\>Data to Fields\</emph\>\</link\> icon to match the contents of the fields to the currently selected record.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114	9			0	uk	If several records are selected when you choose the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> function, the mail merge fields will be inserted according to the number of records. Also, a field command such as "Next record" will be inserted automatically between individual field command blocks.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	10			0	uk	The \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog lets you define which database fields to insert into the document and how to format the paragraphs.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136	2			0	uk	Fields				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571	11			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> area, use the arrow button to select the database table columns into which you want to insert field contents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345	3			0	uk	Database columns				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535	12			0	uk	Lists all columns of the database table, which can be accepted in the selection list box to insert them into the document. \<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_LB_TXT_DB_COLUMN\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Select the database columns that you want to insert it in the document.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152551	4			0	uk	>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	13			0	uk	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_TOEDIT\"\>Moves the fields that you selected in the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box into the selection field.\</ahelp\> You can also double-click the entry to select it.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166411	5			0	uk	Select				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802	14			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_MULTILINEEDIT_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_ED_DB_TEXT\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Lists the database columns that you selected to be inserted into the document. You can also enter text here. This text will be also inserted into the document.\</ahelp\> The entries' order in the selection field corresponds to the data order in the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153257	7			0	uk	Paragraph Style				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430	15			0	uk	By default, the inserted paragraphs are formatted with the current Paragraph Styles. This format corresponds to the "none" entry in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> list box. \<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_LB_DB_PARA_COLL\" visibility=\"visible\"\>This is where you can select other Paragraph Styles to apply to the paragraph you want to insert into the document.\</ahelp\> The list box displays the available Paragraph Styles defined in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> and managed in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Style Catalog\"\>Style Catalog\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
