helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144436				0	uk	\<image src=\"res/sc10714.png\" id=\"img_id3153894\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153894\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147143	3			0	uk	Sort Order				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	HTML Filters and Forms				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163829				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>forms; HTML filters\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163829	1			0	uk	HTML Filters and Forms				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147285	2			0	uk	You can use all control elements and form events in HTML documents. There have been numerous events to date (for example, focus events), which have not been changed. They will continue to be imported and exported as ONFOCUS, ONBLUR, and so on for JavaScript and as SDONFOCUS, SDONBLUR, and so on for $[officename] Basic.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3150616	3			0	uk	Generic names that consist of the Listener interface and the method name of the event are used for all other events: An event registered as XListener::method is exported as				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571	4			0	uk	SDEvent-XListener-method = "/* event-code */"				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425	5			0	uk	Note that the XListener- and method components of this option are case sensitive.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3153683	6			0	uk	Event handling of controls is performed using the $[officename] API. If you assign an event to a control, an object registers itself internally as a "Listener" for a specific control event. To do this, the object must use a specific interface, for example the XFocusListener Interface, so that it can react to focus events. When the event occurs, the control then invokes a special method of the Listener interface when the control receives the focus. The internally registered object then invokes the JavaScript or $[officename] Basic code, which was assigned to the event.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	7			0	uk	The HTML filter now uses precisely these listener interfaces and method names so that it can import and export events as desired. You can register a focus event through				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3150506	8			0	uk	<INPUT TYPE=text ONFOCUS="/* code */"				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154289	9			0	uk	rather than through the				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391	10			0	uk	<INPUT TYPE=text SDEvent-XFocusListener-focusGained="/* code */"				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	11			0	uk	register. Events can therefore be registered as desired, including those not offered in the list boxes. To define the script language of events, you can write the following line in the document header:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443	12			0	uk	<META HTTP-EQUIV="content-script-type" CONTENT="...">				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	13			0	uk	As CONTENT you can, for example, use "text/x-StarBasic" for $[officename] Basic or a "text/JavaScript" for JavaScript. If no entry is made, JavaScript is assumed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797	14			0	uk	During exporting, the default script language will be defined based on the first module found in macro management. For events, only one language can be used per document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Graphics Mode				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149762	1			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24020000.xhp\" name=\"Graphics Mode\"\>Graphics Mode\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150255	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:GrafMode\"\>Lists view attributes for the selected graphic object. The embedded or linked graphic object in the current file will not be changed, only the view of the object.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3154515\" src=\"res/helpimg/zellvor.png\" width=\"1.528in\" height=\"0.292in\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154515\"\>Cell Styles\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771	3			0	uk	Graphics mode				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155262	4			0	uk	Default				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155434	5			0	uk	The view of the graphic object is not changed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574	6			0	uk	Grayscale				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153760	7			0	uk	The graphic object is shown in grayscale. A color graphic object can become monochrome in grayscale. You can also use the color sliders to apply a uniform color to the monochrome graphic object.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151246	8			0	uk	Black and White				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062	9			0	uk	The graphic object is shown in black and white. All brightness values below 50% will appear black, all over 50% will appear white.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146795	10			0	uk	Watermark				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	11			0	uk	The graphic object is raised in brightness and reduced in contrast so that it can be used in the background as a watermark. 				20220827 09:49:47
