helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151378	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"formulartext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Config\"\>The Form Controls toolbar contains tools that you need to create an interactive form.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can use the toolbar to add controls to a form in a text, spreadsheet, presentation, or HTML document, for example a button that runs a macro.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200809391346				0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336	68			0	uk	Icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar (you may need to enable this initially invisible icon):				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155341				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3150943\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_config.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150943\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	3			0	uk	Form Controls				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B21				0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xforms.xhp\"\>XML Form documents\</link\> (XForms) use the same controls.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152771	45			0	uk	To create a form, open a document and use the Form Controls toolbar to add and define the form controls. If you want, you can also link the form to a database, so that you can use the controls to manipulate a database.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150791	46			0	uk	When you create a form in an HTML document, you can use the form to send data over the Internet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171	47			0	uk	%PRODUCTNAME only exports the form properties that are supported by the HTML version that you export to. To specify the HTML version, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C39				0	uk	To add a control to a document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154918	4			0	uk	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the icon of the control that you want to add.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C4D				0	uk	In the document, drag to create the control. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C50				0	uk	To create a square control field, hold down the Shift key while you drag.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127	78			0	uk	To add a field from the field list of a table or query to a form, drag a cell into the form. In a text document, you can also drag a column header to add a field to a form. To include a label for the field, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift key down when you drag a column head.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C87				0	uk	Modifying a Control				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645	5			0	uk	Right-click the control and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>. A dialog opens where you can define the properties of the control.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363	163			0	uk	To specify a accelerator key for a control, add a tilde (~) in front of the character in the label for the control.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152792	135			0	uk	You can drag and drop controls from one document to another document. You can also copy and paste controls between documents. When you insert a control from another document, $[officename] analyzes the data source, content type, and content properties of the control so that the control fits the logical structure in the target document. For example, a control that displays contents from an address book continues to display the same contents after you copy the control to a different document. You can view these properties on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page of the \<emph\>Form properties\</emph\> dialog. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154411	24			0	uk	Select				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156106				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3153516\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153516\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150470	25			0	uk	This icon switches the mouse pointer to the select mode, or deactivates this mode. The select mode is used to select the controls of the current form.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146914	10			0	uk	Check Box				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148483				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3156380\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_checkbox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156380\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153927	11			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CheckBox\"\>Creates a check box.\</ahelp\> Check boxes allow you to activate or deactivate a function in a form.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153794	16			0	uk	Text Box				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3163665				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3153266\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_edit.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153266\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444	17			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Edit\"\>Creates a text box.\</ahelp\> Text boxes are fields in which the user can enter text. In a form, text boxes display data or allow for new data input.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151218	124			0	uk	Formatted Field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154836				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3143277\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formattedfield.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3143277\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147547	125			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormattedField\"\>Creates a formatted field.\</ahelp\> A formatted field is a text box in which you can define how the inputs and outputs are formatted, and which limiting values apply.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155346	126			0	uk	A formatted field has \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170002.xhp\" name=\"special control properties\"\>special control properties\</link\> (choose \<emph\>Format - Control\</emph\>).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148774	6			0	uk	Push Button				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3151073\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertpushbutton.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151073\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147046	7			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Pushbutton\"\>Creates a push button.\</ahelp\> This function can be used to execute a command for a defined event, such as a mouse click.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731	138			0	uk	You can apply text and graphics to these buttons.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157844	8			0	uk	Option Button				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3152999\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_radiobutton.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152999\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123	9			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RadioButton\"\>Creates an option button.\</ahelp\> Option buttons enable the user to choose one of several options. Option buttons with the same functionality are given the same name (\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"Name\"\>\<emph\>Name\</emph\>\</link\>\<emph\>property\</emph\>). Normally, they are given a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"group box\"\>group box\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156064	18			0	uk	List Box				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154326				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3154135\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_listbox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154135\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428	19			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ListBox\"\>Creates a list box.\</ahelp\> A list box lets users select an entry from a list. If the form is linked to a database and the database connection is active, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"List Box Wizard\"\>\<emph\>List Box Wizard\</emph\>\</link\> will automatically appear after the list box is inserted in the document. This wizard helps you create the list box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147171	20			0	uk	Combo Box				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3148817\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_combobox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148817\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149407	21			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ComboBox\"\>Creates a combo box.\</ahelp\> A combo box is a single-line list box with a drop-down list from which users choose an option. You can assign the "read-only" property to the combo box so that users cannot enter other entries than those found in the list. If the form is bound to a database and the database connection is active, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box Wizard\"\>\<emph\>Combo Box Wizard\</emph\>\</link\> will automatically appear after you insert the combo box in the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145618	12			0	uk	Label Field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145295				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3151017\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertfixedtext.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151017\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534	13			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Label\"\>Creates a field for displaying text.\</ahelp\> These labels are only for displaying predefined text. Entries cannot be made in these fields.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	uk	More Controls				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CDC				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/more_controls.xhp\"\>\<emph\>More Controls\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CF7				0	uk	Form Design				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D0D				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0226.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Form Design\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B57				0	uk	Wizards On/Off				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B65				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id6128727\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_usewizards.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6128727\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B76				0	uk	Turns on and turns off the automatic form controls wizards.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id6403088				0	uk	These wizards help you to enter the properties of list boxes, table controls, and other controls.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149436	134			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170001.xhp\" name=\"Context Menu Commands\"\>Context Menu Commands\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11A56				0	uk	Spin Button				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11A64				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id7816400\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_spinbutton.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7816400\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11A75				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SpinButton\"\>Creates a spin button.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id710776				0	uk	If you add a spin button to a Calc spreadsheet, you can use the Data tab page to create a two-way link between the spin button and a cell. As a result, when you change the contents of a cell, the contents of the spin button are updated. Conversely, if you change the value of the spin button, the contents of the cell are updated.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11ABC				0	uk	Scrollbar				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11ACA				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id8203985\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_scrollbar.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8203985\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11ADB				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ScrollBar\"\>Creates a scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CA3				0	uk	You can specify the following properties for a scrollbar:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CDA				0	uk	UI name				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CE0				0	uk	Semantics				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CE7				0	uk	Scroll value min				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CED				0	uk	Specifies the minimum height or the minimum width of a scrollbar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CF4				0	uk	Scroll value max				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CFA				0	uk	Specifies the maximum height or the maximum width of a scrollbar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D01				0	uk	Default scroll value				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D07				0	uk	Specifies the default value of a scrollbar, used when the form is reset.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D0E				0	uk	Orientation				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D14				0	uk	Specifies the orientation of a scrollbar, that is, horizontal or vertical.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D1B				0	uk	Small change				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D21				0	uk	Specifies the minimum amount by which you can scroll a scrollbar, for example, by clicking an arrow.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D28				0	uk	Large change				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D2E				0	uk	Specifies the amount that a large step scrolls a scrollbar, for example, when you click between the scrollbar thumb and a scrollbar arrow.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D35				0	uk	Delay				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D3B				0	uk	Specifies the delay in milliseconds between scrollbar trigger events. For example, the delay that occurs when you click an arrow button on the scrollbar and hold down the mouse button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D42				0	uk	Symbol color				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D48				0	uk	Specifies the color of the arrows on the scrollbar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D4F				0	uk	Visible Size				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D55				0	uk	Specifies the size of the scrollbar thumb in "value units". For example, a value of ("Scroll value max." minus "Scroll value min.") / 2 results in a scrollbar thumb that occupies half of the scrollbar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D58				0	uk	To make the width of the scrollbar equal to the height of the scrollbar, set the Visible Size to zero.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D63				0	uk	In a Calc spreadsheet, you can use the Data tab page to create a two-way link between a scrollbar and a cell.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153316	22			0	uk	Image Button				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159622				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3154378\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_imagebutton.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154378\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148601	23			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Imagebutton\"\>Creates a button displayed as an image.\</ahelp\> Aside from the graphic representation, an image button has the same properties as a "normal" button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159171	49			0	uk	Image Control				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155869				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3152381\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_imagecontrol.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152381\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149596	50			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ImageControl\"\>Creates an image control. It can only be used to add images from a database.\</ahelp\> In the form document, double-click one of these controls to open the \<emph\>Insert Graphic\</emph\> dialog to insert the image. There is also a context menu (not in design mode) with commands for inserting and deleting the image.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150318	70			0	uk	Images from a database can be displayed in a form, and new images can be inserted in the database as long as the image control is not write-protected. The control must refer to a database field of the image type. Therefore, enter the data field into the properties window on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156040	29			0	uk	Date Field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149423				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3150096\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_adddatefield.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150096\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151312	30			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DateField\"\>Creates a date field.\</ahelp\> If the form is linked to a database, the date values can be adopted from the database.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151302	131			0	uk	If you assign the "Dropdown" property to the date field, the user can open a calendar to select a date under the date field. This also applies to a date field within a Table Control field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154395	63			0	uk	Date fields can be easily edited by the user with the up arrow and down arrow keys. Depending on the cursor position, the day, month, or the year is can be increased or decreased using the arrow keys.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153112	132			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170003.xhp\" name=\"Specific Remarks on Date Fields\"\>Specific Remarks on Date Fields\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
