helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id4563127				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the default text for a text box or a combo box.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145206	144			0	uk	Default button				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154681	145			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_BUTTON\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The\<emph\> Default button\</emph\> property specifies that the corresponding button will be operated when you press the Return key.\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Default button\</emph\> property specifies that the corresponding button will be operated when you press the Return key. If you open the dialog or form and do not carry out any further action, the button with this property is the default button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149750	175			0	uk	This property should be assigned only to a single button within the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931	177			0	uk	When using Web page forms, you might come across this property in search masks. These are edit masks that contain a text field and a Submit type button. The search term is entered in the text field and the search is started by activating the button. If the button is defined as the default button, however, simply hit Enter after entering the search term in order to start the search.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153389	221			0	uk	Prefix symbol				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150271	222			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURRSYM_POSITION\"\>Determines if the currency symbol is displayed before or after the number when using currency fields.\</ahelp\> The default setting is currency symbols are not prefixed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154548	48			0	uk	Tabstop				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155361	49			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TABSTOP\"\>The \<emph\>Tabstop \</emph\>property determines if a control field can be selected with the tab key.\</ahelp\> The following options are available:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148627	52			0	uk	No				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3161673	53			0	uk	When using the tab key, focusing skips the control.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159323	50			0	uk	Yes				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584	51			0	uk	The control can be selected with the Tab key.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146909	147			0	uk	Thousands separator				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154936	148			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SHOWTHOUSANDSEP\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a thousands separator.\</ahelp\>With numerical and currency fields you can determine whether thousands separators are used.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156256	7			0	uk	Label				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156432	8			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LABEL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The Label property sets the label of the control field that is displayed in the form.\</ahelp\>The Label property sets the label of the control field that is displayed in the form. This property determines the visible label or the column header of the data field in table control forms.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154568	54			0	uk	When you create a new control, the description predefined in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> property is used as the default for labeling the control. The label consists of the control field name and an integer numbering the control (for example, CommandButton1). With the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> property, you can assign another description to the control so that the label reflects the function of the control. Change this entry in order to assign an expressive label to the control that is visible to the user.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163820				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>multi-line titles in forms\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>names; multi-line titles\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>controls; multi-line titles\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163820	223			0	uk	To create a multi-line title, open the combo box using the arrow button. You can enter a line break by pressing Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159407	55			0	uk	The \<emph\>Title\</emph\> property is only used for labeling a form element in the interface visible to the user. If you work with macros, note that at runtime, a control is always addressed through the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> property.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150293	56			0	uk	URL				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154358	57			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TARGET_URL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the URL address that opens when you click an "Open document / web page" button.\</ahelp\>Enter the URL address for a Open document or web page button type in the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> box. The address opens when you click the button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146074	211			0	uk	If you move the mouse over the button in User mode, the URL appears as the extended tip, provided that no other Help text was entered.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147134	149			0	uk	Currency symbol				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145160	150			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURRENCYSYMBOL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter a character or a string for the currency symbol.\</ahelp\>In a currency field, you can pre-define the currency symbol by entering the character or string in the \<emph\>Currency symbol\</emph\> property.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144444	154			0	uk	Value				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152417	155			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HIDDEN_VALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter the data that is inherited by the hidden control.\</ahelp\>In a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"hidden control\"\>hidden control\</link\>, under \<emph\>Value\</emph\>, you can enter the data which is inherited by the hidden control. This data will be transferred when sending the form.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157315	156			0	uk	Password characters				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155323	157			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ECHO_CHAR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If the text box is used as a password input, enter the ASCII-code of the display character. This character is displayed instead of the characters typed by the user for the password.\</ahelp\>If the user enters a password, you can determine the characters that will be displayed instead of the characters typed by the user. Under \<emph\>Password character\</emph\>, enter the ASCII code of the desired character. You can use the values from 0 to 255.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152493	158			0	uk	The characters and their ASCII codes can be seen in the \<emph\>Special Characters\</emph\> dialog (Insert - Special Character).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157884	159			0	uk	Literal mask				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3157557	160			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LITERALMASK\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the literal mask. The literal mask contains the initial values and is always visible after downloading a form.\</ahelp\>With masked fields you can specify a literal mask. A literal mask contains the initial values of a form, and is always visible after downloading a form. Using a character code for the Edit mask, you can determine the entries that the user can type into the masked field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148513	161			0	uk	The length of the literal mask should always correspond to the length of the edit mask. If this is not the case, the edit mask is either cut off or filled with blanks up to the length of the edit mask.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146762	5			0	uk	Font				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151037	6			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FONT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the font for the text that is in the control field.\</ahelp\>For control fields which have visible text or titles, select the display font that you want to use. To open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Font\"\>\<emph\>Font\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button. The selected font is used in control fields names and to display data in table control fields.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156734	162			0	uk	Row height				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3160455	163			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ROWHEIGHT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the row height of a table control field.\</ahelp\>In table controls, enter a value for the row height. If you want, you can enter a value followed by valid measurement unit, for example, 2 cm.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11FB6				0	uk	Text lines end with				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11FBA				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For text fields, select the line end code to be used when writing text into a database column.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160477	168			0	uk	Time format				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145187	169			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TIMEFORMAT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can define the desired format for the time display.\</ahelp\>You can define the desired format for the time display.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158195	170			0	uk	Help text				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146823	171			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TAG\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies additional information or a descriptive text for the control field.\</ahelp\>In each control field you can specify additional information or a descriptive text for the control field. This property helps the programmer to save additional information that can be used in the program code. This field can be used, for example, for variables or other evaluation parameters.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157828	232			0	uk	Formatting				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146843	233			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FORMATKEY\"\>Specifies the format code for the control. Click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to select the format code.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN122C4				0	uk	Scale				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN122C8				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SCALEIMAGE\"\>Resizes the image to fit the size of the control.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1209F				0	uk	Acting on a record				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120B1				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"37930\"\>Specifies to show or hide the action items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Action items are the following: Save record, Undo, New record, Delete record, Refresh.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120BE				0	uk	Positioning				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120D9				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"37928\"\>Specifies to show or hide the positioning items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Positioning items are the following: Record label, Record position, Record count label, Record count.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120D7				0	uk	Navigation				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120DB				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"37929\"\>Specifies to show or hide the navigation items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Navigation items are the following: First record, Previous record, Next record, Last record.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12156				0	uk	Filtering / Sorting				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1215A				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"37931\"\>Specifies to show or hide the filtering and sorting items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Filtering and sorting items are the following: Sort ascending, Sort descending, Sort, Automatic filter, Default filter, Apply filter, Remove filter/sort.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12175				0	uk	Icon Size				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12179				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"37927\"\>Specifies whether the icons in a selected Navigation Bar should be small or large.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0409200920593864				0	uk	Visible				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200920593851				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines whether the control will be visible in live mode. In design mode, the control is always visible.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154683				0	uk	Note that if this property is set to "Yes" (the default), this does not necessarily mean the control will really appear on the screen. Additional constraints are applied when calculating a control's effective visibility. For instance, a control placed in a hidden section in Writer will never be visible at all, until at least the section itself becomes visible.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154691				0	uk	If the property is set to "No", then the control will always be hidden in live mode.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154614				0	uk	Older OpenOffice.org versions up to 3.1 will silently ignore this property when reading documents which make use of it.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12314				0	uk	Visible size				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12318				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the size of scrollbar thumb in "value units". A value of ("Scroll value max." minus "Scroll value min." ) / 2 would result in a thumb which occupies half of the background area.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12375				0	uk	If set to 0, then the thumb's width will equal its height.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12332				0	uk	Orientation				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12336				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the horizontal or vertical orientation for a scrollbar or spin button.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
