helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Special Tips for Table Controls				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109850				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>table controls; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of table controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table controls;keyboard-only edit mode\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850	124			0	uk	Special Tips for Table Controls				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539	51			0	uk	You can define a table control to display the records as you like. In other words you can define data fields for displaying or editing data like in a database form.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152372	62			0	uk	The following fields are possible in a table control: text, date, time and currency field, numeric field, pattern field, check box and combo box. In the case of combined date/time fields, two columns are created automatically.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194	125			0	uk	The number of selected lines, if any are selected, is in parentheses after the total number of records.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155616	52			0	uk	To insert columns into the table control, click in the column heads and bring up the context menu. The following commands are available:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789	53			0	uk	Insert Column				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750	54			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_INSERTCOL\"\>Calls a submenu to select a data field to adopt it in the table control.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552	59			0	uk	Configure the table control using drag and drop: Open the data source browser and drag the desired fields out of the data source browser and on to the column heads of the table control. A pre-configured column is created.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827	55			0	uk	Replace with				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	56			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_CHANGECOL\"\>Opens a submenu to select a data field to replace the data field selected in the table control.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267	57			0	uk	Delete Column				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958	58			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETECOL\"\>Deletes the currently selected column.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275	73			0	uk	Column				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	74			0	uk	Opens the properties dialog of the selected column.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148539	79			0	uk	Hide Columns				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157	80			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_HIDECOL\"\>Hides the selected column.\</ahelp\> Its properties are not changed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771	81			0	uk	Show columns				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400	82			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS\"\>Calls a submenu where you can select the columns to show again.\</ahelp\> To show only one column, click the column name. You see only the first 16 hidden columns. If there are more hidden columns, choose the \<emph\>More\</emph\> command to call the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193	83			0	uk	More				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159269	84			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS_MORE\"\>Calls the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	85			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVX_DLG_SHOWGRIDCOLUMNS:1\"\>In the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog you can select the columns to be shown. Hold down the Shift or Ctrl (Mac: Command) key to select multiple entries.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561	86			0	uk	All				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	87			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWALLCOLS\"\>Click \<emph\>All \</emph\>if you want to show all columns.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153349	127			0	uk	Keyboard-only control of Table Controls				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149416	126			0	uk	If you use the keyboard only to travel through controls in your document, you will find one difference to the other types of controls: the Tab key does not move the cursor to the next control, but moves to the next column inside the table control. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the next control, or press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the previous control.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153062	128			0	uk	To enter the special keyboard-only edit mode for Table Controls:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510	129			0	uk	The form document must be in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"design mode\"\>design mode\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758	130			0	uk	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to select the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3161657	131			0	uk	Press Shift+F4 to select the first control. If the Table Control is not the first control, press Tab until it is selected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056	132			0	uk	Press Enter to enter the edit mode. The handles are shown farther out from the control border.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938	133			0	uk	In the edit mode, you can open the edit mode context menu by pressing Shift+F10.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365	134			0	uk	If you want to edit columns, press Shift+Space to enter column edit mode. Now you can rearrange the order of columns with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow keys. The Delete key deletes the current column.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419	135			0	uk	Press the Escape key to exit the edit mode.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Add Field				20220827 09:49:47
