helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"text\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AddField\"\>Opens a window where you can select a database field to add to the form or report.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114	3			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FIELD_SEL\"\>The field selection window lists all database fields of the table or query that was specified as the data source in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147620	4			0	uk	You can insert a field into the current document by dragging and dropping. A field is then inserted which contains a link to the database.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541	5			0	uk	If you add fields to a form and you switch off the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"Design Mode\"\>Design Mode\</link\>, you can see that $[officename] adds a labeled input field for every inserted database field.				20220827 09:49:47
