helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811	9			0	uk	Inserts a new line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379	10			0	uk	Up Arrow				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192	11			0	uk	Places the cursor into the previous line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933	12			0	uk	Down Arrow				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041	13			0	uk	Places the cursor into the next line.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153178	14			0	uk	Enter				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228	15			0	uk	Completes the input in the field and places the cursor into the next field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422	16			0	uk	As with list boxes or combo boxes, you can open or close the list with a mouse click at the arrow on the right end of the field. However, the input here can be entered either in the opened list or in the top text field. An exception is the properties that expect a list representation, for example, the property \<emph\>List Entries\</emph\>, which can be set for the control fields \<emph\>List Box\</emph\> and \<emph\>Combo Box\</emph\>. Here, you can only edit the entries when the field is opened.				20220827 09:49:47
