helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	hd_id04092009442139524				0	uk	Supports primary keys				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id04096620092139526				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enable to overrule Base's heuristics used to detect whether the database supports primary keys.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id66841631				0	uk	When connecting to a database using a generic API like ODBC, JDBC, or ADO, Base currently applies heuristics to determine whether this database supports primary keys. None of those APIs has dedicated support to retrieve this information.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id66841632				0	uk	The heuristics sometimes fails. This tri-state check box by default is set to the undetermined state, which means "apply the heuristics". If the check box is enabled, primary key support is assumed. If the check box is disabled, no primary key support is assumed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id66841633				0	uk	Note that if this option is just for overruling the heuristics. If you enable the check box for a database which actually does not support primary keys, you will see some errors.				20220827 09:49:47
