helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id8773155				0	uk	\<variable id=\"rep_main\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5248573				0	uk	The Report Builder is a tool to create your own database reports. Unlike with the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100000.xhp\"\>Report Wizard\</link\>, using the Report Builder you can take control to design the report the way you want. The generated report is a Writer document that you can edit, too.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7128818				0	uk	To use the Report Builder, the Report Builder extension must be installed. In addition, the Java Runtime Environment (JRE) software must be installed, and this software must be selected in %PRODUCTNAME.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3753776				0	uk	To Install the Report Builder Extension				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5284279				0	uk	Choose Tools - Extension Manager to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>Extension Manager\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4494766				0	uk	If you see the Report Builder in the Extension Manager list, then you do not need to install the extension. Else click the link "Get more extensions here". This opens your web browser at the address \<link href=\"http://extensions.openoffice.org\"\>http://extensions.openoffice.org\</link\> and shows a list of available extensions.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7858516				0	uk	Find the Report Builder extension. Click at the icon or the "click here" text link. This opens the download page for the extension.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id973540				0	uk	Click the "Get it!" icon. The extension file will be downloaded to your computer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4680928				0	uk	Switch back from your web browser to the %PRODUCTNAME window. The Extension Manager should still be visible.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id9014252				0	uk	In the Extension Manager, click Add to open the Add extensions dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id6011841				0	uk	Select the extension file that you downloaded. Click Open.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2591326				0	uk	This starts the installation of the Report Builder extension.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id6201666				0	uk	Read the license. If you accept the license, click Accept to continue the installation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id208136				0	uk	Click Close to close the Extension Manager.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id20813699				0	uk	Restart %PRODUCTNAME. If the Quickstarter is running, also close the Quickstarter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id556047				0	uk	To install the JRE software				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4515823				0	uk	The Report Builder requires an installed Java Runtime Environment (JRE).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4044312				0	uk	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/java.xhp\"\>Java\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id1369060				0	uk	Wait up to one minute, while %PRODUCTNAME collects information on installed Java software on your system.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id860927				0	uk	If a recent JRE version is found on your system, you see an entry in the list.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id8581804				0	uk	Click the option button in front of the entry to enable this JRE version for use in %PRODUCTNAME.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7730033				0	uk	Ensure that \<emph\>Use a Java runtime environment\</emph\> is enabled.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id6317636				0	uk	If no JRE version is found on your system, open your web browser and download the JRE software from \<link href=\"http://www.java.com\"\>http://www.java.com\</link\>. Install the JRE software. Then restart %PRODUCTNAME and open \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Java again.				20220827 09:49:47
