helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153674	109			0	uk	Querying text fields				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149134	110			0	uk	To query the content of a text field, you must put the expression between single quotes. The distinction between uppercase and lowercase letters depends on the database in use. LIKE, by definition, is case-sensitive (though some databases don't see it that strict).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149302	111			0	uk	Querying date fields				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3157998	252			0	uk	\<emph\>Date fields\</emph\> are represented as #Date# to clearly identify them as dates. Date, time and date/time constants (literals) used in conditions can be of either the SQL Escape Syntax type, or default SQL2 syntax.				20220827 09:49:47
