helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150247				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>changes; accepting or rejecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function;accepting or rejecting changes\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150247	23			0	uk	\<variable id=\"redlining_accept\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_accept.xhp\" name=\"Accepting or Rejecting Changes\"\>Accepting or Rejecting Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	uk	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1110200810120034				0	uk	In Writer text documents you can also accept or reject changes by choosing commands from the context menu.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571	24			0	uk	When you edit a document in which others have made changes, you can accept or reject the changes individually or all together.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	25			0	uk	If you have put multiple copies of the document in circulation, first merge these into one document (see \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp#redlining_docmerge\"/\>).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	26			0	uk	Open the document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Accept or Reject\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\> dialog appears.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	27			0	uk	Select a change on the \<emph\>List\</emph\> tab. The change is selected and displayed in the document and you can now enter your decision with one of the buttons.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209	28			0	uk	If one author has modified another author's change, you will see the changes hierarchically arranged with a plus sign for opening up the hierarchy.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474	29			0	uk	If the list of changes is too long, you can switch to the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> tab in the dialog and specify that you only want to see the changes of certain authors, or only the changes of the last day, or that you want the list to be restricted in some other way.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271	42			0	uk	Color-coded entries display the result of the filter that is set. Entries in black can be accepted or rejected and match the filter criteria. Entries in blue do not themselves match the filter criteria, but have subentries that are included by the filter. Gray entries cannot be accepted or rejected and do not match the filter criterion. Green entries do match the filter but cannot be accepted or rejected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Editing Chart Legends				20220827 09:49:47
