helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275	3			0	uk	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog appears.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164	4			0	uk	Select the file you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149234	13			0	uk	Restrict Files to Display				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985	14			0	uk	To restrict the display of files in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog to a certain type select the corresponding \<emph\>File type\</emph\> from the list. Select \<emph\>All Files (*.*)\</emph\> to display all files.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id4651326				0	uk	Cursor Position				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id5509201				0	uk	In general, all documents open with the cursor at the start of the document. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id6594744				0	uk	One exception appears when the author of a Writer text document saves and reopens a document: The cursor will be at the same position where it has been when the document was saved. This only works when the name of the author was entered in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - User Data\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3422650				0	uk	Press Shift+F5 to set the cursor to the last saved position.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148453	17			0	uk	Opening an Empty Document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287	19			0	uk	Click the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon on the Standard bar or choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>. This opens a document of the document type specified.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092	20			0	uk	If you click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon, a submenu opens in which you can select another document type.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501358				0	uk	System File Dialogs or %PRODUCTNAME Dialogs				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501356				0	uk	On most operating systems, you can choose to use the system file dialogs or %PRODUCTNAME dialogs.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501429				0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\> to switch the type of open/save dialogs.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501449				0	uk	The %PRODUCTNAME dialogs support file download and upload using secure https connections.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501453				0	uk	Opening Files from a Web Server				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	9			0	uk	You can enter a URL in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialogs. The URL must start with file:/// or ftp:// or http://. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501548				0	uk	If you use the %PRODUCTNAME dialog, you can use the https:// prefix for a secure connection, and you can save a document on the web server.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C4				0	uk	When you open a file by a URL from the Windows file dialog, Windows will open a local copy of the file, located in the Internet Explorer cache. The %PRODUCTNAME file dialog opens a local copy of the file in the system's temp folder.				20220827 09:49:47
