helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147834	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"spadmin\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\" name=\"Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms\"\>Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159876				0	uk	%PRODUCTNAME uses the installed fonts of your system. In a text document you can select from all printable fonts. In an HTML document or in Web layout, only fonts that are visible on screen are offered. In spreadsheets and drawings you can select from all installed fonts.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	2			0	uk	Under UNIX based platforms, the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> is provided to help you set up printers and faxes for use with the $[officename] software.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	117			0	uk	Call the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> as follows:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242	11			0	uk	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209	12			0	uk	Enter: ./spadmin				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349	14			0	uk	After it starts, the window of the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> appears.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580	10			0	uk	Following a server installation, the system administrator first logs on as with root privileges, and starts the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>. The administrator then creates a general printer configuration file called {install_path}/share/psprint/psprint.conf for all users. All changes are immediately available to all users.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159177	121			0	uk	Setting up Printers				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157	122			0	uk	Under UNIX based platforms, the $[officename] software only offers direct support for printers using the PostScript technology. Other printers must be set up as described in the section \<emph\>Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software\</emph\>. The $[officename] software automatically provides a printer with the default driver for each system queue. You can add additional printers as needed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148564	286			0	uk	Adding a Printer				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559	353			0	uk	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360	354			0	uk	Enter: ./spadmin				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360	287			0	uk	Click the \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\> button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	288			0	uk	Select the \<emph\>Create Printer\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192	289			0	uk	Select the appropriate driver for your printer. If you are not using a PostScript printer or your model is not listed, use the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> driver or follow the steps below. You can also add new drivers using the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> button or delete unnecessary drivers using the \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> button. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863	290			0	uk	Choose a command line that you can use to print on your printer (for example, lp -d my_queue). Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	291			0	uk	Give the printer a name and determine whether it should become the default printer. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429	292			0	uk	To print a test page, click on \<emph\>Test Page\</emph\>. If the test page fails to print or is incorrectly printed, check all settings as described in \<emph\>Changing Printer Settings\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146147	294			0	uk	Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428	124			0	uk	When installing a non-PostScript printer, you must set your system so that PostScript can be converted into the language of the printer. We recommend using current PostScript conversion software such as Ghostscript (http://www.cs.wisc.edu/~ghost/).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154639	125			0	uk	You should set up the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> in that case. Also make sure that the page margins are set correctly.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153	127			0	uk	If you are using a printer using the PostScript technology, you should install a description file for the printer (PostScript Printer Definition - PPD) so that you can utilize the specific printer features like paper tray selection, duplex print function and all built-in fonts. You can also use the generic printer driver since it contains the most important data and is suitable for most printers. In that case, you will have to do without the paper tray selection and must correctly set the page margins.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976	128			0	uk	Some PPD files are installed as default files. If there is no matching PPD file for your printer, you will find various PPD files at http://www.adobe.com/products/printerdrivers/. You can also ask the manufacturer of your printer for PPD files. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147435	346			0	uk	Importing Drivers When Creating a New Printer				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484	129			0	uk	Click \<emph\>Import\</emph\> in the driver selection dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	347			0	uk	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> to select the directory where you unpacked the PPD files. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147443	348			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Selection of drivers\</emph\> list box, select the printer driver you want to install.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364	349			0	uk	Click OK.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152885	350			0	uk	Deleting Drivers When Creating a New Printer				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729	130			0	uk	Select the printer driver.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417	351			0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149909	352			0	uk	Be sure that you do not delete the generic printer driver, and remember that drivers deleted from server installations are no longer available to other users who are using the same server installation.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456	131			0	uk	If the printer has more fonts built in than the usual PostScript fonts, you must also load the AFM files for these additional fonts. Copy the AFM files into the {install_path}/share/psprint/fontmetric directory or into the {install_path}/user/psprint/fontmetric directory. You can find AFM files, for example, at ftp://ftp.adobe.com/pub/adobe/type/win/all/afmfiles/.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148388	296			0	uk	Changing Printer Settings				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284	22			0	uk	In the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>, select the printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog appears containing several tab pages. This is where you can make settings that are used according to the PPD file of the selected printer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148833	297			0	uk	Select the command on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. You can remove superfluous commands using the \<emph\>Remove\</emph\> button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154270	138			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Paper\</emph\> tab page, you can define the paper format and paper tray to be used as the default settings for this printer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649	265			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Device\</emph\> tab page, you can activate the special options for your printer. If your printer can only print in black and white, choose "grayscale" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\>, otherwise choose "color". If switching to grayscale leads to unfavorable results, you can also select "color" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\> and see how the printer or PostScript emulator applies it. Furthermore, on this tab page you can set the precision with which colors are described as well as the PostScript level.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752	284			0	uk	The \<emph\>Font Replacement\</emph\> tab page allows you to select a printer font type available in the printer for each font type installed on your computer. This way you can reduce the data volume sent to the printer. Font replacement can be turned on or off for each printer individually.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924	266			0	uk	You should also set the page margins correctly on the \<emph\>Additional settings\</emph\> tab when using the generic printer driver so that your printout is not cropped. You can also enter a description in the Comments field, which will also be displayed on the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443	267			0	uk	Some of these settings can also be set for the current printout in the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog or the \<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\> dialog in the $[officename] software with the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042	132			0	uk	Renaming or Deleting Printers				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338	134			0	uk	Select a printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258	136			0	uk	To rename the selected printer, click \<emph\>Rename\</emph\>. Enter an appropriate name in the dialog that appears and click OK. The name must be unique and should be chosen so that you can recognize the printer and the application. Printer names must be assigned the same for all users because, when documents are exchanged, the selected printer remains unchanged if the recipient has it under the same name.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963	137			0	uk	To delete the selected printer, click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>. The default printer or a printer that has been created by the system administrator in a server installation cannot be removed using this dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147346	140			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Selecting a Default Printer \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769	31			0	uk	To make the printer selected from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box the default printer, double-click its name or click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154204	141			0	uk	Using Fax Functionality				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463	52			0	uk	If you have installed a fax package such as Efax or HylaFax on your computer, you can send faxes with the $[officename] software.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154575	355			0	uk	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277	356			0	uk	Enter: ./spadmin				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146808	298			0	uk	Click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151070	299			0	uk	Select \<emph\>Connect a fax device\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150787	300			0	uk	Choose whether to use the default driver or another printer driver. If you are not using the default driver, select the appropriate driver. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111	301			0	uk	Enter a command line with which to communicate with the fax in the following dialog. In the command line of each fax sent "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(PHONE)" by the telephone number of the recipient fax machine. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the PostScript code is transmitted in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135	302			0	uk	Assign a name to your new fax printer and determine whether the telephone numbers (see below) marked in the text should be removed from the printout, or not. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506	303			0	uk	You can now send faxes by printing to the printer that has just been created.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148419	83			0	uk	Enter the fax number as text in the document. You can also enter a field that takes the fax number from your active database. In any case, the fax number must start with the characters @@# and end with @@. A valid entry would have the form @@#1234567@@.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826	304			0	uk	If these characters including the telephone number are not printed, activate the \<emph\>Fax number is removed from the printout\</emph\> option under \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. If no telephone number is entered in the document, a dialog prompting you for it will appear after the printout.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196	305			0	uk	In $[officename] you can also activate an icon for sending faxes to a default fax. To do this, choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Toolbars\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\> and add from "Documents" the \<emph\>Send Default Fax\</emph\> icon. You can set which fax is used when this button is pressed under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517	84			0	uk	Remember to create one separate print job for each fax, otherwise, the first recipient will receive all the faxes. In the \<emph\>Tools - Mail Merge\</emph\> dialog select the \<emph\>Printer\</emph\> option and then select the \<emph\>Single print jobs\</emph\> check box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146929	306			0	uk	Connecting a PostScript to PDF Converter				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154989	307			0	uk	If a PostScript to PDF converter such as Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is installed on your computer, you can quickly create PDF documents in the $[officename] software.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150524	308			0	uk	In spadmin, click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268	309			0	uk	Select \<emph\>Connect a PDF converter\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445	310			0	uk	Choose whether to use the default driver, the Acrobat Distiller driver or another driver. The driver "Generic Printer (T42 enabled)" prefers the type 42 fonts over type 3 fonts; this driver is a good choice for output to a software PostScript interpreter. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155128	311			0	uk	In the next dialog, enter a command line for the PostScript->PDF Converter. Enter the directory where the PDF files should be saved. If you do not provide a directory, the user's home directory will be used. In the command line "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(OUTFILE)" by the target file, the name of which is created from the document name. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the PostScript code is forwarded in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. If Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is in the search path, you can use one of the predefined command lines. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889	312			0	uk	Assign a name to your new PDF converter. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153064	313			0	uk	You can now create PDF documents by printing to the converter that has just been created.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Inserting and Editing Buttons				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149798				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>command buttons, see push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>controls;adding to documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keys;adding push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>buttons;adding push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>press buttons, see push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>push buttons;adding to documents\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798	5			0	uk	\<variable id=\"formfields\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/formfields.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Buttons\"\>Adding a Command Button to a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	uk	You can use the Form Controls toolbar to add checkboxes, buttons, tables showing data records, and other controls to a document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077F				0	uk	To Add a Button to a Document 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751	6			0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	7			0	uk	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A4				0	uk	The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	8			0	uk	In the document, drag to draw the button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	uk	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CD				0	uk	Specify the properties of the button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923	11			0	uk	To change the button label, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and edit the text in the \<emph\>Label\</emph\> box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303	12			0	uk	To attach a macro to the button, click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab, and click the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button beside the button action that you want to run the macro. In the \<emph\>Assign Macro\</emph\> dialog, locate the macro that you want to use, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10814				0	uk	Close the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147350	76			0	uk	(Optional) Specify the properties of the form that the button belongs to.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	uk	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Form\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	uk	The \<emph\>Form Properties\</emph\> dialog opens.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	uk	Specify the properties for the form and then close the dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Protecting Records				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>changes; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protecting; recorded changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>records; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function;protecting records\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"redlining_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Records\"\>Protecting Records\</link\> \</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id1631824				0	uk	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751	2			0	uk	To protect the changes made in a document during editing, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. To turn off the function or to accept or reject changes it is necessary to enter the correct password first.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	3			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Protect Records\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/password_dlg.xhp\" name=\"Password\"\>\<emph\>Password\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	4			0	uk	Enter a password consisting of at least 5 characters and confirm it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
