helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152823				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>data sources; registering address books\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>address books; registering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>system address book registration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering; address books\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228	2			0	uk	\<variable id=\"data_addressbook\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_addressbook.xhp\" name=\"Registering an Address Book\"\>Registering an Address Book\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927	3			0	uk	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you can register different data sources. The contents of the data fields are then available to you for use in various fields and controls. Your system address book is such a data source.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	4			0	uk	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> templates and wizards use fields for the contents of the address book. When activated, the general fields in the templates are automatically replaced with the fields from the data source of your address book.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399	5			0	uk	In order for the replacement to take place, you must tell \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> which address book you use. The wizard asking for this information appears automatically the first time you activate, for example, a business letter template. You can also call the wizard by following the steps listed below.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id5941648				0	uk	The address book data is read-only in %PRODUCTNAME Base. It is not possible to add, edit, or delete address data from within Base.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096	35			0	uk	Address Data Source Wizard				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	36			0	uk	To call the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Address Data Source\"\>Address Data Source\</link\> wizard, choose \<emph\>File - Wizards - Address Data Source\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811	6			0	uk	Registering An Existing Address Book Manually				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771	8			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Address Book Source\</emph\>. The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110101.xhp\" name=\"Templates: Address Book Assignment\"\>\<emph\>Templates: Address Book Assignment\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491	10			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> combo box, select the system address book or the data source you want to use as an address book.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	11			0	uk	If you have not yet registered the system address book in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the data source, click the \<emph\>Address Data Source ...\</emph\> button. This takes you to the \<emph\>Address Book Data Source Wizard\</emph\>, in which you can register your address book as a new data source in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365	13			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> combo box, select the database table you want to use as the address book.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084	15			0	uk	Under \<emph\>Field assignment\</emph\>, match the fields for first name, company, department, and so on to the actual field names used in your address book.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_idN10784				0	uk	When finished, close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983	18			0	uk	Now your data source is registered in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the address book. If you now open a template from the \<emph\>Business Correspondence\</emph\> category, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> can automatically insert the correct fields for a form letter.				20220827 09:49:47
