helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Working With %PRODUCTNAME XML Filters 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>saving;to XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>loading;XML files\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>importing;from XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>exporting;to XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>file filters;XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XSLT filters, see also XML filters\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10923				0	uk	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter.xhp\"\>About XML Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10927				0	uk	%PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>stores documents in XML format\</link\>. You can create customized filters that convert the native OpenDocument XML file format used by %PRODUCTNAME into another format. These filters can be integrated into %PRODUCTNAME seamlessly so that you can save or load these formats transparently.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093A				0	uk	To create an XML filter, you must have a good understanding of XML and XSLT concepts. These concepts are beyond the scope of this help.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	uk	An XML filter contains \<emph\>stylesheets\</emph\> that are written in the XSLT language. The stylesheets define the transformation from the OpenDocument file format to another XML format through export and import filters. There are three types of XML filters:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10947				0	uk	 \<emph\>Import Filters\</emph\> load external XML files and transform the format of the files into the OpenDocument XML file format. After you install an import filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10960				0	uk	 \<emph\>Export Filters\</emph\> transform OpenDocument XML files and \<emph\>save\</emph\> the files to a different XML format. After you install an export filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070001.xhp\"\>Export dialog\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10979				0	uk	 \<emph\>Import/Export Filters\</emph\> load and save OpenDocument XML files into a different XML \<emph\>format\</emph\>. After you install these filters, the names of the filters are added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\> and the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\"\>File Save As dialog\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B39				0	uk	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/Style/XSL/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible \<emph\>Stylesheet\</emph\> Language (XSL)\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4E				0	uk	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/XML/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible Markup Language (XML)\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D97				0	uk	 \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp#xmlformat\"/\> 				20220827 09:49:47
