helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Recording Changes				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>changes; recording\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recording; changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>comments; on changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>review function;tracking changes\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364	7			0	uk	\<variable id=\"redlining_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_enter.xhp\" name=\"Recording Changes\"\>Recording Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7271645				0	uk	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145669	8			0	uk	Not all changes are recorded. For example, the changing of a tab stop from align left to align right is not recorded. However, all usual changes made by a proofreader are recorded, such as additions, deletions, text alterations, and usual formatting.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	17			0	uk	1.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095	9			0	uk	To start recording changes, open the document to be edited and choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Changes\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Changes\</emph\>\</link\> and then choose \<emph\>Record\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749	18			0	uk	2.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802	10			0	uk	Now start making your changes. You will note that all new text passages that you enter are underlined in color, while all text that you delete remains visible but is crossed out and shown in color.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349	19			0	uk	3.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	11			0	uk	If you move to a marked change with the mouse pointer, you will see a reference to the type of change, the author, date and time of day for the change in the Help Tip. If the Extended Tips are also enabled, you will also see any available comments on this change.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156119	12			0	uk	Changes in a spreadsheet document are highlighted by a border around the cells; when you point to the cell you can see more detailed information on this change in the Help Tip.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473	13			0	uk	You can enter a comment on each recorded change by placing the cursor in the area of the change and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Comment\</emph\>. In addition to Extended Tips, the comment is also displayed in the list in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230400.xhp\" name=\"Accept or Reject Changes\"\>\<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153542	14			0	uk	To stop recording changes, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> again. The check mark is removed and you can now save the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627	15			0	uk	In a text document, you can highlight all lines that you have changed with an additional colored marking. This can be in the form of a red line in the margin, for example.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530	16			0	uk	To change the settings for tracking changes, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040700.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>\<emph\>Changes\</emph\>\</link\> or on the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060600.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>\<emph\>Changes\</emph\>\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Pasting Contents in Special Formats				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3620715				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;pasting formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;clipboard options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats;pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;pasting in special formats\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10725				0	uk	\<variable id=\"pasting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pasting.xhp\"\>Pasting Contents in Special Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	uk	Contents that are stored on the clipboard can be pasted into your document using different formats. In %PRODUCTNAME you can choose how to paste the contents using a dialog or a drop-down icon.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	uk	The available options depend on the contents of the clipboard.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144547360				0	uk	In Writer text documents, you can press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+V to paste the contents of the clipboard as unformatted text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	uk	Pasting clipboard contents using an icon menu				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	uk	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard Bar to open the menu.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	uk	Select one of the options.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	uk	If you do not like the result, click the \<emph\>Undo\</emph\> icon and then paste again with another option.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10762				0	uk	Pasting clipboard contents using a dialog				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10769				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10771				0	uk	Select one of the options and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	uk	If you are in a spreadsheet and the contents of the clipboard are spreadsheet cells, then a different \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears. Use the \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog to copy cells using basic or advanced options.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	uk	\<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>: swaps the rows and the columns of the cell range to be pasted.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	uk	\<emph\>Link\</emph\>: pastes the cell range as a link. If the source file changes, the pasted cells change also.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	uk	The other options are explained in the help, when you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\> dialog from within %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BA				0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
