helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145346	71			0	uk	\<variable id=\"autohide\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/autohide.xhp\" name=\"Showing, Docking and Hiding Windows\"\>Showing, Docking and Hiding Windows\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242	52			0	uk	Some windows in $[officename] are dockable, such as the Navigator window. You can move these windows, re-size them or dock them to an edge.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154750	65			0	uk	Docking and Undocking Windows				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	66			0	uk	To dock a window, do one of the following:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503	67			0	uk	Drag the window by its title bar to the side, or				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275	68			0	uk	Double-click inside a vacant area of the window while holding down the Ctrl key. In the Styles and Formatting window, double-click a gray part of the window next to the icons while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. Alternatively, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F10\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335	69			0	uk	These methods can also be used to undock a currently docked window.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149796	70			0	uk	Showing and Hiding Docked Windows				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3149655\" src=\"res/helpimg/ein.png\" width=\"0.1043inch\" height=\"0.4272inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149655\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3152921	64			0	uk	Click the button on the edge of the docked window to show or hide the docked window. The AutoHide function allows you to temporarily show a hidden window by clicking on its edge. When you click in the document, the docked window hides again. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Working with Tables				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id1983703				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table views of databases\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	uk	\<variable id=\"data_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tables.xhp\"\>Working with Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	uk	Data is stored in tables. As an example, your system address book that you use for your e-mail addresses is a table of the address book database. Each address is a data record, presented as a row in that table. The data records consist of data fields, for example the first and the last name fields and the e-mail field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	uk	Creating a New Table With the Table Wizard				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	uk	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new table using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/tablewizard00.xhp\"\>Table Wizard\</link\>:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	uk	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				20220827 09:49:47
