helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>labels; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>business cards; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>synchronizing;labels and business cards\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774	4			0	uk	\<variable id=\"labels\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels.xhp\" name=\"Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\"\>Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345	81			0	uk	Designing Business Cards Through a Dialog				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798	70			0	uk	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Business Cards\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Business Cards\</emph\>\</link\> to open the\<emph\> Business Cards \</emph\>dialog, which allows you to choose how your business cards will look.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147654	82			0	uk	Designing Labels and Business Cards				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349	71			0	uk	You can design both labels and business cards through the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880	5			0	uk	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010200.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Labels\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	32			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, define the label format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674	83			0	uk	$[officename] Writer contains many formats of commercially available sheets for labels, badges, and business cards. You can also add other, user-defined formats.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271	28			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Inscription\</emph\>, you can choose what you want written on the labels.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610	84			0	uk	This often involves database fields, so that the labels can be printed with varying content, when sending "Form Letters" for example. It is also possible to have the same text printed on every label.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	85			0	uk	Use the \<emph\>Database \</emph\>and \<emph\>Table \</emph\>list boxes to select the database and table from which the data fields are obtained. Click on the arrow button to transfer the selected data field into the inscription area. Press Enter to insert a line break. You can also enter spaces and any other fixed text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560	6			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> tab you can define your own label formats, not covered by the predefined formats. To do this, select "User" from the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list box. On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, you can specify whether all labels or only certain ones are to be created.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358	33			0	uk	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, make sure that the \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> box is selected. If this is selected, a label only has to be entered (on the top left label) and edited once.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424	86			0	uk	As soon as you click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, you will see a small window with the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button. Enter the first label. When you click on the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button, the current individual label is copied to all the other labels on the sheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767	29			0	uk	Click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\> to create a new document with the settings you have entered.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449	88			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Business Cards\"\>Business Cards\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153394				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; copying between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394	27			0	uk	\<variable id=\"copy_drawfunctions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copy_drawfunctions.xhp\" name=\"Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\"\>Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	28			0	uk	In $[officename] it is possible to copy drawing objects between text, spreadsheets and presentation documents. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	29			0	uk	Select the drawing object or objects.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426	31			0	uk	Copy the drawing object to the clipboard, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	32			0	uk	Switch to the other document and place the cursor where the drawing object is to be inserted.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234	33			0	uk	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573	34			0	uk	Inserting into a text document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276	35			0	uk	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current paragraph. You can change the anchor by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar. This opens a popup menu where you can select the anchor type.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609	36			0	uk	Inserting into a spreadsheet				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	30			0	uk	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current cell. You can change the anchor between cell and page by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149456\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleanchortype.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149456\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Sending Documents as E-mail				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153345				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>documents; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>e-mail attachments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attachments in e-mails\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"email\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/email.xhp\" name=\"Sending Documents as E-mail\"\>Sending Documents as E-mail\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897	2			0	uk	Working in $[officename], you can send the current document as an e-mail attachment.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335	3			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Document as E-mail\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127	4			0	uk	$[officename] opens your default e-mail program.\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\> If you want to send the current document with another e-mail program, you can select the program to use with \<emph\>Internet - E-mail\</emph\> in the Options dialog box.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986	5			0	uk	In your e-mail program, enter the recipient, subject and any text you want to add, then send the e-mail.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3595385				0	uk	In case you want to send the e-mail to a recipient who only has software that cannot read the OpenDocument format, you can send the current document in an often used proprietary format.\<br/\>For a text document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft Word\</item\>. For a spreadsheet, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft Excel\</item\>. And for a presentation, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft PowerPoint\</item\>. \<br/\>If you want to send the document as a read-only file, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as PDF\</item\>.\<br/\>These commands do not change your current document. Only a temporary copy is created and sent.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Changing Default Templates				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154285				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>modifying, see changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing, see also editing and replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default templates; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;editing and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;templates\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154285	36			0	uk	\<variable id=\"standard_template\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/standard_template.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Templates\"\>Changing Default Templates\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811	2			0	uk	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customized Styles or other contents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	3			0	uk	Modifying Default Templates				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365	4			0	uk	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152	6			0	uk	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	uk	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011	9			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799	11			0	uk	Double-click \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> in the list on the left. You will see the user-defined templates in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>. Select the template you have just saved and open the context menu or open the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901	26			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947	27			0	uk	Resetting Default Templates				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276	12			0	uk	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792	29			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	32			0	uk	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764	13			0	uk	Using Custom Templates				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	uk	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109	15			0	uk	Templates in the Template Folder				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918	16			0	uk	You can save a new template with \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> or by selecting "Template" file type in any Save dialog. Save the template in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\> to be able to access the template from within the \<emph\>File - New - From Templates and Documents\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960	33			0	uk	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialog before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343	17			0	uk	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
