helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798	104			0	uk	\<variable id=\"data_tabledefine\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\" name=\"Table Design\"\>Table Design\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535	2			0	uk	This section contains information about how to create a new database table in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05010000.xhp\" name=\"design view\"\>design view\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288	3			0	uk	Open the database file of the database where you want a new table. Click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon. Choose \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\> to create a new table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798	4			0	uk	In the Design view, you can now create the fields for your table.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349	5			0	uk	Enter new fields in rows from top to bottom. Click the \<emph\>Field Name\</emph\> cell and enter a field name for each data field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id1595507				0	uk	Include a "primary key" data field. Base needs a primary key to be able to edit the table contents. A primary key has unique contents for each data record. For example, insert a numerical field, right-click the first column, and choose \<emph\>Primary Key\</emph\> from the context menu. Set \<emph\>AutoValue\</emph\> to "Yes", so Base can automatically increment the value for each new record.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	6			0	uk	In the next cell to the right, define the \<emph\>Field Type\</emph\>. When you click in the cell, you can select a field type in the combo box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760	38			0	uk	Each field can only accept data corresponding to the specified field type. For example, it is not possible to enter text in a number field. Memo fields in dBASE III format are references to internally-managed text files which can hold up to 64KB text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456	41			0	uk	You can enter an optional \<emph\>Description\</emph\> for each field. The text of the description will appear as a tip on the column headings in the table view.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379	42			0	uk	Field Properties				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798	45			0	uk	Enter properties for each selected data field. Depending on the database type, some input facilities may not be available.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762	46			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> box, enter the default contents for every new record. This contents can be edited later.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869	47			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Entry required\</emph\> box, specify whether or not the field may remain empty.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908	7			0	uk	For the \<emph\>Length\</emph\> box, a combo box may be shown that provides the available choices.				20220827 09:49:47
