helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329	38			0	uk	Repeatedly pressing F6 switches the focus and circles through the following objects:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669	37			0	uk	menu bar,				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234	36			0	uk	every toolbar from top to bottom and from left to right,				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618	35			0	uk	every free window from left to right,				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514	34			0	uk	document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252	32			0	uk	Press Shift+F6 to switch through objects in the opposite direction.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152473	31			0	uk	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to switch to the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360	30			0	uk	Press F10 to switch to the menu bar and back.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896	29			0	uk	Escape closes an open submenu, a toolbar, or the current free window.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3161656	21			0	uk	Calling a menu command				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056	20			0	uk	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> or F6 or F10 to select the first menu (the \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu). With right arrow, the next menu to the right is selected; with left arrow, the previous menu.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381	19			0	uk	Arrow down opens a selected menu. Any additional arrow down and up arrow move the selection through the menu commands. With right arrow you open any existing submenus.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798	18			0	uk	Press Enter to execute the selected menu command.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147086	17			0	uk	Executing an icon command				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922	16			0	uk	Press F6 repeatedly until the first icon on the toolbar is selected. Use the right and left arrows to select an icon on a horizontal toolbar. Similarly, use the up and down arrows to select an icon on a vertical toolbar. The Home key selects the first icon on a toolbar and the End key, the last.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3144433	15			0	uk	Press Enter to execute the selected icon. If the selected icon normally demands a consecutive mouse action, such as inserting a rectangle, then pressing the Enter key is not sufficient: in these cases press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968	28			0	uk	Pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter on an icon for creating a draw object. A draw object will be placed into the middle of the view, with a predefined size.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449	27			0	uk	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter on the Selection tool to select the first draw object in the document. If you want to edit, size, or move the selected draw object, first use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to set the focus into the document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041	26			0	uk	If a toolbar is longer than can be displayed on screen, it shows an icon at the right or lower edge. Select the toolbar and press PageUp or PageDown to display the remaining icons.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440	14			0	uk	Special hints for toolbars				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983	13			0	uk	Press the down arrow or right arrow to open the selected toolbar. This is equivalent to a mouse click. In the toolbar use the right arrow and left arrow keys. The Home and End keys select the first and last icon in the toolbar, respectively.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145365	12			0	uk	Close the toolbar with Esc. It is not possible to move the toolbar without a mouse.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119	11			0	uk	Selection from a combo box				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3148645\" src=\"res/helpimg/zellvor.png\" width=\"1.528in\" height=\"0.292in\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148645\"\>Combo box\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666	10			0	uk	Select the combo box. Press Enter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366	9			0	uk	Use the down arrow or Page Down key to scroll down the combo box entries, or the up arrow or Page Up key to scroll upwards. The Home key takes you to the first entry and the End key takes you to the last entry.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749	8			0	uk	Press Enter to execute the selected entry.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150685	41			0	uk	Selection in Tables				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320	42			0	uk	In several windows, dialogs, and in the table control field, there are tables to select data, for instance, in the right part of the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\" name=\"Data Source View\"\>Data Source View\</link\>. The following keys are used for selections in these tables:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014	43			0	uk	Spacebar: switches from selection of the current row and cancellation of any selection, but not if the current cell is in edit mode.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	44			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+spacebar: switches between selection of the current row and cancellation of this selection.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149488	45			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+spacebar: switches between selection of the current column and cancellation of this selection.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	73			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Up Arrow or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Down Arrow: moves the window separator between table and form, for instance in the bibliography database.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251	147			0	uk	In a table control or in the data source view, the Tab key moves to the next column. To move to the next control, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab. To move to the previous control, press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150592	7			0	uk	Size and Position of Windows and Dialogs				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153221	6			0	uk	First press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+spacebar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456	5			0	uk	A system menu opens with menu commands like \<emph\>Move\</emph\>, \<emph\>Resize\</emph\> and \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400	4			0	uk	Choose a command (down arrow, then Enter).				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155083	3			0	uk	Now you can use the arrow keys to move or resize the dialog or window.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497	2			0	uk	Press Enter to accept the change. Press Escape to cancel the changes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146988	150			0	uk	Docking and Undocking Windows and Toolbars				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176	151			0	uk	Press F6 until the window or toolbar is selected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	152			0	uk	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F10.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154479	148			0	uk	Selecting objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148993	149			0	uk	Press Shift+F4 to select the first object in the current document. When an object is selected, press Tab to select the next object, or press Esc to go back to the text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152962	54			0	uk	Edit Objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156379	53			0	uk	A selected OLE object can be activated with the Enter key.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766	55			0	uk	Edit Position and Size of Objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405	56			0	uk	Use the arrow keys to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145619	57			0	uk	Set the grid resolution unit with \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Grid\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> area. If you enter a number greater than 1 in the \<emph\>Subdivision\</emph\> area, you must press the arrow key as often as the number states to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450	58			0	uk	Use the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and arrow keys to move the selected object by one pixel.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345	59			0	uk	Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to enter the handle edit mode. The upper left handle is the active handle, it starts blinking. Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to select the next handle. Press Escape to exit the handle edit mode.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565	60			0	uk	In the handle edit mode, the arrow keys move the selected handle, which changes the object size.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361	61			0	uk	Edit the Anchors of Objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534	62			0	uk	You can move the anchor of an object with the arrow keys. First enter the handle edit mode and select the anchor. Depending on the type of anchor, you can then move the anchor in different directions.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808	63			0	uk	Select the object.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150646	64			0	uk	Enter the handle edit mode with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150940	65			0	uk	The upper left handle starts blinking. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab several times, until no handle blinks. This signals that now the anchor of the object is activated. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In text documents you can press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A to activate the anchor directly.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919	66			0	uk	Use the arrow keys to move the anchor. The object follows the anchor as appropriate.				20220827 09:49:47
