helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154186	64			0	uk	\<variable id=\"data_search\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_search.xhp\" name=\"Searching Tables and Form Documents\"\>Searching Tables and Form Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3153311\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_recsearch.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153311\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149178	65			0	uk	In spreadsheets and documents in which form controls are used, you can click the \<emph\>Find Record\</emph\> icon on the form bar to open a dialog to find any text and values. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	66			0	uk	You can search in one or in all data fields. You can select whether the text must be at the beginning, end or any location of the data field. You also can use the ? and * wildcards, as in the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog. You can find additional information about the database search function in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Assistive Tools in $[officename]				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] assistive technology\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assistive technology in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen readers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399	22			0	uk	\<variable id=\"assistive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"Assistive Tools in $[officename]\"\>Assistive Tools in $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267	25			0	uk	$[officename] supports some assistive technology tools like screen magnification software, screen readers, and on-screen keyboards. Most of these tools communicate with $[officename] by means of the Java(TM) Access Bridge software, that uses the Java Accessibility API, a part of the Java runtime environment.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id8847010				0	uk	A current list of supported assistive tools can be found on the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Accessibility\"\>Apache OpenOffice Wiki\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345	12			0	uk	Requirements to use assistive tools in $[officename]				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209	13			0	uk	Java Runtime Environment (JRE) version 1.4.1_01 and higher, or version 1.4.0_02 with the locale set to "en_us".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797	26			0	uk	Most recent version of the software for your assistive tool				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	15			0	uk	On Windows systems, \<link href=\"http://www.sun.com/access/downloads/\" name=\"Java Access Bridge\"\>Java Access Bridge\</link\> software version 1.0.3 or higher 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762	16			0	uk	On UNIX(R) systems, the GNOME 2 desktop environment with the Java Access Bridge software for GNOME				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149795	23			0	uk	Supported Assistive Tools				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419	2			0	uk	On Windows systems, $[officename] directly supports most on-screen keyboard software. Additional support for assistive tools is provided by the Java Access Bridge software. The following is a list of some assistive tools that use the Java Access Bridge software to exchange data with $[officename]:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329	4			0	uk	ZoomText Screen Magnifier (version 7.11 or higher)(Windows)				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628	5			0	uk	Gnopernicus Screen Reader and Magnifier, using GNOME Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface (at-spi) and Java Accessibility API software				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474	6			0	uk	GNOME On Screen Keyboard (GOK), using GNOME at-spi and Java Accessibility API software				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061	24			0	uk	Supported Input Devices				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024	7			0	uk	$[officename] provides the ability to use alternative input devices for access to all functions of $[officename].				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045	8			0	uk	Screen magnification software allow users with low vision to work in $[officename] with caret and focus tracking.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811	9			0	uk	On-screen keyboards enable users to perform almost all data input and commands with a mouse.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379	10			0	uk	Screen readers allow visually impaired users to access $[officename] with text-to-speech and Braille displays.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149808	11			0	uk	When accessibility support in $[officename] is enabled, the Java Runtime Environment is loaded, and increases the startup time for $[officename].				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933	18			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010800.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - View\"\>$[officename] - View\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155430	19			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Appearance\"\>$[officename] - Appearance\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148617	20			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01013000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Accessibility\"\>$[officename] - Accessibility\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Error Report Tool				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150616				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>reports;error reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>crash reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>activating;Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616	17			0	uk	\<variable id=\"error_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/error_report.xhp\" name=\"Error Report Tool\"\>Error Report Tool\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	1			0	uk	The Error Report Tool starts automatically when a program crash occurs.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	2			0	uk	The Error Report Tool gathers all necessary information that can help the program developers to improve the code, so that in later versions this error can possibly be avoided. Please help us to improve the software and send the generated error report.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538	4			0	uk	Starting the Error Report Tool				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	5			0	uk	With most program crashes the Error Report Tool will start automatically.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154046	7			0	uk	Completing the Report				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335	8			0	uk	On the main Error Report Tool dialog, you can enter some additional information that may help the developers to localize the error. For example, if the error only appears after a change in your hardware or software environment, or if you clicked on a button, please include that information.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399	9			0	uk	Sending the Error Report				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	10			0	uk	The Error Report Tool uses the HTTP PUT / SOAP protocol to send the report data. You may optionally enter some descriptive text that will help us to identify the context of the program crash. Then click the \<emph\>Send\</emph\> button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	11			0	uk	You will not get an answer to your error report. If you need support, please visit the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\"\>support forum\</link\> on the Internet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526	12			0	uk	You may choose to respond to questions that the developers may have about the reported error. Mark the check box if you allow to be contacted by e-mail, should additional information be required. By default this box is not marked, so you will not get any e-mail.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	13			0	uk	What Data is Sent?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366	14			0	uk	The error report consists of several files. The main file contains information about the error type, operating system name and version, memory usage, and the description that you entered. You can click the \<emph\>Show Report\</emph\> button on the main dialog of the Error Report Tool to view what will get sent in the main file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177	15			0	uk	In addition, relevant memory contents and stack traces are gathered by some system standard tools ("dbhhelp.dll" on Windows systems, "pstack" on UNIX systems). This information will be sent also.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Using the Filter Navigator				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150322				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>filters; Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filter conditions;connecting\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	uk	\<variable id=\"filternavigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/filternavigator.xhp\"\>Using the Filter Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3150322	13			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterNavigator\"\>To connect several filter conditions with Boolean OR, click the \<emph\>Filter navigation\</emph\> icon on the filter bar.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> window appears.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711	14			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FILTER_NAVIGATOR\"\>The filter conditions that have been set appear in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. As soon as a filter is set, you see a blank filter entry at the bottom of the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. You can select this entry by clicking the word "Or". Once you have selected the blank filter entry, you can enter additional filter conditions in the form. These conditions are linked by Boolean OR to the previously defined conditions.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3145620	15			0	uk	The context menu can be called for each entry in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. \<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_FILTER_IS_NOT_NULL\"\>You can edit the filter conditions in this area directly as text. If you wish to check if a field has content or no content, you can select the filter conditions "empty" (SQL:"Is Null") or "not empty" (SQL: "Is not Null").\</ahelp\> It is also possible to delete the entry by using the context menu.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3156374	16			0	uk	You can move filter conditions in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> by dragging and dropping, or use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Up Arrow or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Down Arrow. To copy filter conditions, drag them while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156426				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>faxes; sending\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faxes;configuring $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as faxes \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>configuring;fax icon\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156426	5			0	uk	\<variable id=\"fax\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/fax.xhp\" name=\"Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\"\>Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	3			0	uk	To send a fax directly from $[officename], you need a fax modem and a fax driver that allows applications to communicate with the fax modem.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410	6			0	uk	Sending a Fax Through the Print Dialog				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	7			0	uk	Open the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog by choosing \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\> and select the fax driver in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> list box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135	8			0	uk	Clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\> opens the dialog for your fax driver, where you can select the fax recipient.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825	9			0	uk	Configuring $[officename] a Fax Icon				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822	10			0	uk	You can configure $[officename] so that a single click on an icon automatically sends the current document as a fax:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	11			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040400.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Print\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</link\>\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985	12			0	uk	Select the fax driver from the \<emph\>Fax\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EB				0	uk	Click the arrow icon at the end of the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar. In the drop-down menu, choose \<emph\>Customize\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	uk	The \<emph\>Toolbar\</emph\>s tab page of the \<emph\>Customize\</emph\> dialog appears.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FA				0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	uk	Select the "Documents" category, then select the "Send Default Fax" command.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	uk	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10712				0	uk	On the \<emph\>Toolbars\</emph\> tab page, click the down arrow button to position the new icon where you want it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	uk	Your \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar now has a new icon to send the current document as a fax.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Creating XML Filters 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>testing XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XML filters;creating/testing\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id1413922				0	uk	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_create.xhp\"\>Creating XML Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053D				0	uk	Creating an XML Filter for %PRODUCTNAME				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109A9				0	uk	When you create an XML filter for %PRODUCTNAME, you need to design an \<emph\>XSLT stylesheet\</emph\> that can convert to and from the OpenDocument XML file format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B0				0	uk	For more information about the OpenDocument XML format, go to \<link href=\"https://xml.openoffice.org/\"\>https://xml.openoffice.org/\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C5				0	uk	If you want, you can include a \<emph\>template\</emph\> with your filter to apply %PRODUCTNAME styles to an XML document that you import.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CC				0	uk	You can also include the \<emph\>Document Type Definition\</emph\> (DTD) for the external XML format so you can validate the XML format, for example, when you test the filter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10531				0	uk	To Create an XML Filter				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E0				0	uk	Create an XSLT transformation \<emph\>stylesheet\</emph\> that maps the elements of the external XML format to the elements of the OpenDocument XML file format and back again.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E8				0	uk	Create a template that assigns %PRODUCTNAME styles to elements in the external XML format when you import a file in this format into %PRODUCTNAME.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	uk	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, create a text document, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109F4				0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109FC				0	uk	In the \<emph\>XML Filter\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and define the properties of the filter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A03				0	uk	In the \<emph\>Filter Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the XML filter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CA1				0	uk	This name is displayed in the \<emph\>XML Filter Settings\</emph\> dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A09				0	uk	In the \<emph\>Application\</emph\> box, select the %PRODUCTNAME application that the filter is for.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0F				0	uk	In the \<emph\>Name of File Type\</emph\> box, enter the file type that the filter is for.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	uk	This name is displayed in the list of file types in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\>, \<emph\>Export\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialogs.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A15				0	uk	In the \<emph\>File extension\</emph\> box, enter the extension for the exported file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1B				0	uk	To differentiate the file from other XML files, enter an extension other than *.xml.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1F				0	uk	On the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page, define the transformation properties for the filter.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	uk	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DocType\</emph\> box, enter the document type identifier for the external file format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D0E				0	uk	This identifier is used to detect the file type on import.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A2C				0	uk	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DTD\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the DTD for the external file format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D1F				0	uk	This DTD is used to validate the files on export.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A32				0	uk	In the \<emph\>XSLT for export\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from OpenDocument format to the external format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A38				0	uk	In the \<emph\>XSLT for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name to the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from the external format to OpenDocument format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A3E				0	uk	(Optional) In the \<emph\>Template for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and name of the template that defines the %PRODUCTNAME styles that are used in the imported file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A44				0	uk	The files that are specified on the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page are copied to the local %PRODUCTNAME users directory.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A4C				0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A56				0	uk	To Test an XML Filter				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A5A				0	uk	You can perform basic tests on a custom XML filter in %PRODUCTNAME.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A91				0	uk	The document is not altered by these tests. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A60				0	uk	Create or open a text document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A67				0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A6F				0	uk	In the list of filters, select the filter that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Test XSLTs\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A82				0	uk	To test an \<emph\>Export\</emph\> Filter, do one of the following in the \<emph\>Export\</emph\> area of the dialog:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DEB				0	uk	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>, select the %PRODUCTNAME document that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DF7				0	uk	To test the current document, click \<emph\>Current Document\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A99				0	uk	To test an \<emph\>Import\</emph\> Filter, click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> area of the dialog, select a document, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E32				0	uk	To validate the transformed file against the specified DTD, click \<emph\>Validate\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_id8579668				0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter.xhp\"\>About XML Filters\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
