helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154788				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>documents; comparing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comparisons;document versions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changes;comparing to original\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154788	32			0	uk	\<variable id=\"redlining_doccompare\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_doccompare.xhp\" name=\"Comparing Versions of a Document\"\>Comparing Versions of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	uk	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3995178				0	uk	Imagine you have some co-authors or reviewers who collaborate with you writing your original document. One day you send out copies of your document to all reviewers. You ask them to edit the copy and send it back.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id9948423				0	uk	Normally, the reviewers enable change tracking by \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> and you can easily see the changes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421	33			0	uk	If one of the authors has made changes to a document without recording them, you can compare the changed document to your original document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087	35			0	uk	Open the reviewer's document and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Compare Document\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4208807				0	uk	You should always start with opening the newer document and compare it with the older document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	36			0	uk	A file selection dialog appears. Select your older original document and confirm the dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762	37			0	uk	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> combines both documents into the reviewer's document. All text passages that occur in the reviewer's document but not in the original are identified as having been inserted, and all text passages that got deleted by the reviewer are identified as deletions.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674	38			0	uk	You can now accept or reject the insertions and deletions. At the end you may save the reviewer's document as a new original with a new name.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Printing in Black and White				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150125				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>printing; black and white\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>black and white printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colors; not printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; printing in black\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150125	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"print_blackwhite\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/print_blackwhite.xhp\" name=\"Printing in Black and White\"\>Printing in Black and White\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499	3			0	uk	Printing text and graphics in black and white				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	4			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. The \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page of the dialog opens.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892	5			0	uk	Click on \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. This opens the Properties dialog for your printer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313	6			0	uk	Select the option to print in black and white. For further information, refer to the user's manual of your printer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	7			0	uk	Confirm the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog and click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113	8			0	uk	The current document will be printed in black and white.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653	9			0	uk	Printing in black and white in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	10			0	uk	Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress or Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Draw, as appropriate.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275	11			0	uk	Then choose \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573	12			0	uk	Under \<emph\>Quality,\</emph\> select either \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> or \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307	13			0	uk	When either of these options is selected, all presentations or drawings will be printed without color. If you only want to print in black for the \<emph\>current\</emph\> print job, select the option in \<emph\>File - Print - %PRODUCTNAME Draw/Impress\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149786	15			0	uk	               \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> converts all colors to a maximum of 256 gradations from black to white. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610	16			0	uk	               \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> converts all colors into the two values black and white. All borders around objects are printed black. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896	17			0	uk	Printing only text in black and white				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559	18			0	uk	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer you can choose to print color-formatted text in black and white. You can specify this either for all subsequent text documents to be printed, or only for the current printing process.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150358	19			0	uk	Printing all text documents with black and white text				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541	20			0	uk	Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer or Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer/Web.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084	21			0	uk	Then choose \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910	22			0	uk	Under \<emph\>Contents,\</emph\> mark \<emph\>Print black\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762	23			0	uk	All text documents or HTML documents will be printed with black text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148920	24			0	uk	Printing the current text document with black and white text				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933	25			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. Then click the \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> tab.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667	27			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Print text in black\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
