helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807	18			0	uk	From now on, if you save a document, the \<emph\>File type \</emph\>will be set according to your choice. Of course, you still can select another file type in the file save dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423	19			0	uk	Opening Microsoft Office Files by Default				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153092	20			0	uk	Converting Many Microsoft Office Files into OpenDocument Format				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986	21			0	uk	The \<emph\>Document Converter Wizard\</emph\> will copy and convert all Microsoft Office files in a folder into $[officename] documents in the OpenDocument file format. You can specify the folder to be read, and the folder where the converted files are to be saved.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3150486	22			0	uk	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01130000.xhp\" name=\"File - AutoPilot - Document Converter\"\>\<emph\>File - Wizards - Document Converter\</emph\>\</link\> to start the wizard.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154319	23			0	uk	Macros in Microsoft Office and $[officename]				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3154921	24			0	uk	With a few exceptions, Microsoft Office and $[officename] cannot run the same macro code. Microsoft Office uses VBA (Visual Basic for Applications) code, and $[officename] uses Basic code based on the $[officename] API (Application Program Interface) environment. Although the programming language is the same, the objects and methods are different.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id0804200804173539				0	uk	The most recent versions of %PRODUCTNAME can run some Excel Visual Basic scripts if you enable this feature at \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - VBA Properties\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577	25			0	uk	If you use macros in one of the applications and want to use the same functionality in the other application, you must edit the macros. $[officename] can load the macros that are contained within Microsoft Office files and you can then view and edit the macro code in the $[officename] \<link href=\"text/shared/main0600.xhp\" name=\"Basic IDE\"\>Basic IDE\</link\> editor.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596	26			0	uk	You can choose to preserve or delete VBA macros				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144	27			0	uk	Open a Microsoft Office document that contains VBA macro code. Change only the normal contents (text, cells, graphics), and do not edit the macros. Save the document as a Microsoft Office file type. Open the file in Microsoft Office, and the VBA macros will run as before.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011	28			0	uk	You may delete the VBA macros from the Microsoft Office file on loading or on saving.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366	29			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01130100.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - VBA Properties\"\>Load/Save - VBA Properties\</link\>\</emph\> to set the VBA macro handling of $[officename].				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Editing Hyperlinks				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153910				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; editing hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>buttons;editing hyperlink buttons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL;changing hyperlink URLs\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910	11			0	uk	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Hyperlinks\"\>Editing Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id4124881				0	uk	When you \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click a hyperlink in a Writer document, your web browser opens with the requested web address. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the hyperlink and open the context menu by Shift+F10, then choose Open Hyperlink.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071	26			0	uk	Change the text of a hyperlink as follows				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	12			0	uk	In Writer documents, you can click anywhere into a hyperlink and edit the visible text. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id2690511				0	uk	If you leave the hyperlink by positioning the cursor somewhere else, only the visible text will be changed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id1983092				0	uk	If you leave the hyperlink by entering a space character directly following the last character, the AutoCorrect - if enabled - will change the target URL to be the same as the visible text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id333262				0	uk	In all document types, you can open the Hyperlink dialog to edit a hyperlink. First set the cursor into the hyperlink or directly in front of the hyperlink, then click the Hyperlink icon on the Standard bar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158432	30			0	uk	Change the URL of a hyperlink as follows				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503	31			0	uk	Option 1: As described above, open \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Dialog\"\>Hyperlink Dialog\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119	32			0	uk	Option 2: Open \<link href=\"text/shared/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Bar\"\>Hyperlink Bar\</link\> (\<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>). Click on the hyperlink, do not release the mouse button and drag the hyperlink to the Hyperlink Bar. Edit the URL on the Hyperlink Bar and press the Return key.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148686	33			0	uk	Change the attribute of all hyperlinks				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943	25			0	uk	Open the Styles and Formatting window.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10826				0	uk	Click the Character Styles icon.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	uk	Right-click the "Internet Link" or "Visited Internet Link" character style, and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	uk	In the dialog, select the new attributes, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147530	34			0	uk	Edit a hyperlink button				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361	13			0	uk	If the hyperlink is a button, click on the border to select it, or press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while clicking. Open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog through the context menu. You can edit the label text under "Caption," and modify the address in the "URL" field.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>ImageMap; editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editors; ImageMap editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>images; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hotspots;adding to images\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>URL;in pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10631				0	uk	\<variable id=\"imagemap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/imagemap.xhp\"\>Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	uk	An ImageMap allows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a picture in your document. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	uk	You can draw three types of hotspots: rectangles, ellipses, and polygons. When you click a hotspot, the URL is opened in the browser window or frame that you specify. You can also specify the text that appears when your mouse rests on the hotspot.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10677				0	uk	To add a clickable hotspot to an image				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	uk	Position the cursor where you want the ImageMap in your document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>, select and insert a bitmap picture.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	uk	With the picture selected, choose \<emph\>Edit - ImageMap\</emph\>. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>, which displays the picture at the background.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	uk	Use the icons in the ImageMap Editor to draw a hotspot shape, for example a rectangle, over the image at the background.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	uk	You can see an extended help text on the functions of each icon when you enable Extended Help in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	uk	Enter the "Address" URL that will be shown in a Web browser when the user clicks the hotspot.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	uk	Optionally, enter the "Text" that will be shown as a tip when the user points the mouse to the hotspot.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B3				0	uk	Click the Apply button to apply your changes, and close the ImageMap Editor.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	uk	Save the document in the %PRODUCTNAME or HTML format.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	uk	You may save the ImageMap as a file and upload that file to a Web server, for example.				20220827 09:49:47
