helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3154145	12			0	uk	Double-click the white area of the ruler to set one tab. The \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\> dialog appears with the \<emph\>Tabs\</emph\> tab page open.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748	21			0	uk	Moving Tabs on the Ruler				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145264	22			0	uk	Move individual tab stops on the ruler using the mouse.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156	13			0	uk	To move several tab stops on the ruler, press the Shift key before you click a tab. Drag one tab while continuing to press Shift to move that tab as well as all the tabs to the right of it. The spacing between those tabs remains the same.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3147349	23			0	uk	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you drag a tab on the ruler to move that tab and all the tabs to the right of it. This results in the spacing between those tabs changing proportionally to their distance from the margin.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146146	24			0	uk	Changing the Properties of Tabs				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145646	16			0	uk	To change tab type, click the tab you want to change on the ruler, then right-click to open the context menu.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729	25			0	uk	Deleting Tabs				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3148879	17			0	uk	To delete a tab, hold down the mouse button while you drag the tab outside the ruler.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151074	26			0	uk	Changing the Defaults				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3151059	14			0	uk	If you want to change the settings of your default tab stops, you will find further information under \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070500.xhp\" name=\"Drawing - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Draw - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070500.xhp\" name=\"Presentation - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>(module name) - General\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> in the Options dialog box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972	15			0	uk	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\> of the ruler allows you to change the displayed units of measurement. These changes are only valid until you exit $[officename], and they only apply to the ruler on whose context menu you made the change. If you want to change the ruler measurement units permanently, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - [Document type] - View\</emph\> and change the measurement unit there.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3148429	30			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/swriter/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Ruler\"\>Ruler\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Registering and Deleting a Database 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	bm_id4724570				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>databases;registering (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;registered databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	uk	\<variable id=\"data_register\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_register.xhp\"\>Registering and Deleting a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	uk	Data from any \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> can be registered to %PRODUCTNAME. To register means to tell %PRODUCTNAME where the data is located, how it is organized, how to get that data, and more. Once the database is registered, you can use the menu command \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to access the data records from your text documents and spreadsheets.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	uk	To register an existing database file:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	uk	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E1				0	uk	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and select the database file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	uk	To remove a registered database from %PRODUCTNAME				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	uk	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10719				0	uk	Select the database file and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F3				0	uk	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FB				0	uk	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154136				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>graphics, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting and editing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>illustrations, see pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pixel graphics; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invert filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>smoothing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sharpening filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remove noise filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>solarization filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aging filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>posterizing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pop-art filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charcoal sketches filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mosaic filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filters;pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154136	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"insert_bitmap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_bitmap.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\"\>Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811	2			0	uk	Inserting Bitmaps				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	3			0	uk	A bitmap image can be inserted in $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209	4			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236	5			0	uk	Select the file. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box you can restrict the selection to certain file types.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	6			0	uk	Click the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box if you want a link to the original file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306	7			0	uk	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is marked, whenever the document is updated and loaded the bitmap image is reloaded. The editing steps that you have carried out in the local copy of the image in the document are re-applied and the image is displayed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336	8			0	uk	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is not marked, you are always working with the copy created when the graphic was first inserted.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824	26			0	uk	To embed graphics that were first inserted as links, go to \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Break Link\</emph\> button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384	9			0	uk	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the image.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303	10			0	uk	Editing Bitmaps				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id187078				0	uk	Icons on the Picture bar				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552	11			0	uk	When you select the bitmap image, the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar offers you the tools for editing the image. Only a local copy is edited in the document, even if you have inserted an image as a link.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413	12			0	uk	The \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar may look slightly different depending to the module you are using.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	13			0	uk	A number of filters are located on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\" name=\"Graphic Filter\"\>Graphic \<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar, which you can open with the icon on the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7055574				0	uk	The original picture file will not be changed by the filters. Filters are applied to a picture only inside the document. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273	14			0	uk	Some of the filters open a dialog, which you can use to select, for example, the intensity of the filter. Most filters can be applied multiple times to increase the filter effect.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105	15			0	uk	In $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress, you can add text and graphics, select these objects together with the bitmap, and export the selection as a new bitmap image.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id2572405				0	uk	The Picture dialog				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id6457411				0	uk	Right-click the picture and choose \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> from the submenu to open a properties dialog.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7991882				0	uk	Change the properties of the selected picture, then click OK.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153574	16			0	uk	Saving Bitmaps				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576	17			0	uk	If you want to save in a format such as GIF, JPEG or TIFF, you must select and export the bitmap image.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803544667				0	uk	To export a bitmap in Draw or Impress:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414	18			0	uk	Select the bitmap image. You can also select additional objects, such as text, to be exported with the image by pressing the shift key while selecting or by opening a selection frame around all objects.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618	19			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> dialog opens.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3157139				0	uk	The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> command writes the picture with all applied filter effects to a file. The \<emph\>Save as Picture\</emph\> command in the context menu saves the picture without any filter effects, if the picture was inserted as a linked picture. An embedded picture will always be saved or exported with filters applied.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443	20			0	uk	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> field, select the file format you want, for example GIF or JPEG.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462	21			0	uk	If you only want to export the selected objects, mark the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150874	22			0	uk	If \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not marked, the entire page of the document is exported.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417	23			0	uk	Enter a name for the file and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803525078				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To export a bitmap in Writer: Right-click the bitmap, choose Save Graphics. You see the Graphics Export dialog. Enter a file name and select a file type.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id1033051				0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\"\>Graphic Filter Bar from the Picture Bar\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Integrating new UNO components				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149760				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>add-ons, see UNO components\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>UNO components;integrating new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;UNO components\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149760	7			0	uk	\<variable id=\"integratinguno\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/integratinguno.xhp\" name=\"Integrating new UNO components\"\>Integrating new UNO components\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571	1			0	uk	Programmers can write and integrate their own UNO (Universal Network Objects) components to $[officename]. Those new components can be added to the $[officename] menus and toolbars; we call them "Add-Ons".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751	2			0	uk	The integration of new components is supported by some tools and services. Details can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide. The three main steps are as follows:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	3			0	uk	Register the new components within $[officename]. This can be accomplished using the tool \<item type=\"literal\"\>unopkg\</item\>, which can be found in {installpath}\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>/ \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\\\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>program.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	4			0	uk	Integrate the new components as services. The ProtocolHandler and JobDispatch services assist you; more information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	5			0	uk	Change the user interface (menus or toolbars). This can be done almost automatically by writing an XML text file that describes the changes. More information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110	6			0	uk	The Add-Ons can extend the functionality of $[officename]. They are not related to the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Add-Ins\"\>Add-Ins\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Add-Ins\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> that provide new functions for $[officename] Calc.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Using and Editing Database Reports 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147834				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>database reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;opening and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;database reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;templates\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149178	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"data_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_report.xhp\" name=\"Create, Use, and Edit Database Reports\"\>Using and Editing Database Reports\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609	13			0	uk	Using a Report				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265	14			0	uk	%PRODUCTNAME stores the information about the created reports in the database file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758	15			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> and select the database file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054	16			0	uk	In the database file window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280	18			0	uk	Double-click one of the report names to open the report.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	uk	These links are added automatically when you create a new report by the Report Wizard or in the Report Builder window.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id1695608				0	uk	Editing a Report Created in the Report Builder Window				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id7510910				0	uk	Right-click the name of a report in the database file window, then choose Edit.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id8138065				0	uk	The Report Builder window opens with the report's information loaded. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id5086825				0	uk	Use the toolbars and menu commands and drag-and-drop to edit the report as stated in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\> guide.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id4747154				0	uk	Execute the report to see the resulting report document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153104	19			0	uk	Editing a Report Created by the Report Wizard				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863	20			0	uk	On the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100500.xhp\" name=\"last dialog page of the Report AutoPilot\"\>last dialog page of the Report Wizard\</link\>, you can choose to edit the report template before you use the report.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3155431	22			0	uk	You can edit the page styles for the first page and the following pages of the report as well as the paragraph styles, the number formats, the printed field labels, and more.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D7				0	uk	Unless you have a thorough understanding of the database the report accesses, do not edit the SQL statement, database name, the hidden form controls, or the related information on the report.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Languages Using Complex Text Layout				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153662				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>CTL;complex text layout languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>languages;complex text layout\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;CTL languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text layout for special languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>right-to-left text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering text from right to left\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bi-directional writing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hindi;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hebrew;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Arabic;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Thai;entering text\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662	13			0	uk	\<variable id=\"ctl\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ctl.xhp\" name=\"Languages Using Complex Text Layout\"\>Languages Using Complex Text Layout\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618	10			0	uk	Currently, $[officename] supports Hindi, Thai, Hebrew, and Arabic as \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#ctl\" name=\"CTL languages\"\>CTL languages\</link\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3155420	11			0	uk	If you select the text flow from right to left, embedded Western text still runs from left to right. The cursor responds to the arrow keys in that Right Arrow moves it "to the text end" and Left Arrow "to the text start".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609	1			0	uk	You can change the text writing direction directly be pressing one of the following keys:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758	2			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+D or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Right Shift Key - switch to right-to-left text entry				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047	3			0	uk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+A or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Left Shift Key - switch to left-to-right text entry				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656	4			0	uk	The modifier-only key combinations only work when CTL support is enabled.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541	5			0	uk	In multicolumn pages, sections or frames that are formatted with text flow from right to left, the first column is the right column and the last column is the left column.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797	6			0	uk	In $[officename] Writer text formatted in \<emph\>Thai language\</emph\> has the following features:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280	7			0	uk	In paragraphs with justified alignment, the characters are stretched to flush the lines at the margins. In other languages the spaces between words are stretched.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909	8			0	uk	Use the Delete key to delete a whole composite character. Use the Backspace key to delete the last part of the previous composite character.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809	9			0	uk	Use the Right or Left Arrow key to jump to the next or previous whole composite character. To position the cursor into a composite character, use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow key.				20220827 09:49:47
