helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145071				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; data source view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data source view; drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;from data source view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;from data source view\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071	10			0	uk	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_beamer\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_beamer.xhp\" name=\"Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View\"\>Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111	34			0	uk	A fast way of copying from a data source into a text or spreadsheet document, or of creating forms based on a data source, is by drag-and-drop.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3155390\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155390\"\>Mouse pointer copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	35			0	uk	Copying with Drag-and-Drop				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	28			0	uk	If you want to reverse a drag-and-drop, position the cursor in your document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656	46			0	uk	It is also possible to copy by drag-and-drop from a document into a data source:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379	47			0	uk	A text table or the selected range of a spreadsheet can be dragged using drag-and-drop to a table container in the data source explorer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211	48			0	uk	Plain text can be copied using drag-and-drop from one document to a data field in the data source view.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145421	36			0	uk	Using data in a text document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	12			0	uk	You can insert a database field in a text document by dragging a field name from the column header of the data source view into the document. This is especially useful when designing form letters. Simply drag the desired fields - home address, form of address, and so on - into your document.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153105	37			0	uk	To insert a complete record, select the corresponding header and drag it into the document. When you release the mouse button, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Insert database columns\"\>\<emph\>Insert database columns\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears, in which you can decide whether to use all database fields, and whether to copy the data into the document as text, a table or fields. All currently selected records will be inserted.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230	39			0	uk	Applying data to a table document				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	40			0	uk	You can insert one or more records into the current sheet of a spreadsheet by selecting the rows in the data source view and dragging and dropping them into the spreadsheet. The data is inserted at the place where you release the mouse button.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149766	42			0	uk	Inserting controls in a text form				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132	43			0	uk	When you create a text form linked to a database, you can generate controls by drag-and-drop from the data source view.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562	45			0	uk	When you drag a database column into the text document, you insert a field. If you hold down Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging, a text field is inserted, grouped with an appropriate label field. The text field already contains all the database information that you need for the form.				20220827 09:49:47
