helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267	7			0	uk	Some toolbar icons, for example the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, can open another toolbar. Click the arrow next to the icon to open a toolbar containing further icons.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450	8			0	uk	You now have a choice: either click the icon that you want to activate, or seize the toolbar by its title bar and drag it while holding down the mouse button. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id733970				0	uk	Context of Toolbars				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id341196				0	uk	Some toolbars open automatically depending on the context. For example, when you click inside a table in a text document, the Table toolbar opens. When you click inside a numbered paragraph, the Bullets and Numbering toolbar opens.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id4224372				0	uk	To Close a Toolbar Temporarily				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id295724				0	uk	Click the icon in the toolbar's title bar, or choose \<emph\>Close Toolbar\</emph\> from the context menu. The toolbar will be shown automatically again when the context becomes active again.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id1905575				0	uk	To Close a Toolbar Permanently				20220827 09:49:47
