helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326	2			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:TABPAGE:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT\"\>Defines settings for HTML pages.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154897	3			0	uk	Font sizes				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673	4			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:NUMERICFIELD:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:NF_SIZE7\"\>Use the spin buttons \<emph\>Size 1\</emph\> to \<emph\>Size 7\</emph\> to define the respective font sizes for the HTML <font size=1> to <font size=7> tags.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148943	5			0	uk	Import				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	6			0	uk	Defines the settings for importing HTML documents.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id6065248				0	uk	Use 'English (USA)' locale for numbers				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id8023926				0	uk	When importing numbers from an HTML page, the decimal separator and the thousands separator characters differ according to the locale of the HTML page. The clipboard however contains no information about the locale. For example, the characters "1.000" copied from a German Web page most possibly mean "one thousand" because the period is the thousands separator in a German locale. If copied from an English Web page, the same characters stand for the number 1 as in "one dot zero zero zero".				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id7658314				0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If not checked, numbers will be interpreted according to the setting in \<emph\>Language Settings - Language of - Locale setting\</emph\> in the Options dialog box. If checked, numbers will be interpreted as 'English (USA)' locale.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068	7			0	uk	Import unknown HTML tags as fields				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149295	8			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:CB_UNKNOWN_TAGS\"\>Mark this check box if you want \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tags\"\>tags\</link\> that are not recognized by $[officename] to be imported as fields.\</ahelp\> For an opening tag, an HTML_ON field will be created with the value of the tag name. For a closing tag, an HTML_OFF will be created. These fields will be converted to tags in the HTML export.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797	43			0	uk	Ignore font settings				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149202	44			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:CB_IGNORE_FONTNAMES\"\>Mark this check box to ignore all font settings when importing. The fonts that were defined in the HTML Page Style will be the fonts that will be used. \</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151177	9			0	uk	Export				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449	10			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:LISTBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:LB_EXPORT\"\>Defines the settings for exporting HTML documents.\</ahelp\> To export in HTML format select the \<emph\>HTML Document\</emph\> file type in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>\<emph\>Save As\</emph\>\</link\> dialog. You can find further instructions in the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000020.xhp\" name=\"Import and export filters\"\>Import and export filters\</link\> description.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606	42			0	uk	To optimize the HTML export, select a browser or HTML standard from the Export box. If "$[officename] Writer" is selected, specific $[officename] Writer instructions are exported.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155132	16			0	uk	$[officename] Basic				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120	17			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:CB_STARBASIC\"\>Mark this check box to include the $[officename] Basic instructions when exporting to HTML format.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872	29			0	uk	You must activate this option before you create the $[officename] Basic Script, since otherwise it will not be inserted. $[officename] Basic Scripts must be located in the header of the HTML document. Once you have created the macro in the $[officename] Basic IDE, it appears in the source text of the HTML document in the header.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664	45			0	uk	Display warning				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150420	46			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_HTMLOPT:CB_STARBASIC_WARNING\"\>If this field is marked, when exporting to HTML a warning is shown that %PRODUCTNAME Basic macros will be lost.\</ahelp\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729	28			0	uk	Print layout				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145254	39			0	uk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you mark this field, the print layout of the current document is exported as well.\</ahelp\> It can be read by $[officename], Netscape Navigator, and MS Internet Explorer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276	41			0	uk	The HTML filter supports CSS2 (Cascading Style Sheets Level 2) for printing documents. These capabilities are only effective if print layout export is activated.				20220827 09:49:47
