helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153088	17			0	uk	When saving in another format than Microsoft Format, the Microsoft Basic Code is not saved. For example, if the document contains Microsoft Basic Code and you save it in $[officename] format, you will be warned that the Microsoft Basic Code will not be saved.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246	18			0	uk	The \<emph\>Save original Basic code\</emph\> checkbox takes precedence over the \<emph\>Load Basic code\</emph\> check box. If both boxes are marked and you edit the disabled Basic Code in the $[officename] Basic IDE, the original Microsoft Basic code will be saved when saving in the Microsoft format. A message appears to inform you of this.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148946	19			0	uk	To remove any possible Microsoft Basic macro viruses from the Microsoft document, unmark the \<emph\>Save Original Basic Code \</emph\>check box and save the document in Microsoft format. The document will be saved without the Microsoft Basic code.				20220827 09:49:47
