helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	4			0	uk	To open the\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw \<emph\>Mode \</emph\>toolbar, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Effects \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar. In %PRODUCTNAME Impress, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Mode\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150199	6			0	uk	Rotate				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148489	40			0	uk	Rotates or skews the selected 2D object(s) around a pivot point. Drag a corner handle of the object in the direction you want to rotate it. To skew an object, drag a center handle in the direction you want to skew it.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022	9			0	uk	Each slide has only one pivot point. Double-click an object to move the pivot point to the center of the object. You can also drag the pivot point to a new location on the screen, and then rotate the object.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914	10			0	uk	If you select a group that includes a 3D object, only the 3D object is rotated. You cannot skew a 3D object, instead, you can rotate it about the X and Y axes by dragging the center handles.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	uk	\<image id=\"img_id3153811\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectrotatemode.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153811\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20220827 09:49:47
