helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id7954954				0	uk	If you are using a mouse with a scroll wheel, you can hold down Ctrl and turn the wheel to change the zoom factor in all main modules of %PRODUCTNAME.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116	14			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut keys for presentations\"\>Shortcut keys for presentations\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Using Gluepoints				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	bm_id0919200803534995				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>glue points;using\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	uk	\<variable id=\"gluepoints\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/gluepoints.xhp\"\>Using Gluepoints\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803040964				0	uk	In Impress and Draw, you can connect each two shapes with a line called a \<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10100000.xhp\"\>connector\</link\>. When you draw a connector between shapes, the connector will be attached to a gluepoint on each shape. Each shape has some default gluepoints, and the positions of the default gluepoints depend on the specific shape. You can add your own custom gluepoints to a shape and then attach connectors to the custom gluepoints.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041099				0	uk	To add and edit gluepoints				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id091920080304108				0	uk	Do one of the following:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041082				0	uk	Click the \<emph\>Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Drawing toolbar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041186				0	uk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Glue Points\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041160				0	uk	Click the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Gluepoints toolbar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041115				0	uk	Click inside the shape where you want to add the new gluepoint.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041133				0	uk	If the shape is filled, you can click anywhere inside the shape. If the shape is unfilled, you can click the border to insert a glue point. Once inserted, you can drag the glue point to another position inside the shape.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041250				0	uk	With the four icons next to the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon, you choose the directions which will be permitted for a connector at this gluepoint. You can choose one or more directions for a particular gluepoint.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041298				0	uk	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is active, the gluepoint moves when you resize the object to keep its position relative to the object borders.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041223				0	uk	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is not active, the icons next to it are no longer grayed out. With these icons you can decide where a gluepoint will be placed when the size of the object is changed.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Inserting Layers				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148797				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>layers; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; layers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;layer properties\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797	9			0	uk	\<variable id=\"layer_new\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layer_new.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Layers\"\>Inserting Layers\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	uk	Drawings in %PRODUCTNAME Draw support layers.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	uk	Right-click the layer tab area at the bottom.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418	11			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Insert Layer\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	12			0	uk	Type a name for the layer in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	15			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>area, set the options for the layer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964	13			0	uk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The new layer automatically becomes the active layer.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3154658	16			0	uk	To change the properties of a layer, click the name tab of the layer, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Layer\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3153814	17			0	uk	You cannot change the name of or delete a predefined \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw layer.				20220827 09:49:47
