helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715	7			0	uk	You can add a blank $[officename] Calc spreadsheet to a slide as an OLE object.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749	3			0	uk	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	18			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - OLE- Object\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Create new\</emph\> and select the %PRODUCTNAME Spreadsheet. Click OK. Click in the spreadsheet to enter your data. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2466505				0	uk	Click outside the spreadsheet to view the slide.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870	9			0	uk	To resize the spreadsheet without resizing the cells, double-click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle. To resize the cells of the spreadsheet, click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150215	11			0	uk	Inserting a spreadsheet from a file				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154765	19			0	uk	When you insert an existing spreadsheet into your slide, changes that are made to the original spreadsheet file are not updated on your slide. You can, however, make changes to the spreadsheet in your slide.				20220827 09:49:47
