helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153191	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/footer.xhp\" name=\"Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\"\>Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\</link\> \</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1356547				0	uk	Every slide is based on a slide master. The text, pictures, tables, fields or other objects that you place on the slide master are visible as a background on all slides that are based on that slide master.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id704672				0	uk	Masters exist for slides, notes, and handouts. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8403576				0	uk	To edit a slide master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the slide master.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5641651				0	uk	To edit a notes master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Notes Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the notes master.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1583300				0	uk	To edit a handout master, click the Handout tab above the slide. Click the Normal tab to leave the handout master.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id7251808				0	uk	Adding predefined header or footer objects				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5015411				0	uk	Every type of master has some predefined areas to hold the date, footer, and slide numbers. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8217413				0	uk	When you switch to the master view, you can move that areas to any position on the master. You can enter additional text and resize the areas. You can select the contents of the areas and apply text formats. For example, you can change the font size or color.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id7549668				0	uk	A predefined Header Area is available only for notes and handouts. If you want a header on all slides, you can move the Footer Area on the slide master to the top.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1829889				0	uk	Objects that you insert on a slide master are visible on all slides that are based on that slide master.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8843043				0	uk	Choose \<emph\>View - Header and Footer\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1876583				0	uk	You see a dialog with two tab pages: \<emph\>Slide\</emph\> and \<emph\>Notes and Handouts\</emph\> where you can enter contents to the predefined areas. 				20220827 09:49:47
