helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150021	55			0	uk	Натисніть \<emph\>Гаразд\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145244	56			0	uk	To use an image for the slide background				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148394	57			0	uk	You can display an entire image as a slide background, or you can tile the image to produce a patterned background.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156064	58			0	uk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3145356	59			0	uk	In the \<emph\>Fill \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>, and then click an image in the list.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150757	60			0	uk	If you want to use a custom image for the slide background, close the \<emph\>Page Setup \</emph\>dialog, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Bitmaps \</emph\>tab, and then click \<emph\>Import\</emph\>. Locate the image you want to import and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When you return to the \<emph\>Background \</emph\>tab, the image you imported will be in the \<emph\>Bitmap \</emph\>list.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153151	61			0	uk	Do one of the following:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150263	62			0	uk	To display the entire image as the background, clear the \<emph\>Tile \</emph\>check box in the \<emph\>Position \</emph\>area, and then select \<emph\>AutoFit\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149756	63			0	uk	To tile the image on the background, select \<emph\>Tile\</emph\>, and set the \<emph\>Size\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> options for the image.				20220827 09:49:47
