helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145828	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"defining_conditions\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\"\>Визначення умов\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145242	13			0	uk	Conditions are logical expressions that you can use to control the display of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\"\>fields\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\"\>sections\</link\> in your document. Although the following examples apply to fields, they also apply to sections.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147171	93			0	uk	You can define conditions for the following field types:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151185	14			0	uk	Conditional text: displays text A if the condition is true, or text B if the condition is false.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149289	15			0	uk	Hidden text: hides the contents of the field if the condition is true.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145412	16			0	uk	Прихований абзац: приховує абзац, якщо умова істинна				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515	17			0	uk	Any record and next record: controls the access to database records.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149802	18			0	uk	The simplest way to define a condition is to type the logical expression directly in a \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box using the following values:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153677	19			0	uk	TRUE				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960	20			0	uk	The condition is always met. You can also enter any value not equal to 0 as the conditional text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155900	21			0	uk	FALSE				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154191	22			0	uk	The condition is not met. You can also enter the value 0.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147090	23			0	uk	If you leave the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box empty, the condition is interpreted as not being met.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148980	24			0	uk	When you define a condition, use the same \<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\"\>elements\</link\> for defining a formula, namely comparative operators, mathematical and statistical functions, number formats, variables and constants.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153638	25			0	uk	You can use the following types of variables when you define a condition:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135	27			0	uk	Predefined \<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\"\>$[officename] variables\</link\> that use statistics on document properties				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156273	26			0	uk	Custom variables, that are a created with the "Set variable" field				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149174	94			0	uk	Змінні на основі даних користувача				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145781	28			0	uk	Змінні на основі вмісту полів бази даних				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916	29			0	uk	You cannot use internal variables, such as page and chapter numbers, in condition expression.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151375	30			0	uk	Умови і змінні				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150122	31			0	uk	The following examples use a variable called "x":				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147417	32			0	uk	x == 1 або x EQ 1				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147500	33			0	uk	Умова істинна, якщо "х" кратне пі.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145259	34			0	uk	x != 1 або x NEQ 1				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150551	35			0	uk	Умова істинна, якщо "х" кратне пі.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147749	36			0	uk	sinx == 0				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146345	37			0	uk	Умова істинна, якщо "х" кратне пі.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846	38			0	uk	To use comparative operators with strings, the operands must be bounded by double quotation marks:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151078	39			0	uk	x == "ABC" або x EQ "ABC"				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150162	40			0	uk	Checks if variable "x" contains (true) the "ABC" string, or not (false).				20220827 09:49:47
