helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B0E				0	uk	The space character is appended after you type the first character of the next word after the auto-completed word. The space character is suppressed if the next character is a delimiter, such as a full stop or a new line character.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CC				0	uk	To Define the Accept Key				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B20				0	uk	Choose the key to accept the suggested word using the \<emph\>Accept with\</emph\> list box.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D2				0	uk	To Select the Minimum Number of Characters				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B36				0	uk	Use the \<emph\>Min. word length\</emph\> box to set the minimum number of characters a word must have to be collected into the list.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	uk	To Select the Scope of Collected Words				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4C				0	uk	Disable the option \<emph\>When closing a document, remove the words collected from it from the list\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B53				0	uk	Now the list is also valid for other documents that you open. When you close the last %PRODUCTNAME document, the word list is deleted.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B56				0	uk	If you enable the checkbox, the list is only valid as long as the current document is open.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2634968				0	uk	If you want the word list to exist longer than the current %PRODUCTNAME session, save it as a document, as described in the following section.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	uk	To Use the Word List for Further Sessions				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B94				0	uk	If the automatic spellcheck option is enabled, only the words that are recognized by the spellcheck are collected.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA1				0	uk	Use the word list to always start with a defined set of technical terms for the word completion feature.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA7				0	uk	Open the text document that contains the terms that you want to use for word completion.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BAB				0	uk	The word completion feature collects the words.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	uk	Select all or some of the words in the list.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	uk	Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy all selected words into the clipboard. Paste the clipboard into a new document and save it to get a reference list of collected words.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BC6				0	uk	Later you can open the reference list and automatically collect the words, so that the word completion feature starts with a defined set of words.				20220827 09:49:47
