helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812	186			0	uk	Відкриває діалог, щоб вставити об'єкт, для якого був встановлений заповнювач.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216	187			0	uk	Вставити посилання				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239	188			0	uk	Переміщає покажчик миші на посилання.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147267	189			0	uk	Виконати макрос				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147290	190			0	uk	Запускає макрос.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145614	191			0	uk	Поле вводу				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637	192			0	uk	Відкриває діалогове вікно для редагування вмісту поля.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3151244	10			0	uk	Placeholder, hidden text, insert reference, variable, database, and user-defined fields display a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field in a document. To enable this feature, ensure that the Extended Tips option (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>What's This?\</item\>) is selected in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Help\</item\> menu.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155937	11			0	uk	Оновлення полів				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155963	12			0	uk	To update all of the fields in a document, press F9, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Select All\</emph\>, and then press F9.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155984	13			0	uk	Щоб відновити поле, вставлене з бази даних, виділіть його, а потім натисніть клавішу F9.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Counting Words				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149686				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>words; counting in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number of words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; number of words/characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; number of words/characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters; counting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number of characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>counting words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word counts\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686	1			0	uk	\<variable id=\"words_count\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/words_count.xhp\" name=\"Counting Words\"\>Counting Words\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D1				0	uk	If you want to count only some text of your document, select the text.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3149821	5			0	uk	Виберіть \<emph\>Сервіс - Підрахувати слова\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	hd_id1116200901133957				0	uk	How does %PRODUCTNAME count words?				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id1116200901133998				0	uk	In general, every string of characters between two spaces is a word. Tabs, line breaks, and paragraph breaks are word limits, too.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id1116200901133985				0	uk	Words with dashes or always visible hyphens, as in plug-in, add-on, user/config, are counted as one word each.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id111620090113399				0	uk	The words can be a mix of letters, numbers, and special characters. So the following text counts as four words: abc123 1.23 "$" http://www.example.com.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E2				0	uk	To get some more statistics about the document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties - Statistics\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3147418	4			0	uk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100400.xhp\" name=\"File - Properties - Statistics\"\>File - Properties - Statistics\</link\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155856				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>table mode selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>proportional distribution of tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative distribution of table cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard;modifying the behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155856	7			0	uk	\<variable id=\"tablemode\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/tablemode.xhp\" name=\"Modifying the Behavior of Rows and Columns for Table\"\>Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149835	12			0	uk	When you insert or delete cells, rows or columns in a table, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Behavior of rows/columns\</item\> options determine how the neighboring elements are affected. For example, you can only insert new rows and columns into a table with fixed row and column dimensions if space permits.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id7344279				0	uk	Note that these properties are valid only for changes to the column width that are made using the keyboard. Using the mouse, you are free to make any column width changes.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3156110	8			0	uk	To set the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Behavior of rows/columns\</item\> options for tables in text documents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</item\>, or use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fixed\</item\>, \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fixed/Proportional\</item\>, and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variable\</item\> icons on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table\</item\> Bar. There are three display modes for tables:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149638	9			0	uk	\<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> - changes only affect the adjacent cell, and not the entire table. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cell becomes narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149613	10			0	uk	\<emph\>Fixed, proportional\</emph\> - changes affect the entire table, and wide cells shrink more than narrow cells. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cells become proportionally narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149864	11			0	uk	\<emph\>Variable\</emph\> - changes affect the table size. For example, when you widen a cell, the width of the table increases.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Вставка графічного об'єкту з галереї шляхом перетягування				20220827 09:49:47
