helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149820	65			0	uk	\<variable id=\"text_emphasize\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_emphasize.xhp\" name=\"Emphasizing Text\"\>Emphasizing Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922	66			0	uk	Here are a few examples of how to emphasize text in a document:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412	67			0	uk	Select the text and apply a different font style or effect, such as \<emph\>bold\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149840	68			0	uk	Right-click in a paragraph, choose \<emph\>Paragraph, \</emph\>set the options that you want, for example, the background color, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	69			0	uk	Select the text, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Frame\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id6924649				0	uk	Use the Text tool on the Drawing toolbar. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E7				0	uk	Use Fontwork. To open the Fontwork window, click the Fontwork Gallery icon on the Drawing bar.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uk	Using Smart Tags				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155622				0	uk	\<bookmark_value\>smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>options;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>disabling;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3563951				0	uk	\<variable id=\"smarttags\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/smarttags.xhp\"\>Using Smart Tags\</link\>\</variable\>				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id368358				0	uk	Smart Tags provide additional information and functionality to specified words in a Writer document. The available features can be different for different Smart Tags extensions.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id9298379				0	uk	Installing Smart Tags				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	uk	Smart Tags can be supplied as \<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>extensions\</link\> to %PRODUCTNAME Writer. 				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id2508621				0	uk	To install a Smart Tag, do one of the following:				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id3856013				0	uk	Save the *.oxt extension file to your harddrive, then double-click the *.oxt file in your file manager. Alternatively, in %PRODUCTNAME choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\> to open the Extension Manager, click Add and browse to the file.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id7814264				0	uk	Click a Smart Tag *.oxt file link on a web page and open the link with the default application. This requires a properly configured Web browser.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id8142338				0	uk	Smart Tags Menu				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1917477				0	uk	Any text in a Writer document can be marked with a Smart Tag, by default a magenta colored underline. You can change the color in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Appearance\</item\>.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id192266				0	uk	When you point to a Smart Tag, a tip help informs you to Ctrl-click to open the Smart Tags menu. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the marked text and open the context menu by Shift+F10.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1998962				0	uk	In the Smart Tags menu you see the available actions that are defined for this Smart Tag. Choose an option from the menu. The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Smart Tags Options\</item\> command opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page of Tools - Autocorrect Options.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id2376476				0	uk	To Enable and Disable Smart Tags				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id349131				0	uk	When you have installed at least one Smart Tags extension, you see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Autocorrect Options\</item\>. Use this dialog to enable or disable Smart Tags and to manage the installed tags.				20220827 09:49:47
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1216467				0	uk	Text that is recognized as a Smart Tag is not checked by the automatic spellcheck.				20220827 09:49:47
